{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting","id":784966,"title":"[2ED] Boston & New England setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-12T13:55:54-08:00","id":784966,"title":"[2ED] Boston & New England setting","content":"So I rather liked Boston as signature setting in the 1ED. I'm very <i>Tim Burton-</i>liking guy and loved the feeling of <i>Sleepy Hallow</i>. Also, I run London game and have soft spot for &quot;old magic&quot;. As such, when thinking about new <b>Mage</b> chronicle to run in our RPG club - &quot;Maybe cool would be to revisit New England and Boston, in 2ED way?&quot; This topic is exactly for this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This game will start in small New England town, &quot;somewhere in woods&quot;. PCs will be first Sleepers and then freshly Awakened that goes after <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/668690-idea-philosopher-s-stone-as-grand-mystery\">Philosopher's Stone Mystery</a>. They will have brush with local Sleepers cult, probably becoming heads of it in few weeks with their new magic. And then Boston Consilium will find them after looking for Magnum Opus, by the rivaling cabals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As I suspect we do not see Boston in 2ED <b>Mage</b>, what I need is this:<br /> <br /> 1. I need cool name for New England small town, one &quot;in the woods&quot;. Something evoking is always nice to see. Town will be far away from Boston so that Consilium will not discover mages - at least untill they will not make a large noise.<br /> <br /> 2. Any &quot;official&quot; changes to Boston setting. I heard that Nemean was exiled being accused of Left-Hand practices in <b>Fallen World Anthology</b> book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T20:08:58-08:00","id":785140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting#post784966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any &quot;official&quot; changes to Boston setting. I heard that Nemean was exiled being accused of Left-Hand practices in <b>Fallen World Anthology</b> book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nemean was imprisoned within his own Oneiros in &quot;The Cage is the Lion's Heart,&quot; the opening fiction for the Silver Ladder book, and at some point between then and &quot;The Unmurdered Man,&quot; became something not entirely like an archmaster, such that he managed to escape but serves as the separating intermediary between our world and the Prince of 100,000 Leaves mentioned in the Secret Concord.<br /> <br /> While all that was happening, he was stripped of his position as Hierarch of Boston in a trial held in Chicago, on testimony from his daimon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T20:46:39-08:00","id":785155,"title":"","content":"If you're dong New England, you owe Livecraft a nod. Arkham and Innsmouth might be a bit too on the nose, but there's always Kingsport...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T23:25:44-08:00","id":785210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=785140#post785140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While all that was happening, he was stripped of his position as Hierarch of Boston in a trial held in Chicago, on testimony from his daimon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone has been chosen to take on Hierarch's place to this day? Books mentioned who it could be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=785155#post785155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're dong New England, you owe Livecraft a nod. Arkham and Innsmouth might be a bit too on the nose, but there's always Kingsport...</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to honor Lovecraft with particular Acamoth that attacked him in game universe in 1920 leading to creation of Cthulhu Mythos. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But as to towns name I do not want to over done this - I thought about using even <b>Secret World</b>'s <i>Kingsmouth</i>, but one player has extensive playthrough with this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now I think maybe better for start will be something like <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipswich,_Massachusetts\" target=\"_blank\">Ipswitch</a></i> - but the real town is to close for Boston to let me run mine first story Arc about lone new Awakened, away from Consilium. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T03:41:07-08:00","id":785294,"title":"","content":"Isn't the Consilium buiseness based in Salem, anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T09:24:49-08:00","id":785434,"title":"","content":"Well, the game I\u00b4m currently directing is based in New England, I love the dark writer tradition of Lovecraft, Frost and King. And also like The Secret World. In my game, the characters are building a Sanctuary in the ruins of Insmouth mannor and exploring Solomon Island in a Sandbox type campaign. Lots of inspiring mysteries there.<br /> <br /> In the politics side, there is a cold war between the Boston mages and New England mages. The first, specially those in the Nemean side see Boston as the capital of New England\u00b4s Council. Non Bostonian mages, see Boston Council as Only Boston Council. Massachussets Council at most. I already make them distrust the Nemean and his warlord attitude and began to forge links with some opposition cabals, like Illuminated Pentacle.<br /> <br /> So, my game is a mix of Sandbox in the local side, and a &quot;normal&quot; game in the political field. But I think my players don\u00b4t want to play politics too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T11:41:44-08:00","id":785493,"title":"","content":"If I get it correctly, Boston ( or rather Salem ) Consilium's Grand Mystery should be Secret Concord and what exactly went in Salem, just before the Witch Trials, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T14:07:31-08:00","id":785558,"title":"","content":"Just for the sake of reference, there was a thread some time ago about the evolving setting of Boston and New England:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it\"> Boston Unveiled: What have you done with it? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hi, everyone! In the spirit of sharing and storytelling, what have you done with the Boston supplement? Myself, I never ran it, since at the time I felt the Salem Consilium was too much like a kindred princedom to my liking. Maybe it was the presentation, I don't know, it just felt that despite the </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T14:18:44-08:00","id":785562,"title":"","content":"For the starting town itself I chosen <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wendell,_Massachusetts\" target=\"_blank\">Wendell</a> - it's small enough and out of the way, I suspect Consilium would not come near to it. Also, it was <i>not</i> mentioned in <b>Boston Unveiled</b> and it's located amidst forests and lake, so good scluded place from all the Awakened society to start mine game.<br /> <br /> <i>I'm still much interested on official and fan interpretations of what is going with Boston and New England at large in <b>Mage</b> games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T14:42:20-08:00","id":785575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=785140#post785140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nemean was imprisoned within his own Oneiros in &quot;The Cage is the Lion's Heart,&quot; the opening fiction for the Silver Ladder book, and at some point between then and &quot;The Unmurdered Man,&quot; became something not entirely like an archmaster, such that he managed to escape but serves as the separating intermediary between our world and the Prince of 100,000 Leaves mentioned in the Secret Concord.<br /> <br /> While all that was happening, he was stripped of his position as Hierarch of Boston in a trial held in Chicago, on testimony from his daimon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the subtext of The Unmurdered Man and The Human Heart was about the Nemean's Seeking, and that he is now an Archmaster proper, and an Aswad at that.<br /> Then again, I always looked upon the Nemean with some kind of horrified fascination and respect. I like the character, I really do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T14:55:41-08:00","id":785580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=785575#post785575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the subtext of The Unmurdered Man and The Human Heart was about the Nemean's Seeking, and that he is now an Archmaster proper, and an Aswad at that.<br /> Then again, I always looked upon the Nemean with some kind of horrified fascination and respect. I like the character, I really do.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>*</b>Sets up a &quot;Fuck the Buddha - The Nemean&quot; T-shirt booth*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T15:37:37-08:00","id":785604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=785580#post785580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>*</b>Sets up a &quot;Fuck the Buddha - The Nemean&quot; T-shirt booth*</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any &quot;Have you ever eaten a human heart&quot;-shirts? Preferably with a picture of a heart held in a slightly clawed hand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T15:42:56-08:00","id":785610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=785604#post785604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have any &quot;Have you ever eaten a human heart&quot;-shirts?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Growth is painful. Don't forget it.&quot;<br /> <br /> He's a quotable bastard, isn't he.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T09:10:51-08:00","id":786016,"title":"","content":"He'd be an Archmaster of Life, right? Not Spirit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T09:57:41-08:00","id":786051,"title":"","content":"Coming away from the subtopic about Nemean, who is Ruling in Heavens ( or Hells )...<br /> <br /> <b>Do official sources points who is new Hierarch?</b> <b>Or does Boston ( and Salem ) is assumed to be Consilium going down without the lead of anyone competent? </b><br /> <br /> Also - <b>Did some of official NPCs in Boston Unveiled died in gameline fictions?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T12:41:46-08:00","id":786141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=786051#post786051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Do official sources points who is new Hierarch?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to have misphrased my summation slightly - the Nemean is still nominally the Hierarch of Boston at the time of &quot;The Cage is the Lion's Heart,&quot; according to his daimon, but the man everyone believes to be the Nemean is indisposed for the foreseeable future. From Khonsu's summary in &quot;The Unmurdered Man,&quot; the Ebon Noose had still been running things for a while when the Censor lost his soul.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why you'd think the Nemean was the only competent member of the administration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:13:57-08:00","id":824009,"title":"","content":"Wondering and reading more, I think that I would made central political event on <b><i>Ebony Noose</i> and <i>White Putnams</i> fight over Consilium, leading slowly to breaking of Secret Concord</b>. After over 2 years, <i>Nemean</i> is declared missing or dead. <i>Ebony Noose</i> grip on Consilium is failing, with <i>White Putnams</i> exploiting the lack of Hierarch. All Consilium knows that sooner or later, someone need to lead Ruling Council. 2016 is election year in Boston. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Other question - <i>Are there some mages interested in Alchemy in <b>Boston Unveiled?</b></i> I do not remember any on my first read few years ago. I need some NPCs interested into it for mine plot on researches for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/668690-mystery-supernal-alchemy-philosopher-s-stone?p=770207#post770207\">Nicholas Flamel and his discovers</a> PCs are entwined in to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T02:11:09-08:00","id":824120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=824009#post824009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Consilium knows that sooner or later, someone need to lead Ruling Council. 2016 is election year in Boston. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not going to be much of a fight. Without the Nemean, the Mysterium is basically uncontestable. The FC and Guardians aren't important enough. The leading arrows are the subordinates of other cabals or really too old and distracted.<br /> <br /> The interesting thing is if you pay particular attention to the Silver Ladder magi's status'. Khumeia is actually the ranking leader. You could infer that the Nemean has basically been holding down all his subordinates. There's no one to challenge him, but if he goes missing there's no one to replace him either.<br /> <br /> An interesting question is how the Noose even stay together without the Nemean? Tiamat might be able to, but she's fairly middle ranking in the consilium, and she's second rank in the Arrow.<br /> <br /> Other question - <i>Are there some mages interested in Alchemy in <b>Boston Unveiled?</b></i> I do not remember any on my first read few years ago. [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Khumeia from the Pentad. I don't think it's explicitly said, but the Company are also kinda alchemically inclined. Tiamat in the Noose is into Alchemy.<br /> If you want to get really interesting, Amanda Kether the head of Psychomimetic Operations is probably your best bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T06:21:28-08:00","id":824245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=824120#post824120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not going to be much of a fight. Without the Nemean, the Mysterium is basically uncontestable. The FC and Guardians aren't important enough. The leading arrows are the subordinates of other cabals or really too old and distracted.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Mysterium has inner fight - good, what 2-3 candidates for Hierarch seat would you propose from it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=824120#post824120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interesting thing is if you pay particular attention to the Silver Ladder magi's status'. Khumeia is actually the ranking leader. You could infer that the Nemean has basically been holding down all his subordinates. There's no one to challenge him, but if he goes missing there's no one to replace him either.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston Unveiled, p. 34</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, Khumeia, of the Illuminated Pentad, freely exploits the gender bias angle (among all of the other angles she can scrounge up) for whatever foothold she can manage to build from it in her quest to become Boston\u2019s fifth Councilor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds to me that Khumeia may try to play on Nemean disapperance to get to Council in few weeks after him. She also could try to run for the Hierarch seat after those two years without proper Hierarch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=824120#post824120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting question is how the Noose even stay together without the Nemean? Tiamat might be able to, but she's fairly middle ranking in the consilium, and she's second rank in the Arrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noose Cabal can survive miss of Nemean, but their political standing would go lower and lower with each week, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=824120#post824120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Khumeia from the Pentad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good, one of candidates for Hierach seat needs something big - like uncovering personal journal-Grimoires from Father of Alchemy... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=824120#post824120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's explicitly said, but the Company are also kinda alchemically inclined. Tiamat in the Noose is into Alchemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good, good - more to the mess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=824120#post824120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to get really interesting, Amanda Kether the head of Psychomimetic Operations is probably your best bet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I was going to ask what Seers could be interested also... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-05-2016, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T02:05:53-08:00","id":824877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=824245#post824245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Mysterium has inner fight - good, what 2-3 candidates for Hierarch seat would you propose from it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Numa and Potestas are the obvious ones. Aurem might see this as a good time to strike out on his own from Potestas.<br /> <br /> Maybe Chain as a wild card. He's not nearly as powerful as them, but... he is the Provost for the Hierarch. If he can get the Noose to continue to act as muscle, he might be able to stand-in for the Nemean for the 2 years that he's missing. That's a long time to be defacto leader of Boston, he could be a pretty plausible candidate by then.<br /> <br /> (I totally forgot about Anacaona, she could plausibly keep the Noose on task)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It sounds to me that Khumeia may try to play on Nemean disapperance to get to Council in few weeks after him. She also could try to run for the Hierarch seat after those two years without proper Hierarch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I would guess so. The various short stories indicate that she got a fair bit of the consilium to agree to her plans, at the very least after the fact. Being the woman who brought down the Nemean is quite an accomplishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T02:27:55-08:00","id":824882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=824877#post824877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being the woman who brought down the Nemean is quite an accomplishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, where is this described?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T02:44:49-08:00","id":824886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=824882#post824882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, where is this described?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the intro to the Silver Ladder book... I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T03:46:25-08:00","id":824892,"title":"","content":"For other looking in this topic, oh great Malcom Sheppard, Creator of <b>Mage: The Awakening</b> himself, has posted this reading order for <i>Nemean</i> official storyline in books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=521804#post521804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The story order should be:</div> </div> </div> </div><i>- Mysterium: <b>&quot;Censorious&quot;</b><br /> - Silver Ladder: <b>&quot;The Cage is the Lion's Heart&quot;</b><br /> - Left-Hand Path: <b>&quot;The Veil, Nothing More&quot;</b><br /> - FWC Anthology: <b>&quot;The Human Heart&quot;</b><br /> - FWC Anthology: <b>&quot;The Unmurdered Man&quot;</b><br /> <br /> With the last two it's possible to read them the other way around. It should be noted, however, that the Nemean isn't really an archmage. He didn't *quite* get there, which is why he can screw around on Earth.</i><br /> <br /> As I read <b>Censorious</b>, it seems is time for <b>Cage is the Lion's Heart</b> and see what exactly <i>Khumeia</i> had done to <i>Nemean</i>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T09:36:53-08:00","id":824964,"title":"","content":"<i>Khumeia</i> made a nice fortel there in <b>Cage is the Lion's Heart</b> - and Convocation punishment of <i>Nemean </i>was great and terrible in the same instance.<br /> <br /> Thinking about long term repercussions - <b>Maybe <i>Khumeia</i> become Magister and new Deacon of Boston by the overseeing the punishment?</b> It was at least 2 years of game time ( when counting the original run of <b>Awakening</b> 1ED corebook - more like 10 years now ) so 1 extra point in Gnosis ( to level of 4 ) and rising to Mind 5 sounds okay to me for her. I also would made her Uncrowned Queen, with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas-and-forum-conventions?p=813606#post813606\">changes to Legacy I propose</a> for 2ED. Then I would give her at least Matter 2, maybe even 3 also.<br /> <br /> One interesting thing I saw in the story - <b>There is mentioning of Chinese cabal <i>Arhats</i> - something more is known about them?</b> Maybe they returned to Boston when <i>Nemean</i> went &quot;missing&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-06-2016, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T03:14:27-08:00","id":825336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=824964#post824964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also would made her Uncrowned Queen, with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas-and-forum-conventions?p=813606#post813606\">changes to Legacy I propose</a> for 2ED. Then I would give her at least Matter 2, maybe even 3 also.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without further changes, Khumeia will be a really terribly Uncrowned King. It's oblations and attainments are based on doing some form of physical labour. She's a manipulative socialite and financier. Mind you, she could have taken up some form of craft. There's the reversed Devil from Supernal Tarot. He'd be a pretty plausible tutor.<br /> <br /> I'd think about making her a Subtle One. I mean, she's attempting to socially engineer the Boston Consilium, it'd go together really easily. She can still be into Alchemy as a different interest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One interesting thing I saw in the story - <b>There is mentioning of Chinese cabal <i>Arhats</i> - something more is known about them?</b> Maybe they returned to Boston when <i>Nemean</i> went &quot;missing&quot;? </div> </div> </div>I've never seen any mention of them elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T05:21:55-08:00","id":825365,"title":"","content":"Wyrd thinks the Uncrowned Kings should also be socialites because he can't separate the idea of alchemy from its nickname of royal arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T05:35:10-08:00","id":825367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=825365#post825365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd thinks the Uncrowned Kings should also be socialites because he can't separate the idea of alchemy from its nickname of royal arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you limit Silver Ladder to &quot;social Order&quot;, even they're Order Mysteries are to uncover Truth of Atlantis...<br /> <br /> I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=814175#post814175\">long post about how Uncrowned Kings should work also as Silver Ladder Legacy</a> - this also works with <i>Khumeia</i> reasoning for taking Legacy for her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-07-2016, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T06:18:45-08:00","id":825378,"title":"","content":"I didn't say she couldn't be an Uncrowned King because she's a socialite and a thearch, I meant that's where her skills are as opposed to in craft or science that are actually relevant to the legacy. You need a craft, and it kinda requires it be a calling. Unless she's gone through a fairly radical reassessment of herself*, I don't really see her being into manual labour.<br /> <br /> *That could still be interesting. A character who was known for being an emaculate socialite, now turns up to Consilium functions with dirt on her face from practicing alchemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T07:28:07-08:00","id":825399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=825367#post825367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you limit Silver Ladder to &quot;social Order&quot;, even they're Order Mysteries are to uncover Truth of Atlantis...<br /> <br /> I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=814175#post814175\">long post about how Uncrowned Kings should work also as Silver Ladder Legacy</a> - this also works with <i>Khumeia</i> reasoning for taking Legacy for her.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually don't, but I do disagree with your reasoning. *Shrugs.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T10:58:31-08:00","id":825474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=825378#post825378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say she couldn't be an Uncrowned King because she's a socialite and a thearch, I meant that's where her skills are as opposed to in craft or science that are actually relevant to the legacy. You need a craft, and it kinda requires it be a calling. Unless she's gone through a fairly radical reassessment of herself*, I don't really see her being into manual labour.<br /> <br /> *That could still be interesting. A character who was known for being an emaculate socialite, now turns up to Consilium functions with dirt on her face from practicing alchemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking over the 1ED Mage corebook write-up I could totally see <i>Khemeia </i>as Uncrowned Queen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1ED Uncrowned Kings</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Suggested Oblations: </b> Engaging inphysical labor; <b>meaningful work (other than the calling he practices for his attainments, described below); leading others in a coordinated teamwork effort;</b> practicing a craft or hobby (again, other than his attainment\u2019s calling)<br /> <b>Concepts: </b>Metallurgists and foundry workers, carpenters, farmers, stonecutters and <b>mason</b>s, scientists (applied) and laboratory technicians</div> </div> </div> </div>Leading a Masonic Lodge is also being a Mason, is it not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:30:08-08:00","id":825597,"title":"","content":"She has literally no dots in Craft. Read the attainments section. She needs some kind of craft or similiar thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=825474#post825474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leading a Masonic Lodge is also being a Mason, is it not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>... No?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T00:09:24-08:00","id":825811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=825597#post825597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She has literally no dots in Craft. Read the attainments section. She needs some kind of craft or similiar thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attainments still will need to be remade as most in 1ED are Mind/Prime, with only first based on Matter - but 2ED rules try to stick to using Optional Arcanum as Orginating Path's Ruling - in <i>Uncrowned Kings</i> example, that would be Matter. So choosing other powers will need new Attainments - and those I think can be made more general in use. But Crafts sure - <i>Khumeia</i> could get dot or two in it, it's nothing dedicated character could get in time of few years between <b>Boston Unveiled</b> and new version of setting. <i>Thanatos</i> is still Pedants main craftsman. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-08-2016, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T02:05:54-08:00","id":825853,"title":"","content":"I actually only just notice Thanatos was an Uncrowned King.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T02:58:44-08:00","id":825872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=825853#post825853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually only just notice Thanatos was an Uncrowned King.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my reasoning also - <i>Illuminated Pentad </i>is shown in <b>Boston Unveiled</b> as Alchemy dedicated cabal and it does have sense that character calling herself <i>Khumeia</i> would want to dwell in to this also, especially as she was described as Alchemy Obsessed character in 1ED book. With new Legacy rules, even when Silver Ladder were not Order for <i>Uncrowned Kings</i>, I think she would want to talk <i>Thanatos</i> in to teaching her, even if she would need Praxis for this. <b>Especially</b> after <i>Nemean</i> thing, when she understands that defense and perfection of ones Mind are so important. Adding Matter to her arsenal is just nice bonus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Notice:</b><span style=\"font-size:11px\"> Yes, I plan to house rule &quot;Double Ruling&quot; thing if </span><b>Dave</b><span style=\"font-size:11px\"> stick to XP discount for Attainment in to making Optional Arcanum the Third Ruling for characters. And those that have both Attainments from Path Ruling Arcanum - just get extra free Reach on Double Ruling. but this will be for other topic material. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-08-2016, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T03:04:22-08:00","id":825877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=825872#post825872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Notice:</b> Yes, I plan to house rule &quot;Double Ruling&quot; thing if <b>Dave</b> stick to XP discount for Attainment in to making Optional Arcanum the Third Ruling for characters. And those that have both Attinements from Path Ruling Arcanum - just get extra free Reach on Double Ruling. but this will be for other topic material. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Free Reach is kind of a big deal, I'd boost their Mage Sight with the arcana instead so that it finds clues and info better, fast, cheaper leading to more Arcane Beats. Which is similar to an XP rebate, but with more impact on the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T03:26:20-08:00","id":825889,"title":"","content":"Thanatos has pretty irrevocably broken with the people who probably initiated him into his legacy. Plus that was in Germany. I don't think anyone is going to care what he does with his legacy.<br /> <br /> Mind you, he'd need to be 2 dots higher in Gnosis to teach. 2e might have changed that, though I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T09:35:19-08:00","id":826036,"title":"","content":"For all it's worth, an Uncrowned King could take up calligraphy or embroidery as their craft. No need to dirty one's hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T09:35:26-08:00","id":826037,"title":"","content":"Can someone tell me - <b>What exactly is happening in </b><i>&quot;The Veil, Nothing More&quot; </i><b>story?</b><br /> <br /> I just read it and completely do not understand - only that there is Scelasti and mentioned Secret Concord...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=825889#post825889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanatos has pretty irrevocably broken with the people who probably initiated him into his legacy. Plus that was in Germany. I don't think anyone is going to care what he does with his legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I just read his full write up it's to me puzzled he is <i>Uncrowned King</i> in the first place - he is so much written as bad Necromancer, not Alchemist. Well, small changes here and there and probably he will work better as Alchemy student. <b>Only what would be creepy Alchemy related Nimbus for him? </b>Dead shades all the times sounds more as Necromancers side of Moros Path. <b>Maybe some gem-like halo, based on <i>Uncrowned Kings</i> takes?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=825889#post825889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, he'd need to be 2 dots higher in Gnosis to teach. 2e might have changed that, though I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>If <i>Thanatos</i> is also Gnosis 4 by now - not very large leap here also, after all those years - he can teach <i>Khumeia</i> (2ed) 1st and 2nd Attainments</b><b> for Gnosis 2.</b> It also would mark whole<i> Illuminated Pentad </i>all more dedicated in getting <i>Uncrowned Kings </i>Daimonomica - books that my story PCs also get from Flamel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And as we talk about whole <i>Illuminated Pentad </i>- <b>To me it's <i>Faustina</i> that should be <i>Subtle One</i>.</b> She is &quot;street level&quot; mage, dedicated on the social cause, not very much in Alchemy angle. Also, she works as architect and it's one of classical <i>Subtle Ones</i> concepts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T09:52:58-08:00","id":826042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=826037#post826037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I just read his full write up it's to me puzzled he is <i>Uncrowned King</i> in the first place - he is so much written as bad Necromancer, not Alchemist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>If <i>Thanatos</i> is also Gnosis 4 by now - not very large leap here also, after all those years - he can teach <i>Khumeia</i> (2ed) 1st and 2nd Attainments</b><b> for Gnosis </b> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it, you really don't need to explain it. Khumeia was initiated as an Uncrowned King by her uncle, that's how she met Thanatos as a fellow legacy member.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>To me it's <i>Faustina</i> that should be <i>Subtle One</i>.</b> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T21:25:54-08:00","id":826541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=825378#post825378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> *That could still be interesting. A character who was known for being an emaculate socialite, now turns up to Consilium functions with dirt on her face from practicing alchemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine the drama now. &quot;I see you've been working.&quot; *Points to face.* &quot;On...alchemy, or something, right? You ARE a necromancer I mean.&quot; *smiles*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:26:22-08:00","id":826589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiwass</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=826541#post826541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can imagine the drama now. &quot;I see you've been working.&quot; *Points to face.* &quot;On...alchemy, or something, right? You ARE a necromancer I mean.&quot; *smiles*</div> </div> </div> </div>What Necromancer? <i>Khumeia</i> is Mastigos. We only pointed that <i>Thanatos</i> was written in <b>Boston Unveiled</b> as Necromancer archetype of Moros Path, not Alchemist.<br /> <br /> I think that I change him that what particula revent was in Germany made him to hate all Necromancers, so he is even more dedicated in to Alchemy studies, more than typical Moros. Think of him as Cobalt of Boston. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T02:22:57-08:00","id":826657,"title":"","content":"I have almost clear view of <i>Illuminated Pentad </i> in 2ED that I can try to write &quot;first draft&quot; version of them before Mage 2ED comes out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I only point that as I like to make <i>Faustina</i> in to <i>Subtle One</i>, I searched <b>Boston Unveiled</b> and it come to me that <i>Simon</i> from <i>White Putams </i> is member of them, also Mastigos of Silver Ladder. It would be interesting to see him as mentor to her, even when their cabals are clealry in antagonistic relations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:01:30-08:00","id":826830,"title":"","content":"I took and wrote down my versions of <i>Illuminated Pentad</i> - nice reading and I look forward to comments. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Illuminated Pentad 2ED (Pre-corebook version)</b></span><br /> <br /> Once new and rising stars of Boston Concilium, two years after <i>Nemean</i> official \u201cdisappearance\u201d, <i>Pentad</i> is clearly showing some cracks. This Silver Ladder cabal has always close to social and political issues in the city. But when <i>Khumeia </i>finally joined Ruling Council after her role in solving Nemean problem, there grew a distance between her and <i>Faustina</i> that is clearly to this day. When her apprentice decided to become <i>Subtle One</i>, under supervise of <i>Simon</i> from <i>White Putnams</i>, new Councilor took it very personally. Still, they remain to be one cabal, even if there are rumors that\u2019s it all only publicity stunt to let <i>Khumeia</i> become Hierarch.<br /> <br /> Even then, <i>Illuminated Pentad</i> is known of his shared Obsessions over Supernal Alchemy. Three members of the group see human minds as \u201cgross matter\u201d of common life that can be perfected into ideal state in that new Hieraconis of Silver Ladders legends will emerge with this transmutations. This theory works in over way also \u2013 minds can shape substance all around them, changing environment around you. In the other words, <i>Illuminated Pentad</i> want to remake Boston\u2019s street and buildings to remodel the people \u2013 and model the people to remake the city. For their Alchemy it\u2019s one and the same. Perfect the \u201csubstance\u201d to perfect the mind. And perfect the mind to perfect the \u201csubstance\u201d.<br /> <br /> With their connections and alchemical lore, <i>Pentad </i>has become one of focal points for the Silver Ladder Cryptopoly in Boston. There always were rumors they \u201cheritage\u201d connections from Guardians of Veil in Order of Golden Dawn era. Cabal do not confirm and do not deny those statements. Truth is they have a large sway over Boston\u2019s mystery cults.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Khumeia (Concilium Councilor)</span></i><br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>We have this city. Now we can make it shine.</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Background:</b> Yvonne Saint-Martin was born into a war. Half of her wealthy, influential Parisian family was a lineage of Proximi, with a handful of mages among them, while the other half constituted the leadership of a Sleeper Exarch cult. Her parents, Proximi both, were killed in a plane crash when she was six months old, leaving the only child an orphan and sole heiress to a vast fortune. Her second cousin <i>Luc</i>, arranged for her to be sent to a branch of the family living north of Boston, far enough away from the conflict that it would not touch her until she was ready to fight back. With only a few vague snippets of prophecy from Luc to go on, the few Saint-Martin Proximi in America did what little they could to try to guide Yvonne toward an Awakening. At the age of 20, to the great relief of her kinsmen, she found her way to the great iron watchtower of Pandemonium. Her great-uncle, a Mastigos of the Silver Ladder, came overseas to teach her what he could before he had to return to the struggle in France. He instructed her in basis of Uncrowned Kings and her first two Attainments.<br /> <br /> By a few years later, Yvonne (now calling herself <i>Khumeia</i>, from the Greek: \u201ccast/pour together, alloy,\u201d a possible origin for the word, \u201calchemy\u201d), had inherited her parents\u2019 wealth and was ready to become part of local Awakened society. She found the politics of the Concilium not much to her liking, however, and quickly resolved to change the situation, opting to fight a different battle than that which occupied the rest of her European family. Her upbringing had stressed subtlety, patience and cunning, and so she set the foundations for a new cabal by purchasing the top two floors of one of the downtown skyscrapers in which she discovered a Hallow. She then sought out prospective allies who shared her vision of freeing Boston and reuniting it under new leadership \u2013 by Legacy Sympathy she uncovered presence of <i>Thanatos</i> in Boston area, other Uncrowned King. And he was more than happy to join her \u201cgreat social experiment\u201d, almost decade ago. Seven years past from now, she rescued young sorceress from her own newly Awakened powers that become <i>Faustina</i>, but their relations are now tense.<br /> <br /> Since that time, she has steadily worked to sever Boston from Salem\u2019s control, though always through open and politically acceptable means. So far, she has made big headway, with helping to move <i>Nemean</i> from power. Rumors said it\u2019s she and <i>Illuminated Pentad </i>that are behind his \u201cdisappearance\u201d and she was granted seat in his place for that. Since it she still need to gather stable connections in community and look over the <i>Ebon Noose</i> and <i>White Putnams</i> rule in the Boston area. She thinks that key to everything is getting Secret Concord and break it, somehow.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Whatever physical imperfections Khumeia might have had before her majority have all been erased by the world\u2019s best plastic surgeons. She is a statuesque, stunningly attractive woman of about 40, with long, black hair, hazel eyes and a flawless alabaster complexion. She favor dark lipstick, but wears little in the way of eye makeup. Her clothing is the best money can buy, consisting mostly of elegant custom-tailored suits. She speaks politely and with great propriety, but makes it quite clear that she knows her opinion to be the correct one, even when she is forced to concede an issue. She is sometimes to be found with dirty hands, oddly contrasting with her otherwise perfect form, from the next avenue she tries to work as Uncrowned Queen.<br /> <br /> Her Nimbus appears as golden halo of light, manifesting from nowhere and spreading across her back of her statue, extending to be nearly twice as long as she is tall.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> <i>Khumeia</i> is interested in the alchemy of the spirit, the process by which the individual transforms and, ultimately, transcends herself, becoming something far greater and more wondrous. She wants to rule a reborn and independent Boston Concilium, but recognizes that such a goal may be decades in coming, should it ever come to pass. She is imperious and self-assured, thinks that her lead of Boston will brought some Golden Age to it, but does her best not to fall to hubris, well aware of the tales of the Exarchs and their legendary arrogance.<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools:</b> Leather handbag<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Yvonne Saint-Martin<br /> <b>Path:</b> Mastigos<br /> <b>Order:</b> Silver Ladder<br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 3, Wits 3 Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes: </b>Presence 5, Manipulation 4, Composure 4<br /> <b>Mental Skills: </b>Academics (Finance) 4, Crafts (Calligraphy) 2, Computer 2, Investigation 2, Occult (Secret Societies) 4, Politics (Awakened) 4, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills: </b>Athletics 3, Brawl 1, Firearms 1, Weaponry (Fencing) 1<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy (Motives) 3, Expression 3, Intimidation (Veiled Threats) 3, Persuasion 4, Socialize (Black Tie Affairs) 4, Subterfuge 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies (International Banking 4, IRS 3), Barfly, Contacts (High Society), Destiny 3 (Bane: \u201cThat which you love shall become venom unto you, and only by embracing that which you despise shall you be saved.\u201d), Enhanced Item 3, Fame 1, Hallow (Shared) 3, High Speech, Language (Ancient Greek, French, Japanese, Latin, Spanish), Library (Shared; Alchemy, Boston Concilium, Sacred Geometry, Secret Societies, Seers of the Throne), Resources 5, Sanctum (Shared) 5, Sleepwalker Retainer 5, Status (Consilium 5, Order 3, Saint-Martin Financial, Inc. 5), Striking Looks 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Wisdom: </b>6<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Dedicated (Fortitude)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Ambitious (Pride)<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Become Hierarch of Boston, Uncover secrets of Uncrowned Kings, \u201cTransmute\u201d society of Boston<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed: </b>10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 4<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Fate 2, Matter 2, Mind 4, Space 3<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> 2nd \u2014???<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><i>Thanatos</i></span><br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>To master matter is to control all life.</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Background: </b>Irwin Paul has put his Sleeping days behind him. He was reborn out of his own death, Awakened and, for the first time, truly alive. He learned his craft from (and choose shadow name to remember) cabal of Necromancers in Germany, where his father was stationed, but was later cast out by them for some crime or has run from them after something they did to him (He has occasionally intimidated that it was those same Necromancers made he despise Death magic and decided to joined the Legacy based on Alchemy.) He returned to Boston, where he had been born and had spent summers with his mother, who had passed away two years before. Well aware of how difficult it was to get by as a solitary mage, he readily accepted <i>Khumeia</i>\u2019s invitation to join the new cabal she was forming.<br /> <br /> Now, he uses Alchemy and experiments on various effects it has on surroundings, trying to shape perfected and independent Boston Consilium. It is slow work, as the mages of behind Secret Concord made this place resistant to changes. Still, he has time; more time, he imagines, than most. Until then, he steadily builds his \u201calchemical empire\u201d, collecting lore and Sleepers supporters, working hard on items and favors for Awakened, waiting for the day that he will be able to use them to topple the <i>Ebon Noose</i> and the <i>White Putnams</i>, when the cabals of Boston will finally band together to drive out the open conspiracy that rules their collective fate. Being best Alchemist in the city and cabalmate to Councilor has its perks \u2013 many people own him the favor. Time of payment is coming.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> <i>Thanatos</i> is a man of slightly taller than average height and slim, with somewhat broad shoulders. His dark brown hair is worn at medium length and never worn in any particular way for too long. His eyes are deep, and his stare is deeply unnerving, like looking over depth of ocean. His garb, always formal, usually seems vaguely antiquated in some way that no one can quite put a finger on. Perhaps it\u2019s simply that even new clothes look somehow old on him. His voice is deep (some say ghoulish), and he speaks slowly, carefully considering each new idea before talking.<br /> His Nimbus manifests as half-seen gaunt, skeletal figures, hovering over him, like spurned lover he chase away.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Perhaps the most important thing to keep in mind about Thanatos is that his creepiness is not an act; he really is that screwed up. The gems and elements are more real to him than the living in many ways. He covets power over the Awakened, but his true hunger is for control over Boston\u2019s \u201ctreasures\u201d \u2013 stashes of alchemical works and lore from Order of Golden Dawn era. Needless to say, this makes him a perfect ally in <i>Khumeia</i>\u2019s book, as she knows that he is not likely to stand in the way of her bid to become the Hierarch of Boston. He has no sense of the impact of his disturbing nature on others; it simply doesn\u2019t occur to him to notice or care.<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tool:</b> Lead forceps<br /> <b>Real Name: </b>Irwin Paul<br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros<br /> <b>Order:</b> Silver Ladder<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Uncrowned King<br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 5<br /> <b>Mental Skills: </b> Academics 3, Crafts (Alloys) 4, Investigation 3, Medicine 2, Occult (Alchemy) 4, Politics 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Larceny 1, Stealth 1, Survival 1, Weaponry (Knives) 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Intimidation (Stare-Downs) 3, Persuasion 2, Socialize 1, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> High Speech, Hallow (Shared) 3, Language (Ancient Greek, French, German, Latin), Library (Shared; Alchemy, Boston Consilium, Sacred Geometry, Secret Societies, Seers of the Throne), Occultation 2, Resources 3, Sanctum (Shared) 5, Status (Consilium 2, Order 1)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 4 (Fixation)<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Patient (Prudence)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Greedy (Greed)<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Uncover secrets of Alchemy, Shape city of Boston, Collect owned Favors<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense: </b>4<br /> <b>Speed: </b>9<br /> <b>Health: </b>7<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 4<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Death 1, Matter 4, Mind 3, Prime 2<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> 3rd \u2014???<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><i>Faustina</i></span><br /> <b>Quote:</b><i> That\u2019s well and good, but what does the current regime actually do for us?</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Background:</b> Brianna Reed was given the name <i>Faustina</i> (after the Roman empress, Faustina the Elder, remembered for her charitable works) when she first met <i>Khumeia</i>, five years her senior. After nearly drowning in a lake, Brianna Awakened, and her experimentation with her newfound abilities brought her to <i>Khumeia</i>\u2019s attention. Brianna enjoyed debates with <i>Khumeia</i> (who inducted her into the Silver Ladder) and agreed to join her new cabal on one condition: that they should establish a system for finding, protecting and instructing the area\u2019s newly Awakened, so that no one should have to stumble through their first weeks, months or even years without proper education.<br /> <br /> Over seven years later, the program still hasn\u2019t really hit its stride, mostly on account of the fact that the <i>Pentad</i> still lacks the clout to make such a far-reaching goal feasible, even with <i>Khumeia </i>as <i>Councilor</i>. <i>Faustina</i>, then, distant herself more and more from her mentor for not fulfilling her promise. She started to take long strides in the city where she met <i>Simon</i> from <i>White Putnams</i> on his \u201cdance\u201d as part of Subtle Ones. Surprisingly, they hit it off and started to meet in secret for few weeks to talk to one another, behind the backs of their antagonistic cabals. Brianna has been inducted by him into Legacy, which quickly came to light. <i>Khumeia</i> was personally affected by her decision, but they still remain cabal mates and Conciliar promise that program <i>will</i> be created.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons Faustina joined <i>Ahl-i-Batin</i> is that she can concentrates on her work as an architect, incorporating the mystic mathematical principles she has learned into her designs, in the hopes of eventually learning some (perhaps lost) trick of willworking that will enable her to exercise her magic effortlessly between any two points in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> <i>Faustina</i> is a good-looking woman, but by no means holds a candle to the resplendent beauty of <i>Khumeia</i>. That suits <i>Faustina</i> just fine, though, as having the spotlight seems to her to be more of a hassle than it could possibly be worth. Her build is a bit taller than average, and slight, and her red-blond hair is worn short. She only rarely uses makeup but dresses well, at <i>Khumeia</i>\u2019s insistence, when meeting with others. However, Faustina prefers her sneakers, sweatpants, jeans and T-shirts when on her own time.<br /> <br /> <i>Faustina</i>\u2019s Nimbus reveals itself as shifting, interlocking geometric patterns that move across her skin like living tattoos.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> <i>Faustina</i> is quite passionate about the causes she supports. Her desire to reign over the Boston Consilium is all but nil, though she recognizes that positive change cannot be made until the Secret Concord is unseated and new leadership steps in. She lacks the discretion and subtlety of <i>Khumeia</i>, so she often holds her tongue, but the occasional thoughtless comment on someone else\u2019s part is known to get her hackles raised. They relations are still strained \u2013 and will be, until <i>Faustina</i> see that <i>Khumeia</i> really is dedicated to the cause.<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools:</b> Iron paperweight with a five-pointed star, sextant (Space magic)<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Brianna Reed<br /> <b>Path: </b>Mastigos<br /> <b>Order:</b> Silver Ladder<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Subtle One<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Architecture) 3, Computer 3, Crafts 3, Occult 2, Politics 2, Science (Structural Engineering) 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 1, Drive 1, Stealth 1<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 2, Expression 1, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 3, Socialize (Bar Hopping) 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Contacts (Construction), Dream 2, High Speech, Language (French, Latin, Spanish), Library (Shared; Alchemy, Boston Consilium, Sacred Geometry, Secret Societies, Seers of the Throne), Resources 2, Sanctum (Shared) 5, Status (Consilium 1, Order 1)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Wisdom: </b>7<br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Caring (Charity)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Demanding (Envy)<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Create system for newly Awakened, Shape society of Boston, ???<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed: </b>9<br /> <b>Health: </b>8<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 3<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Fate 3, Mind 2, Space 3<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> 2rd - ???<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-09-2016, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:15:23-08:00","id":826838,"title":"","content":"Why would Khumeia need plastic surgeons? Get a Thyrsus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:20:32-08:00","id":826839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=826838#post826838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would Khumeia need plastic surgeons? Get a Thyrsus.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from original write-up, on what I base this text. See <b>Boston Unveiled</b> for original versions of characters. But will mark this if on Life magic front if Permanent spells on Living Target will be in 2ED corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:27:13-08:00","id":826841,"title":"","content":"It will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:04:55-08:00","id":827016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting#post784966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I rather liked Boston as signature setting in the 1ED. I'm very <i>Tim Burton-</i>liking guy and loved the feeling of <i>Sleepy Hallow</i>. Also, I run London game and have soft spot for &quot;old magic&quot;. As such, when thinking about new <b>Mage</b> chronicle to run in our RPG club - &quot;Maybe cool would be to revisit New England and Boston, in 2ED way?&quot; This topic is exactly for this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This game will start in small New England town, &quot;somewhere in woods&quot;. PCs will be first Sleepers and then freshly Awakened that goes after <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/668690-idea-philosopher-s-stone-as-grand-mystery\">Philosopher's Stone Mystery</a>. They will have brush with local Sleepers cult, probably becoming heads of it in few weeks with their new magic. And then Boston Consilium will find them after looking for Magnum Opus, by the rivaling cabals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As I suspect we do not see Boston in 2ED <b>Mage</b>, what I need is this:<br /> <br /> 1. I need cool name for New England small town, one &quot;in the woods&quot;. Something evoking is always nice to see. Town will be far away from Boston so that Consilium will not discover mages - at least untill they will not make a large noise.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.shutesbury.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Shutesbury</a>, Massachusetts<br /> The smallest town and most isolated town which still had enough infrastructure to have a library, city clerk, town hall and bit of <a href=\"http://www.shutesbury.org/history\" target=\"_blank\">history</a> to <a href=\"http://www.bostonmagazine.com/2006/05/the-master-race/\" target=\"_blank\">pin</a> <a href=\"http://www.hauntedplaces.org/shutesbury-ma/\" target=\"_blank\">some</a> <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=Tm7lzXmFZmoC&amp;pg=PA141&amp;lpg=PA141&amp;dq=Shutesbury+tragedy&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=R8cRogKnA2&amp;sig=UsfPgsd0pyWSrPbhTm3-t1xR4Jg&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwjHne3QwOvKAhUD7WMKHSRcCSk4ChDoAQgpMAI#v=onepage&amp;q=Shutesbury%20tragedy&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">interesting</a> <a href=\"http://www.suicidecleanup.org/massachusetts/shutesbury.html\" target=\"_blank\">stories</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shutesbury,_Massachusetts\" target=\"_blank\">on</a>. Just because some details are research-able in the real world doesn't mean there isn't plenty of <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=ejLkBQAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PA187&amp;lpg=PA187&amp;dq=shutesbury+historic+horror&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=Hx-8MjBsRB&amp;sig=2K4sD3-sOjoojUu7PuNH-808K60&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiG8o6kyuvKAhVWwWMKHQNCCKEQ6AEIUDAG#v=onepage&amp;q=shutesbury%20historic%20horror&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">wiggle room</a> for a storyteller to back-fill dire supernatural conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Coordinates: 42.452159, -72.410076<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting#post784966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Any &quot;official&quot; changes to Boston setting. I heard that Nemean was exiled being accused of Left-Hand practices in <b>Fallen World Anthology</b> book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry no help there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:46:39-08:00","id":827061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=827016#post827016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.shutesbury.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Shutesbury</a>, Massachusetts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Went with Wendell in the end, but will look on Shuresbury maybe as some side story later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I will gladly listen to what you think about my take on <i>Illuminated Pentad</i> cabal from Boston, as 2ED rewrite of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=826830#post826830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Illuminated Pentad 2ED (Pre-corebook version)</b></span><br /> <br /> Once new and rising stars of Boston Concilium, two years after <i>Nemean</i> official \u201cdisappearance\u201d, <i>Pentad</i> is clearly showing some cracks. This Silver Ladder cabal has always close to social and political issues in the city. But when <i>Khumeia </i>finally joined Ruling Council after her role in solving Nemean problem, there grew a distance between her and <i>Faustina</i> that is clearly to this day. When her apprentice decided to become <i>Subtle One</i>, under supervise of <i>Simon</i> from <i>White Putnams</i>, new Councilor took it very personally. Still, they remain to be one cabal, even if there are rumors that\u2019s it all only publicity stunt to let <i>Khumeia</i> become Hierarch.<br /> <br /> Even then, <i>Illuminated Pentad</i> is known of his shared Obsessions over Supernal Alchemy. Three members of the group see human minds as \u201cgross matter\u201d of common life that can be perfected into ideal state in that new Hieraconis of Silver Ladders legends will emerge with this transmutations. This theory works in over way also \u2013 minds can shape substance all around them, changing environment around you. In the other words, <i>Illuminated Pentad</i> want to remake Boston\u2019s street and buildings to remodel the people \u2013 and model the people to remake the city. For their Alchemy it\u2019s one and the same. Perfect the \u201csubstance\u201d to perfect the mind. And perfect the mind to perfect the \u201csubstance\u201d.<br /> <br /> With their connections and alchemical lore, <i>Pentad </i>has become one of focal points for the Silver Ladder Cryptopoly in Boston. There always were rumors they \u201cheritage\u201d connections from Guardians of Veil in Order of Golden Dawn era. Cabal do not confirm and do not deny those statements. Truth is they have a large sway over Boston\u2019s mystery cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>More to be read in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-new-england-setting?p=826830#post826830\">original post here</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T15:53:36-08:00","id":827141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I will gladly listen to what you think about my take on Illuminated Pentad cabal from Boston, as 2ED rewrite of them.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the overview, and having checked out the characters it is linked to, I like them as well.<br /> <br /> What level of detail are you going into for your Chronicle? Are you mapping out the supernatural ecology and economies, with respect to the various supernatural equivalents of watering holes, feeding grounds, and otherworldly thoroughfares? Are you generating <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/118740-supernatural-populations\">demographics</a>, outlining areas/spheres of influence which are stewarded and preyed upon by overlapping supernatural and supernaturally-aware populations? Do you apply the principles of essence flows, ley lines, and loci to chart where the distribution of supernatural sites should be? (I like using rivers, roads, ridge-lines, and rail tracks because they they represent actual flows which lends symbolic weight to hypothetical metaphysical flows) How much are you creating whole-cloth and how much is research reality with fictionalized supernatural backstory?<br /> <br /> I am gearing up for a 2 Edition of Portland Oregon game which I plan to use as a backdrop for a few chronicles. I live here so the research is easier. Thank you for sharing your material with me.<br /> <br /> About the philosopher stone mystery, even at max gnosis isn't it only possible to be two two arcanum dots shy of mastery of all arcanum? (which leads to the question of how well known that fact is, and how insanely frustrating it would be for those seeking this stone)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T19:10:29-08:00","id":827265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=827141#post827141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the overview, and having checked out the characters it is linked to, I like them as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=827141#post827141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What level of detail are you going into for your Chronicle? Are you mapping out the supernatural ecology and economies, with respect to the various supernatural equivalents of watering holes, feeding grounds, and otherworldly thoroughfares? Are you generating <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/118740-supernatural-populations\">demographics</a>, outlining areas/spheres of influence which are stewarded and preyed upon by overlapping supernatural and supernaturally-aware populations? Do you apply the principles of essence flows, ley lines, and loci to chart where the distribution of supernatural sites should be? (I like using rivers, roads, ridge-lines, and rail tracks because they they represent actual flows which lends symbolic weight to hypothetical metaphysical flows) How much are you creating whole-cloth and how much is research reality with fictionalized supernatural backstory?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I run based on <b>Boston Unveiled</b>, I stick to it's level of detail. Also, I do not see any of my players to be big in to Prime or Spirit to make details on the essence, Shadow or Ley Lines all that need for the play. Maybe I will think about when the setting will be in play or majority made.<br /> <br /> I use <b>Boston Unveiled </b>as entry point and try to move setting few years in to future - with small fixes here and there, based on <b>Mage</b> gameline run and to show more internal setting logic. I very like Salem Witch trials backdrop and Order of Golden Dawn as Nameless War echo from London. Need to explore more Secret Concord as Boston Major Mystery more - probably will come with some Abyssal power ( Acamoth maybe? ) that is tempting sorcerers from every time they first got to the Massachusetts. Just like in the <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt4263482/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Witch</b> 2015 movie</a>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gud8viI-P7Q\" data-code=\"gud8viI-P7Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gud8viI-P7Q/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> ( I really need to see this movie! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=827141#post827141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the philosopher stone mystery, even at max gnosis isn't it only possible to be two two arcanum dots shy of mastery of all arcanum? (which leads to the question of how well known that fact is, and how insanely frustrating it would be for those seeking this stone)</div> </div> </div> </div>I will answer it in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/668690-mystery-supernal-alchemy-philosopher-s-stone\">Alchemy and Philosopher's Stone</a> topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-09-2016, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T01:13:01-08:00","id":827351,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Great Mystery of New England \u2013 Spirit of Land</b></span><br /> There are forces in New England lands. Secret whispers between the sights of wind. The sounds of running river are the same as rhythms of Supernal incantations. Lines of power are crossing land, pointing to forgotten symbols. Immaterial beings are hunting those places for centuries \u2013 and yet they work in to something greater, like common mind. Natives American say this land has its own <i>soul</i>. They may not be wrong\u2026<br /> <br /> From the time first European witches and sorcerers come to the New World, they tried to communicate with this intelligence. It is commonly called \u201eSpirit of Land\u201d \u2013 but Awakened are not sure is it spirit, goetia, powerful ghosts \u2013 or even just some presence they feel when they are alone in the woods. All they want to be study it. And to get the power from it.<br /> <br /> Many attempts on this gone badly \u2013 Spirit, if it\u2019s even exists, is fighting with mages to not get locked up by them. Salem Witch trials are said to be result of first famous attempt. Hubristic Awakened tried to play with forces they could not understood \u2013 and innocent people paid the price. Or at least it\u2019s what Guardians of Veil from New England say.<br /> <br /> Secret Concord from Boston is to be the latest successive attempt on that. Whoever \u2013 no, <i>what</i>ever - is third signer of the document is probably the \u201eThe Spirit of Land\u201d. This is why Ebon Noose and White Putnams so much fortune favors them - the land itself helps them to maintain power. Or so rumors in Awakened circles say.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Possible solutions to Mystery:</b></span><ul><li><b><i>Spirit of the Land</i></b> \u2013 Mysterious being most Awakened sought to know in New England <i>is</i> a powerful Shadows spirit of this Lands. It\u2019s Rank 7 being, on par of Wolf gods the werewolf worship or just a bit below ephemeral beings like Sun or Moon. Many wonder how spirit of surrounding can be this powerful and wonder if Atlantean civilizations that left ruins in New England woods have something to do with it. ( See <b>Boston Unveiled</b>, Chapter Four \u201eOff the Map\u201d )</li> </ul><ul><li><b><i>Bound</i></b> <b><i>unbound </i></b>\u2013 Other theory states that this being is Supernal god, thrown into our world when Exarchs took their Thrones. Instead of being bound in some ancient prison, this being freed itself and roam freely the land. It would explained local Seers interest in to phenomena, as one of their most important dogmas it to lock and sentry this kind of beings. It would also clear why some Awakened disappear in the middle of the night when left alone in the woods \u2013 Bound are always hungry for Mana, pouncing on anything that has a greater amount of it in his Pattern. Awakened are then ideal meal.</li> </ul><ul><li><b><i>Prisoner from Abyss </i></b>\u2013 Most disturbing theory is that \u201eSpirit\u201d is powerful Acamoth, abyssal being living in Astral Space. Most seek mages to use their Astral link with Abyss to go over their home they were separated eons ago. But the New England being had somehow evolved and can travel between strata of Astral on its own \u2013 it lies in Anima Mundi most often, leaving imprint on the land and beings in region. Still, it likes to play with Awakened, offering lore and power. For the price.</li> </ul>And what do you think about idea on Great Mystery of Boston and New England? Liked my write-up? Myself, I plan to go with the third variant in my game\u2026 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T21:38:39-08:00","id":827987,"title":"","content":"Slight addendum to Khumeia<i>'s write-up</i> and possible story hook for PCs.<i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Provost</span></b><br /> In normal circumstances her Provost would be <i>Faustina</i> \u2013 but the strained relation between two lead <i>Khumeia</i> to forsake this choice, for the time being. As new Councilor and from needs of conditions, she takes official matters on herself. Consilium of Boston was always \u201cold boys club\u201d, she is often not taken seriously and her duties are diminished. Still, if she finds new and dedicated mage that wants to help her shape a better Consilium \u2013 preferably from Silver Ladder - she gladly will agree and favor new Provost as putting \u201cfresh blood\u201d into Council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-11-2016, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T03:59:48-08:00","id":828714,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Orders of New England 2ED</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Caucuses</b></span><br /> Pentacle Order in New England are very loose associations of mages spread around terrain of whole Massachusetts State and some borders counties to it. Proper power of Boston is not very much centralized as inner wars of Bostonian Awakened in XX century and waves of scattered emigrants lead too many willworkers being left alone to their own devises in small towns and settlements of the region. Nominally, Orders local societies are full of various ranks many members across New England take on themselves. Realistically, Boston\u2019s day to day mage community is understaffed and many times isolationists with not enough mages to run smoothly tasks of Orders in the city, because members are scattered on the map of the state.<br /> <br /> This situation changes when Caucuses are called in. Representatives of whole Order come once a month or bi-monthly meetings, exchange knowledge and power in their secret halls. Then mages of New England looks as proper community and force to be reckoned with. And Favors or knowledge exchanged there make lasting relations with all participants. Even if most mages in New England are only nominally subordinate to the Boston\u2019s Consilium, however, they respond to call of colleagues and friends from the Order of the city itself. Counting on their return of Favor if necessary.<br /> <br /> <b>Adamantine Arrow: Windham Manor \u2013 Holy Ground</b><br /> <br /> On a sea cliff in Gloucester perched Windham Manor. A network of caves extends beneath the house, carved into the rock by millions of years of tides. A sprawling graveyard is located at the back of the property, overlooking the water, but it is almost completely overgrown. It\u2019s here where New England\u2019s Arrows meet bimonthly (usually sometime during the third week of the month) on request of <i>Ferrum </i>\u2013 Adamant Sage. This place is chosen on the tradition for family ground of <i>Hydra</i> - Sage Emeritus \u2013 that\u2019s family and cabal <i>Gravediggers </i>have protected Boston and region for centuries. At least once a year, Ferrum likes to put on an exhibition of the Duel Arcane, inviting any and all mages of the Arrow to observe or, even better, participate.<br /> <br /> <i>Apollonia</i> from <i>The Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth</i> is Vidantus \u2013 working mostly as teacher of new Arrows, trying to not go for more bloodshed in her life, understanding it\u2019s her time after being defeated by <i>Ferrum </i>and the death of <i>Ares</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Free Council: <i>Emerald Scroll</i> Bar \u2013 Assembly and Lore House</b><br /> Located at Roxbury neighborhood waterfront, this Tarot\u2019s Major Arcana styled place is open Lore House to any mage that will enter. Leaded by Davy Jones column of <i>Dead Wrens</i> can sell you anything they can get hands on. And make great parties. They even sell alchemical potions as drinks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>Emerald Scroll</i> is also Assembly meeting place \u2013 treated mostly as Free Council Caucus once a month, in weekend long \u2018members only\u2019 event \u2013 it\u2019s open on day-to-day basis to any mage that want to trade Mysteries or sell magic for quick cash. \u201cLocal\u201d Assembly can be called almost every day, but it\u2019s rulings are taken only to represent Boston mages only interests \u2013 <i>Dead Wrens</i> understand that beside them, every few days visits of <i>SMG</i> and city passing Libertine or two \u2013 day-to-day rulings of Assembly do not really reflect New England community at large.<br /> <br /> <b>Note: </b><i>I want to remake Dead Wrens as Libertines only column \u2013 they mix of Orders in 1ED looks as dictated only old stereotype of \u201cArrow=warriors\u201d or \u201cMysterium=explorers\u201d. Also, they are pirates and thieves, god damit, how much Nameless can one be more!</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mysterium: Academy of the <i>Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth</i> - Athenaeum</b><br /> <br /> Academy apartment building in the Beacon Hill area, with north wing working as sanctum for fellow Arrows from <i>Exalted Knights of the Gryphon</i> to defend the Supernal Mysteries stronghold. As name suggest, this particular Athenaeum works mostly in Academy model (see <b>Mysterium</b> book), teaching newly Awakened under guise of school for \u201cexceptional students\u201d. Of course there is Scriptorium part of complex and giant libraries Athenea are known of. Interesting, there is not pointed obvious Censorium in place \u2013 maybe Boston\u2019s Guardians to the Veil are having something to it. As institution, Athenaeum is run by <i>Aurem</i>, one of most dedicated and oldest Mystygoges of Caucus.<br /> Mysterium caucuses are convened at 8 P.M. on the 15th of every month (barring emergency), are rigidly ordered affairs. They are run by <i>Potestas </i>\u2013 eldest (literally) mage of Mysterium and Hierophant of Order.<br /> <br /> <b>Guardians of Veil: Order of the Golden Dawn, <i>true</i> Emerald Scroll and Oubliette \u2013 Labyrinth</b><br /> <br /> Once, Guardians Labyrinth was glorious in Boston \u2013 on wave of occult interest in first decades of XX century, it grew and grew, spanning from one secret society to the next. Order of the Golden Dawn split itself in to a lot of cults and sects, each with it slightly different dogma. But each answering to secrets signs of <i>Emerald Scroll</i> \u2013 code name for group of Cultors from the Order. Sadly, it\u2019s now only glorious past.<br /> <br /> Today, Guardians still control many of connections between cults, but after Free Council revolt \u2013 and even Libertines claiming the name for secret cabal as bar slogan! \u2013 It\u2019s much, much weakened. Restoring Labyrinth to its former splendor is one of priorities for <i>Shadow Chorus</i> and its leader <i>Culsu</i> \u2013 Epopt of the Guardians. Overwatching Boston Consilium after \u201edisappearance\u201d of <i>Nemean</i> is second. Both they oversee from their secret sanctum called <i>Oubliette</i>, door\u2019s to one can open anywhere in the New England. Once a month, in the settlement of whole Massachusetts, portals to it are open and Guardians come to plan their next moves in reclaiming the region and safe keeping the magic. <i>Februs</i>, <i>Culsu</i>\u2019s cabal mate, is appointed Interfector of the Caucus.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Ladder: Cryptopoly</b><br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> <i>I was thinking about making Deacon someone other than Khumeia, but as I see in <b>Boston Unveiled</b>, there are not any other Silver Ladder candidates for this. </i><i><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />Even Khumeia cannot be Deacon because she would need to be Magister first, by <b>Silver Ladder</b> book\u2019s standards. Without this, Silver Ladder sounds more as collection of individuals than proper Order.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T07:31:33-08:00","id":828777,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Consilium of Boston 2ED</b></span><br /> Boston\u2019s Ruling Council is in flux. Two years after sudden \u201cdisappearance\u201d of previous Hierarch \u2013 infamous <i>Nemean</i> \u2013 there is slow power shift and still real change cannot be made in Consilium. Mysterious event is less than a puzzle for most of Awakened citizens of Boston, as there were several tries to overthrow a tyrant \u2013 so almost everyone assume he get what he deserved. Rumors says that Silver Ladder Convocation has done something to him, but on day to day life in Boston, most do not care about it. Pentacle mages are just happy that monster stepped down from the throne. Councilors are in fighting against one another on words, looking for weakness to exploit in the race to the now vacant seat of Hierarch.<br /> <br /> It all comes from the simple fact that previous leader of Council run it with iron grip where he found it fit. <i>Nemean</i> maintained his power largely through a combination of scare tactics and a hands-off philosophy of rule. He normally roused to act only by immediate and forceful threats to his authority. When such a threat emerges, however, he used the massive power bloc encompassed by the Secret Concord (about a third of then Boston\u2019s Consilium willworkers) to leverage such action as he desires, usually action of a harshly punitive variety.<br /> <br /> Now, system is slowly degenerating. Or remaking, as others would say. With rumors of her participation in getting rid of<i> Nemean</i>, the ambitious <i>Khumeia</i> assumed the position of Councilor in few months after. <i>Chain Parris</i> also rose on absence of former Hierarch, going from his Provost to proper Council member. This shacked decade\u2019s long status quo, were two new Councilor hailing from the Boston proper area and no one from Salem. Cormant House hadn\u2019t been used for Ruling Council meetings and more and more <i>Ebon Noose</i> is worrying if <i>White Putams</i> are not preparing to change conditions of Secret Concord. With each passing week details of the Concord and the identity of mysterious third signer of it are more and more hot topic in backstage of Pentacle meetings. It looks that <i>Ebon Noose</i> was not thrown out of Consilium only because it has so many combat skilled mages under lead of<i> Anacaona de Xaragua</i>. But the upcoming elections for Hierarch seat in the Council can change everything...<br /> <br /> (<b>Note:</b> <i>I need to think about new cool place for the Ruling Council to meet in Boston \u2013 Maybe you have some ideas?</i>)<br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Council of Boston</b><ul><li><i>Chain Parris</i> of the <i>White Putams</i> \u2013 Provost: ??? (Have idea who could be good candidate for his?)</li> <li><i>Hydra</i> of the <i>Gravediggers</i> \u2013 Provost: <i>Reinga</i></li> <li><i>Khumeia</i> of the <i>Illuminated Pentad</i> - Provost: None</li> <li><i>Numa</i> of the <i>Sanguine Laurel</i> \u2013 Provost: <i>Ranae</i></li> <li><i>Potestas</i> of the <i>Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth</i> \u2013 Provost: <i>Aurem</i></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T02:42:24-08:00","id":829632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=828777#post828777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<i>Chain Parris</i> of the <i>White Putams</i> \u2013 Provost: ??? (Have idea who could be good candidate for his?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with Anacaona. As provost to the acting hierarch, she'd have the increased authority to act as head of the sentinels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]<i>Hydra</i> of the <i>Gravediggers</i> \u2013 Provost: <i>Reinga</i> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't overlook the fact that Hydra was already very old in the book. I'm not sure she'd make it to the present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T02:09:00-08:00","id":845998,"title":"","content":"After J.K. Rowling showing her and Potterverse history of magic in Americas, <b>I think maybe adding rumors of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/844642-scourers\">Scourers</a> mixed in to Salem Witch Trials would be good idea?</b> In nutshell, that some quasi-organized Banishers were in the jury of Trials. it does has sense, if you look over Puritans ideas on magic...<br /> <br /> Also, one of my preAwakening players characters have strong tendency to Guardians of Veil and their Modus Operandi - <b>Does <i>Khumeia</i> have good relation with any Guardian in Boston to present probable apprentice?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T04:00:28-08:00","id":846020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=845998#post845998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In nutshell, that some quasi-organized Banishers were in the jury of Trials. it does has sense, if you look over Puritans ideas on magic...[/B]</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is who were they going after? It seems kinda unlikely that a village would have a large number of Awakened just hanging out and not doing anything. I mean, it could work as a bit of fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T04:09:52-08:00","id":846021,"title":"","content":"Banishers who wait for a trial process to condemn a Mage to burning at the stake or whatever are behaving in a very overconfident fashion. There'd be way too many chances for a Mage to escape or fight back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T05:39:20-08:00","id":846036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=846020#post846020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is who were they going after? It seems kinda unlikely that a village would have a large number of Awakened just hanging out and not doing anything. I mean, it could work as a bit of fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's high of Witch Paranoia in America - almost everyone was <i>suspected</i> to be a Witch. And you need only one active Apostate and magic to working for accusation starting to fly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-12-2016, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T08:32:40-08:00","id":846080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=846036#post846036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's high of Witch Paranoia in America - almost everyone was <i>suspected</i> to be a Witch. And you need only one active Apostate and magic to working for accusation starting to fly...</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the accused were actually the wealthy, the witch trials were mixture of religious and class conflict.<br /> <br /> Sleepers wouldn't remember any actual acts of magic that they witnessed though, so Mages although perhaps easily found among the wealthy elite would be unlikely to be accused of witchcraft (Especially because they have real magic to use to throw off Sleeper investigations).<br /> <br /> Assuming a Mage actually came up on trial? He could use magic to escape, or prove his innocence or whatever he likes. It's highly unlikely they would actually get killed off by Sleepers given any time in a cell to contemplate their situation and solutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-12-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T14:42:43-08:00","id":846282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=846036#post846036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's high of Witch Paranoia in America</div> </div> </div> </div>No it's not. The reason Salem is famous is that it's one of the last (in America at least). I mean, a lot of the people involved in the prosecution later apologised for their role.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> almost everyone was <i>suspected</i> to be a Witch. </div> </div> </div>Again, not really. Gentry don't get accused of witchcraft. Remember the Stone Assembly from Boston.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T16:58:35-08:00","id":846336,"title":"","content":"Well, they do sometimes, which is a part of why the Salem trials ended up getting dissolved. The wife of the governor was among the accused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T02:50:03-07:00","id":865383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=828714#post828714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Silver Ladder: Cryptopoly</b><br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> <i>I was thinking about making Deacon someone other than Khumeia, but as I see in <b>Boston Unveiled</b>, there are not any other Silver Ladder candidates for this. </i><i><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />Even Khumeia cannot be Deacon because she would need to be Magister first, by <b>Silver Ladder</b> book\u2019s standards. Without this, Silver Ladder sounds more as collection of individuals than proper Order.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Got any ideas on solving this? Maybe someone can point us how to make proper Cryptopoly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T03:05:15-07:00","id":865386,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind, the Nemean shouldn't be Deacon either, he has 3 SL status dots. You don't need to be a magister to hold the position, the dots mean whether people will actually respect you as such.<br /> <br /> More generally, Boston was written before the setting had been really stabilised. I've been pondering how to run the setting myself, and really, I think I'd use the Orders as something closer to agendas or Darshana from Demon and TTS, free floating ideologies rather than coherent organisations. The setting just don't really work with the Orders as they were later written up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T07:00:38-07:00","id":865482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=846282#post846282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, not really. Gentry don't get accused of witchcraft. Remember the Stone Assembly from Boston.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I'm sorry, but this triggered the Changeling fan in me and the first thing I imagined was someone being accused of witchcraft, only for the accused to look offended before suddenly dragging everyone in the room through the Hedge:<br /> <br /> &quot;Excuse me, but I'm a fuckmothering faerie..!&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Again, I apologize for the tangent. Back to the topic!<br /> <br /> It was mentioned waaaaaaaay earlier in the thread, but Boston is not a &quot;normal&quot; Consilium. It was designed as a set-up for the players in the setting to remove the Nemean from power; literally, as the Silver Ladder book explained this is a tactic sometimes used by the SL to stir mages out of complacency by presenting a pretend tyrant who creates an environment that will hopefully lead to others toppling them and taking the reins. Unfortunately, as also explained in the SL book, the Nemean did his job a little too well. He was too efficient in sniffing out threats to his power, as well as positioning himself and others so that there really isn't anyone else from his own Order in the Boston area who could reasonably replace him once removed. (Part of his reasoning for this may have something to do with the conditions of the Secret Concord and/or his connection to the Aswadim as an Archmaster...shhh!) But my point is, that would explain the odd imbalance of power within the Orders in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T14:58:44-07:00","id":865712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865383#post865383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got any ideas on solving this? Maybe someone can point us how to make proper Cryptopoly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Another idea I've been thinking about is making the Silver Ladder Caucus much bigger. We've been told that in 2e a caucus is a mystery cult covering a fairly big area including multiple consilia. The issue with that is... where do you draw the boundary? I wondered about maybe a Caucus of New England? But that seems kinda weak. I dunno, maybe the SL did a similiar thing to the Boston Mysterium and were founded as the colonial branch of a Caucus in England.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T21:31:20-07:00","id":865800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865712#post865712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea I've been thinking about is making the Silver Ladder Caucus much bigger. We've been told that in 2e a caucus is a mystery cult covering a fairly big area including multiple consilia. The issue with that is... where do you draw the boundary? I wondered about maybe a Caucus of New England? But that seems kinda weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm <i>doing it</i> right now with other Orders. Boston NPCs seems to be not enough to put one Consilium in working, and what about 5 Caucuses. I assumed NPCs in Boston itself are only leaders and proper Caucuses are stretched in to deep woods of New England. Silver Ladder can be easily much bigger this way. But I have other idea...<br /> <br /> What if Silver Ladder is still in &quot;colonial&quot; structure? Where other Orders finally reforged themselves in New World, Silver Ladder was always understaffed and adapted? That in New England - or even whole West Coast - Ladder cults are known for granting ill adequate titles to positions and many times their Magisters are Adepts or even Disciples in reality! Other Ladder Caucuses are a bit laughing on this power vacuum, but East Coast Tearchs are answering that they give promotion possibilities other groups do not. New England is seen as &quot;wild front to be tamed&quot; by Ladder - who will take it and remake it in to glorious Hieraconis?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-26-2016, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T02:29:46-07:00","id":865854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865800#post865800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm <i>doing it</i> right now with other Orders. Boston NPCs seems to be not enough to put one Consilium in working, and what about 5 Caucuses. I assumed NPCs in Boston itself are only leaders and proper Caucuses are stretched in to deep woods of New England. Silver Ladder can be easily much bigger this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, I'm not suggesting they be the leadership. There could be other consilia with their own leadership. Hell, if you want to fudge some of the stuff in SL slightly, maybe the Nemean is merely Deacon for Boston within a large college of Deacons. He mentions there being other deacons who are out to get him and there are mentions of the Nemean being repremanded by his caucus for his actions (even before the whole psychic imprisonment thing).<br /> <br /> Also, he's tried at the convocation in Chicago. That could suggest the Caucus covers a massive area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if Silver Ladder is still in &quot;colonial&quot; structure? Where other Orders finally reforged themselves in New World, Silver Ladder was always understaffed and adapted? That in New England - or even whole West Coast - Ladder cults are known for granting ill adequate titles to positions and many times their Magisters are Adepts or even Disciples in reality! Other Ladder Caucuses are a bit laughing on this power vacuum, but West Coast Tearchs are answering that they give promotion possibilities other groups do not. New England is seen as &quot;wild front to be tamed&quot; by Ladder - who will take it and remake it in to glorious Hieraconis?! </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really fit with New England terribly well in my mind. Plus, you kinda need a good reason why.<br /> <br /> Though I guess it could be an interesting invertion, that an area among the oldest most settled parts of America is for magi an untamed frontier... I actually really like that idea.<br /> <br /> Also, it's the other West Coast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T06:16:55-07:00","id":865909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865854#post865854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing, I'm not suggesting they be the leadership. There could be other consilia with their own leadership. Hell, if you want to fudge some of the stuff in SL slightly, maybe the Nemean is merely Deacon for Boston within a large college of Deacons. He mentions there being other deacons who are out to get him and there are mentions of the Nemean being repremanded by his caucus for his actions (even before the whole psychic imprisonment thing).<br /> <br /> Also, he's tried at the convocation in Chicago. That could suggest the Caucus covers a massive area.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you say there is only one, massive New England SL Caucus, that each town is is only headed by it's Deacon? So whole Caucus is streching from Augusta in Maine, Concord in New Hampshire, Mont Perlier in Vermont, Boston in Massachusetts, Providance in Rhode Island and Hartfordd in Connecticut? Each have one local Deacon and they rule, instead of proper Magisterium in Ladder?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865854#post865854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I guess it could be an interesting invertion, that an area among the oldest most settled parts of America is for magi an untamed frontier... I actually really like that idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Witch Trials are reason? When rest of States were having more or less steady colonization, New England had Banishers, trials, Inquistion and other problems. I can easily see how this leads to understaffed Silver Ladder and often titels rotation in Order - so New Englands Tearchs adapt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865854#post865854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's the other West Coast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, East Coast, of course - early morning writting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T06:43:44-07:00","id":865922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you say there is only one, massive New England SL Caucus, that each town is is only headed by it's Deacon? So whole Caucus is streching from Augusta in Maine, Concord in New Hampshire, Mont Perlier in Vermont, Boston in Massachusetts, Providance in Rhode Island and Hartfordd in Connecticut? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my basic thinking is that you want a group of magi who are at a similiar level to the Nemean in power and status, but not directly in Boston so they compete directly with him, but not so far removed that they aren't interested in what happens in Boston.<br /> <br /> More thinking aloud: You could read the Chariot of Epona as the proto-SL caucus. Yes, they're a single cabal, but they're supposed to have had a sort of network of other cabals attatched to them, in mutual opposition to the mysterium led Stone Assembly. That'd give a basis for giving the New England caucus some personality. Sort of Greco-Celtic mysticism mixed with native American traditions. Plus...<br /> <br /> One thing I've been thinking of doing is centring the Caucus on the Secret Concord. To join the SL you need to sign your name to the concord, but you obviously can't read it. The further you progress into the Mystery cult the more is revealed to you. So the Nemean being deacon knows the most about it.<br /> <br /> Thing is then, Chain being a singnatory would be a further sign of the Nemean's disrespect of the SL caucus (which he seems to already show). Letting a Mystagogue into the inner most secrets of the caucus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> instead of proper Magisterium in Ladder? </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. The Magisterium is meant to be the college of magisters and you can only have 1 per caucus. The local magisterium presumably includes other caucuses from other regions, like Chicago for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T10:16:21-07:00","id":865994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865909#post865909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you say there is only one, massive New England SL Caucus, that each town is is only headed by it's Deacon? So whole Caucus is streching from Augusta in Maine, Concord in New Hampshire, Mont Perlier in Vermont, Boston in Massachusetts, Providance in Rhode Island and Hartfordd in Connecticut? Each have one local Deacon and they rule, instead of proper Magisterium in Ladder?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe Witch Trials are reason? When rest of States were having more or less steady colonization, New England had Banishers, trials, Inquistion and other problems. I can easily see how this leads to understaffed Silver Ladder and often titels rotation in Order - so New Englands Tearchs adapt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry, East Coast, of course - early morning writting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, couple things I want to point out, because I live in western Massachusetts and have lived in Vermont, and have an insider's knowledge (although I admit I am very, very shaky on my knowledge of Mage and of Boston proper).<br /> <br /> -While Montpelier is the capital of Vermont, it's not the largest city. That belongs to Burlington, which has more colleges, more culture, more people, more shopping, it's just generally more in every way. I'd guess that, unless the local Mages are real sticklers for keeping their head city the same as their capital, they'd choose Burlington instead. (The order of city-sizes goes Burlington, South Burlington, Rutland, Barre, Montpelier. South Burlington is really just an extension of Burlington. Rutland is a scuzzy city that I'm pretty sure is run by vampires. Barre and Montpelier are also basically the same city.)<br /> -I'm pretty sure Maine is similar to Vermont, in that it's capital Augusta is not the most populous or a good place to rule from. I'd pick Portland, Bangor, maybe Auburn. For New Hampshire, you'll want Manchester. Providence for Rhode Island and Hartford for Connecticut are both the largest and the capital, so those work fine.<br /> -Splitting out areas by state makes a kind of sense, until you look at population. Vermont has very few people in it; their total population is only a little more than the city of Boston not including suburbs (0.6M each). New Hampshire (1.3M), Maine (1.3M), and Rhode Island (1.0M) have about twice as many people as Vermont; Connecticut has triple that again (3.6M); and Massachusetts has double that (6.7M). It might make sense population- and area- wise to group Vermont, New Hampshire, and Maine into one area, Connecticut and Rhode Island into another, and Massachusetts into a third, at least starting out. <br /> -Of course, all the states are super independent; I know Vermonters get pissy when they're forgotten about or glossed over because they're so tiny. It could easily be each state has it's own deacon. If you go that route, though, western Massachusetts also gets pissy when Boston/eastern Mass gets all the money and attention. They should either have their own Deacon, or be trying to create one. (Plot hook?) The area has very different interests and needs than the city, and it's a real thing that we get overlooked.<br /> -While New York isn't part of New England (because it was settled by the Dutch first), upstate New York has a lot more cultural similarities with Vermont/New Hampshire/Maine than with NYC proper, and might make sense to include as a region. (This would be the area of New York located north of the city, hence &quot;up&quot;.)<br /> -There's a lot of MA cities that are very full of crime. Holyoke, Springfield, New Bedford, Chelsea, Brockton, Worchester (pronounced wu-ster), probably more that I'm forgetting. But yeah, if you want peaceful small towns, you can do it in Mass, buuuuut be careful of exactly where. Vermont is much more back-country, but there's a lot of drugs. (Fun fact: Vermont has the least strict gun laws in the area, due to all the game hunters in the state. So there's a whole back market of getting guns there, then driving them down to states like Massachusetts that have much stricter laws. New Hampshire has the least strict fireworks laws, so the same thing happens with them.)<br /> -Awakening in Vermont leads to a higher-than-average chance of being a Thyrsus. Seriously the state is so full of hippies. It's against the law to have billboards there. But hunting is still a huge thing.<br /> -Please please please don't use the witch trials as a thing. There's loads of actual historical reasons for things to be weird in the area, given who settled where and when, how we drove out/infected with plague the native folk, how there was a fair amount of eugenics going on after WW1, etc. The witch trials are overdone, and were honestly about claiming land and political power. If you've got a chance to look at the Dark Era's stuff for that, it treats it pretty well, but I strongly encourage you not to make the witch trials a &quot;real&quot; thing. (I'm still pissed at Rowling for doing that. Also for her entire treatment of US magical history. It is some painful bull. But that's offtopic.)<br /> <br /> Sorry for the spew, but I'm happy to add/clarify if there's anything you want to know more about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T11:54:05-07:00","id":866032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865994#post865994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the spew, but I'm happy to add/clarify if there's anything you want to know more about.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>AceOfAlmonds</b>, thanks for info - it's always good to have local people see over your fictional settings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865994#post865994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(All cool informations about New England.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much on the expending my knowledge of area, I will try to have them in my mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865994#post865994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might make sense population- and area- wise to group Vermont, New Hampshire, and Maine into one area, Connecticut and Rhode Island into another, and Massachusetts into a third, at least starting out.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we talk still about one giant Silver Ladder Caucus - or Three smaller ones? And if one giant - Does it governed by &quot;Council of Senior Deacons&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865994#post865994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Of course, all the states are super independent; I know Vermonters get pissy when they're forgotten about or glossed over because they're so tiny. It could easily be each state has it's own deacon. If you go that route, though, western Massachusetts also gets pissy when Boston/eastern Mass gets all the money and attention. They should either have their own Deacon, or be trying to create one. (Plot hook?) The area has very different interests and needs than the city, and it's a real thing that we get overlooked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boston Unveiled is showing Western Massachusetts as disorganized &quot;Here Are Dragons&quot; - I would stick to this idea. The lone Awakened or few cabals try to pass their independence, but still they nominally answer to Boston. At least it would be my take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865994#post865994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-There's a lot of MA cities that are very full of crime. Holyoke, Springfield, New Bedford, Chelsea, Brockton, Worchester (pronounced wu-ster), probably more that I'm forgetting. But yeah, if you want peaceful small towns, you can do it in Mass, buuuuut be careful of exactly where. Vermont is much more back-country, but there's a lot of drugs. (Fun fact: Vermont has the least strict gun laws in the area, due to all the game hunters in the state. So there's a whole back market of getting guns there, then driving them down to states like Massachusetts that have much stricter laws. New Hampshire has the least strict fireworks laws, so the same thing happens with them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect! Ideal reason why New England is still treated as &quot;Untamed Frontier&quot; - we have Wild Wild... East here, yes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865994#post865994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Awakening in Vermont leads to a higher-than-average chance of being a Thyrsus. Seriously the state is so full of hippies. It's against the law to have billboards there. But hunting is still a huge thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will remember where to put my FC hippies from Dreamspeakers Legacy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865994#post865994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Please please please don't use the witch trials as a thing. There's loads of actual historical reasons for things to be weird in the area, given who settled where and when, how we drove out/infected with plague the native folk, how there was a fair amount of eugenics going on after WW1, etc. The witch trials are overdone, and were honestly about claiming land and political power. If you've got a chance to look at the Dark Era's stuff for that, it treats it pretty well, but I strongly encourage you not to make the witch trials a &quot;real&quot; thing. (I'm still pissed at Rowling for doing that. Also for her entire treatment of US magical history. It is some painful bull. But that's offtopic.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Witch Trials <b><i>are</i></b> a thing in <b>Boston Unveiled</b> - it's one of reasons why Salem is center of power in <b>BU</b>. We can always point to other things, but for the so heritage obsessed Order like Silver Ladder. events like Witch Trials will be prominent.<br /> <br /> As to Rowling idea - it can be cheesy in place, but when look over our exploration in topic on Tearchs Caucus - we basiclly make MACUSA for Silver Ladders of New England, with all the Deacons idea, don't we? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I probably do not want to run this as such, make it more cult-like &quot;pyramid&quot; (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) structure - but you can see analogies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T13:03:46-07:00","id":866068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=866032#post866032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we talk still about one giant Silver Ladder Caucus - or Three smaller ones? And if one giant - Does it governed by &quot;Council of Senior Deacons&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it going either way. It would certainly match with real-world politics if there was a head organization in Boston for the entire New England area, with three or six sub-areas that one person was a representative of. (Full disclosure, I have no idea how the Silver Ladder works.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=866032#post866032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boston Unveiled is showing Western Massachusetts as disorganized &quot;Here Are Dragons&quot; - I would stick to this idea. The lone Awakened or few cabals try to pass their independence, but still they nominally answer to Boston. At least it would be my take.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works to some extent. Population-wise, western Mass has about half the population of eastern mass. I could see the area being more Free Council than anything, possibly with a number of small cabals trying to work to get representation. There should be larger groups in places like Springfield, Greenfield, the Pioneer Valley, and Worcester, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=866032#post866032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect! Ideal reason why New England is still treated as &quot;Untamed Frontier&quot; - we have Wild Wild... East here, yes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, &quot;Wild West&quot; implies to me a lack of civilization, so people turn to guns and crime to make their own rules. &quot;Wild East&quot; is more like there's plenty of civilization, loads of it, but people still turn to guns and crime and make their own rules. Still with the edge of there being a lot of forest around, though. Closer to mobsters than cowboys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=866032#post866032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Witch Trials <b><i>are</i></b> a thing in <b>Boston Unveiled</b> - it's one of reasons why Salem is center of power in <b>BU</b>. We can always point to other things, but for the so heritage obsessed Order like Silver Ladder. events like Witch Trials will be prominent.<br /> <br /> As to Rowling idea - it can be cheesy in place, but when look over our exploration in topic on Tearchs Caucus - we basiclly make MACUSA for Silver Ladders of New England, with all the Deacons idea, don't we? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I probably do not want to run this as such, make it more cult-like &quot;pyramid&quot; (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) structure - but you can see analogies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize that Boston Unveiled uses the witch trials, and I don't like it. I have not read it, but it sounds like it's making the witch trials &quot;real&quot; (in the sense of &quot;there was actual magic and said magic-users were persecuted and the cause of this&quot;). Which, no, historically, that's completely wrong, and it's been done a lot, and only rarely well. If you go to Salem, and go on a tour, they'll tell you this, that the trials were about politics, about the conflict between Salem Town and Salem Village, and that deaths happened when trials got out of hand. The whole thing gets a lot more attention then it needs (similar to Roanoke colony, but that's another tangent), while other options remain unexplored.<br /> <br /> Like, if you want New England to be a land of mystery, how about this: Most of the native tribes in New England are extinct. Before white folks came to settle, a lot of them got wiped out by a plague. Once white people got here, they started expediting the process, trading tribes blankets infected with smallpox, enslaving or killing those who were left. For tribes that got wise, they ended up getting driven westward, through broken treaties and bloody bloody Andrew Jackson. <br /> <br /> So, there's this whole land who's magical experts have all been killed or driven off. Of course there's mysteries aplenty; none of the settlers know jack about the area, and so you have your mystery-rich area for Mages. And the first folks to &quot;discover&quot; the answers get a lot of prestige, which gets passed down through history, and so they become a big deal. (And you have to take care to treat this one with respect, too, but this is a whole area of history that's been looked at a lot less than the witch trials.)<br /> <br /> The witch trials for New England are like Vikings for Iceland, or the Inquisition for Spain, or like Guy Fawkes for England: yes, they are a thing that happened, but they get waaaaaaaaaaaay more focus then they proportionally deserve, at the expense of a lot of other history, and have been done and done again with varying levels of respect and accuracy.<br /> <br /> Rowling tangent: the MACUSA can't exist. The timeline doesn't work. Unless the wizards of the 1700s were better at seeing the future than Trelawny was, they couldn't have known how the war was going to turn out. You can't govern an area the size of the US with the structure that only barely works in a place the size of England. The whole thing is just...My dislike is not because it's cheesy, my dislike is because it can't work, not even with the normal suspension of disbelief I grant such things. The reason a pyramid-like structure kinda works in Mage is that 1) it's not actually ruling everyone, and 2) all mages have a vested interest in staying hidden because reality punches them in the face if they don't.<br /> <br /> But that's the last I'm going to say about witch trials, outside of any factual stuff, because while I'd like to convince you otherwise, I don't want to derail the thread or spoil the fun of your game or tell you there's things you can't do. Honestly, I'm pretty thrilled that you're running a New England game, and I'd like to help with authentic stuff that makes the game more fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 04-15-2016, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T13:53:33-07:00","id":866097,"title":"","content":"The Mages in BU used the witch trials, the general atmosphere and all of that as political tools. There really isn't any discussion of Mages being persecuted personally because like you said that would be completely unrealistic. I think the closest it came was some factions not enjoying the atmosphere and moving out to the sticks to maintain cover and there may have been some blackmail, like framing a rival's loved ones as witches to apply pressure so you could get something else.<br /> <br /> Honestly, they don't spend a lot of time on it. It's a blip on the Consilieum's history, noted for what impact it had and then moved on from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-15-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T13:58:25-07:00","id":866100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=866097#post866097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mages in BU used the witch trials, the general atmosphere and all of that as political tools. There really isn't any discussion of Mages being persecuted personally because like you said that would be completely unrealistic. I think the closest it came was some factions not enjoying the atmosphere and moving out to the sticks to maintain cover and there may have been some blackmail, like framing a rival's loved ones as witches to apply pressure so you could get something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I may have overreacted in decrying the thing.<br /> <br /> Also, with a username like yours, am I correct in guessing you have some familiarity with the western MA area? W.E.B. DuBois was a pretty influential guy who came from here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T14:00:21-07:00","id":866101,"title":"","content":"Nah, you're right. There's a lot more interesting stuff you could also focus on. Just wanted to point out, the devs are not exactly hamfisted asshats with setting material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T14:03:21-07:00","id":866102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=866101#post866101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, you're right. There's a lot more interesting stuff you could also focus on. Just wanted to point out, the devs are not exactly hamfisted asshats with setting material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize if I implied such. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T14:04:07-07:00","id":866104,"title":"","content":"Stop apologizing for having an opinion. &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T01:14:36-07:00","id":874334,"title":"","content":"Second draft for the Orders of New England in 2E version of Boston. Any comments and thoughts are more than welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Caucuses</b></span><br /> <br /> Pentacle Orders in New England are very loose associations of mages spread around terrain of whole Massachusetts State and some borders counties to it. Proper power of Boston is not very much centralized as inner wars of Bostonian Awakened in XX century and waves of scattered emigrants lead too many sorcerers being left alone to their own devises in small towns and settlements of the region, often ending in Nameless collection in places really isolated from Consilium. Nominally, Orders local societies are full of various ranks many members across New England take on themselves. Realistically, proper Boston\u2019s day to day mage community is understaffed and many times isolationists with not enough mages to run smoothly tasks of Orders in the city, because members are scattered on the map of the state and region.<br /> <br /> This situation changes when Caucuses are called in. Representatives of whole Order come once a month or bi-monthly meetings, exchange knowledge and power in their secret halls. Then mages of New England looks as proper community and force to be reckoned with. And Favors or knowledge exchanged there make lasting relations with all participants. Even if most mages in New England are only nominally subordinate to the Boston\u2019s Consilium, however, they respond to call of colleagues and friends from the Order of the city itself. Counting on their return of Favor if necessary.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Adamantine Arrow: Windham Manor \u2013 Holy Ground</b></span><br /> <br /> On a sea cliff in Gloucester perched Windham Manor. A network of caves extends beneath the house, carved into the rock by millions of years of tides. A sprawling graveyard is located at the back of the property, overlooking the water, but it is almost completely overgrown. It\u2019s here where New England\u2019s Arrows meet bimonthly (usually sometime during the third week of the month) on request of <i>Ferrum </i>\u2013 Adamant Sage. This place is chosen on the tradition for family ground of <i>Hydra</i> - Sage Emeritus \u2013 that\u2019s family and cabal <i>Gravediggers </i>have protected Boston and region for centuries. At least once a year, Ferrum likes to put on an exhibition of the Duel Arcane, inviting any and all mages of the Arrow to observe or, even better, participate.<br /> <br /> <i>Apollonia</i> from <i>The Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth</i> is Vidantus \u2013 working mostly as teacher of new Arrows, trying to not go for more bloodshed in her life, understanding it\u2019s her time after being defeated by <i>Ferrum </i>and the death of <i>Ares</i>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Free Council: <i>Emerald Scroll</i> Bar \u2013 Assembly and Lore House</b></span><br /> <br /> Located at Roxbury neighborhood waterfront, this Tarot\u2019s Major Arcana styled place is open Lore House to any mage that will enter. Leaded by Davy Jones column of <i>Dead Wrens</i> can sell you anything they can get hands on. And make great parties. They even sell alchemical potions as drinks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Even then this place name is still affront for the Guardians for taking password of their sacred XIX century Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> <i>Emerald Scroll</i> is also Assembly meeting place \u2013 treated mostly as Free Council Caucus once a month, in weekend long \u2018members only\u2019 event \u2013 it\u2019s open on day-to-day basis to any mage that want to trade Mysteries or sell magic for quick cash. \u201cLocal\u201d Assembly can be called almost every day, but it\u2019s rulings are taken only to represent Boston mages self-interests \u2013 <i>Dead Wrens</i> understand that beside them, every few days visits of <i>SMG</i> and city passing Libertine or two \u2013 day-to-day rulings of Assembly do not really reflect New England community at large.<br /> <br /> <b>Note: </b><i>I want to remake Dead Wrens as Libertines only column \u2013 they mix of Orders in 1E looks as dictated only old stereotype of \u201cWarriors=Arrows\u201d or \u201cExplorers=Mysterium\u201d. Also, they are pirates and thieves, god dammit, how much Nameless can one be more!</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Guardians of Veil: Order of the Golden Dawn, <i>true</i> Emerald Scroll and Oubliette \u2013 Labyrinth</b></span><br /> <br /> Once, Guardians Labyrinth was glorious in Boston \u2013 on wave of occult interest in and of XIX century and first decades of XX century, it grew and grew, spanning from one secret society to the next. <i>Order of the Golden Dawn</i> split itself in to a lot of cults and sects, each with it slightly different dogma. But each answering to secrets signs of <i>Emerald Scroll</i> \u2013 code name for group of Cultors from the Order. Sadly, it\u2019s now only glorious past.<br /> <br /> Today, Guardians still control many of connections between cults, but after Free Council revolt \u2013 and even Libertines claiming the name for secret cabal as bar name! \u2013 It\u2019s much, much weakened. Restoring Labyrinth to its former splendor is one of priorities for <i>Shadow Chorus</i> and its leader <i>Culsu</i> \u2013 Epopt of the Guardians. Over watching Boston Consilium after \u201edisappearance\u201d of <i>Nemean</i> is second. Both they oversee from their secret sanctum called <i>Oubliette</i>, door\u2019s to one can open anywhere in the New England. Once a month, in the settlement of whole Massachusetts, portals to it are open and Guardians come to plan their next moves in reclaiming the region and safe keeping the magic. <i>Februs</i>, <i>Culsu</i>\u2019s cabal mate, is appointed Interfector of the Caucus.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mysterium: Academy of the <i>Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth</i> - Athenaeum</b></span><br /> <br /> Academy apartment building in the Beacon Hill area, with north wing working as sanctum for fellow Arrows from <i>Exalted Knights of the Gryphon</i> to defend the Supernal Mysteries stronghold. As name suggest, this particular Athenaeum works mostly in Academy model (see <b>Mysterium</b> book), teaching newly Awakened under guise of private school for \u201cexceptional students\u201d. Of course there is Scriptorium part of complex and giant libraries Athenea are known of. Interesting, there is not pointed obvious Censorium in place \u2013 maybe Boston\u2019s Guardians to the Veil are having something to it. As institution, Athenaeum is run by <i>Aurem</i>, one of most dedicated and oldest Mystygoges of Caucus.<br /> <br /> Mysterium caucus in convened at 8 P.M. on the 15th of every month (barring emergency), are rigidly ordered affairs. They are run by <i>Potestas </i>\u2013 eldest (literally) mage of Mysterium and Hierophant of Order, that rivals <i>Aurem</i> for the power in local Order.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Silver Ladder: Magisterium and Cryptopoly</b></span><br /> <br /> Tearchs of New England are both divided and united \u2013 they started as network of Favors leading to <i>Chariot of Epona</i> cabal in beginning of European colonization. With each Favor the Nameless mages of region took, each come closer to Star Precept and many finally embraced traditions of Silver Ladder and Greco-Celtic mysticism of Epona Awakened. Still, new converts stayed very independent in their ways, leading to tradition of local Tearchs to be very separated from Order. This resulted in the unorthodox way the Magisterium works \u2013 organization is splinted in to regions ruled by one Grand Magister each - Vermont, New Hampshire, and Maine under one. Connecticut and Rhode Island in to second. And Massachusetts as last one. They are filled with local Magisters, but they have lower standing in Order as such.<br /> <br /> Problem came with <i>Nemean </i>\u2013 his tyranny was once a pretense, designed to unite mages in Boston against him, but that he no longer wished to release his grip on Hierarchy for any reason. Thearchs saw the Lion symbols in his appearance and Shadow Name as a forgotten code for his role and hoped to find someone strong enough to make him honor it. Finally, <i>Khumeia</i> with help of her allies made him \u201cdisappear\u201d ( in truth, take him to Chicago on trial under other Magisterium ) and lead to freeing Boston from his iron grip. But then come next problem \u2013 what to do with new found freedom? <i>Khumeia</i> become Deacon and Magister in title, but not in her Arcana and planning \u2013 she is still only Adept and her vision of Boston to come shows signs of bit lack focus. She also is denied, at least for now, Grand Magister title until she become Master \u2013 that result in lowered standing of Boston as whole in New England Caucus. Rest of Boston Tearchs presses her to quicker her Mind Arcanum studies, rest see this as sign of weakness and use it as next excuse to attack her leadership.<br /> <br /> Boston\u2019s Cryptopoly spreads from <i>Lodge of Eight Chambers</i> \u2013 <i>Khumeia\u2019s </i>cabal <i>Illuminated Pentad </i>sanctum on the two top floors of downtown skyscraper. This entrusted with Masonic and alchemical symbols place is heart from which starts to flourish part of Bostonian occult underground. Many secret societies and cults owe them allegiance or are manipulated by <i>Lodge</i>. What\u2019s odd, most of those groups have history with <i>Order of Golden Dawn</i> that put\u2019s in question how Pentad got hold on those groups. Some rumors states they stole them from uncovered Guardians XX century Cultors notes \u2013 but even <i>Shadow Chorus</i> do not dares to accuse them publicly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":".  Added Cryptopoly description 04-26-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T08:29:18-07:00","id":874560,"title":"","content":"Quick question - Awakening of my players is more and more near. With that come the issue of apprenticeship. <b>What cabals could work together with <i>Illuminated Pentad </i>on teaching new mages?</b> Silver Ladder are obviously not needed, but how about Guardians and Free Council, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T10:20:08-07:00","id":875745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=874560#post874560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question - Awakening of my players is more and more near. With that come the issue of apprenticeship. <b>What cabals could work together with <i>Illuminated Pentad </i>on teaching new mages?</b> Silver Ladder are obviously not needed, but how about Guardians and Free Council, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>The White Putnams work well as mentors, provided the new mages don't mind being taught about Awakened Jesus. Better if TWO mages are sent to the estate to be trained, one by team Chain Parris and the other by team Moriah, to highlight the ideological wedge that's being driven in the Cabal.<br /> <br /> The Brotherhood of Ineffable Truth could let a few new mages bunk with the Exalted Knights of the Gryphon and be trained by them, if you have players who are of a more militaristic bent.<br /> <br /> Finally we have the Shadow Chorus who in my opinion make for excellent mentors. They are almost all a blank slate behind their masks so you can give them any reason you can think of for taking in new mages. Plus at the end of the apprenticeship there's a cool mask and robe as parting gifts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11689-kokiteno","name":"Kokiteno","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T11:28:48-07:00","id":875796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=865994#post865994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for the spew, but I'm happy to add/clarify if there's anything you want to know more about.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I am going to take the opportunity to ask: What other mysteries would you suggest for the area? (Aside from the ones already discussed) Doesn't have to be super elaborate, but maybe a few things I could use as plot hooks or to search for more information by myself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T12:58:56-07:00","id":875885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=875796#post875796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I am going to take the opportunity to ask: What other mysteries would you suggest for the area? (Aside from the ones already discussed) Doesn't have to be super elaborate, but maybe a few things I could use as plot hooks or to search for more information by myself?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll give it a shot. Not sure which &quot;area&quot; you want (greater New England, Massachusetts in general, Boston-specific) so I'll try to pitch a couple of each. All of the things here are true, though possibly slightly exaggerated for the sake of being in the World of Darkness. I can go into more detail/throw more stuff from a specific area, too.<br /> <br /> New England:<br /> -Vermont used to be a state of industry, of production, of creation. Now it's a state made primarily of forests. Official history ties it to the water wheel becoming obsolete, but there must be something more to it. Did a powerful Thyrsus achieve archmastery and claim the area as her domain? Did a high-ranking spirit of Technology get destroyed, leaving little Nature spirits to grow in its place? Or was all that productivity stirring up something sinister?<br /> -The city of Killington tried to succeed to New Hampshire, ostensibly for tax reasons. The attempt was absurd and doomed to failure, but why was it made? Did some legal manipulation go awry? Was it meant as a cover or distraction for another act? Or did the location of the city get re-written?<br /> -Country borders don't hold a lot of mystical significance, generally. So why is it that spells can't penetrate the Canadian border from the US side? It works just fine the other way. Is this some Acanthus prank? A quirk from revolutionary times? Or a recent reflection of current national tensions?<br /> <br /> Massachusetts<br /> -Recently closed, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Higgins_Armory_Museum\" target=\"_blank\">Higgins Armory Museum</a> held the second largest collection of arms and armor in the country. While the collection was supposed to be moved to the Worcester Art Museum, a number of pieces don't appear to have been kept. Were they sold privately to interested collectors? Stolen by rival Mages or ardent Hunters? Or were they fated to fall off the back of a truck into the hands of the one who needed them most?<br /> -Speaking of armories, <a href=\"https://www.nps.gov/spar/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Springfield</a> has been holding guns and ammunition since being commissioned by Washington himself. The going theory is that some of the collection is haunted. How else to explain the sounds of gunfire from deep inside on moonless nights?<br /> -In the Pioneer Valley, there's been a rash of murals. It started with a couple officially-sanctioned ones, but since then, more and more walls have been painted over in the same abstract style. No one's taking credit or tagging it, and there's yet to be an arrest for defacing public property. Is one of the original murals a source of memetic infection? Why are the images so resistant to being scrubbed away? And what happens when the surfaces covered reach critical mass?<br /> -After the protests in the 60s, UMass Amherst was redesigned architectually to be a riot-breaker. It doesn't seem to have helped, though. What is it about the campus that drives students into a destructive frenzy? Does it have anything to do with the bricks that are spat out by the 26-floor library?<br /> -There's a little store off I-91 that sells delicious smoked meats, but only when taking exit 25 southbound. If you take exit 25 northbound, you find a dinosaur museum instead. Trying to backtrack will bring you back to 91, and coming from any other exit will show neither place. What the heck?<br /> <br /> Boston<br /> -On Sundays, the 10:14pm outbound Red Line train always skips Porter station. It's not that it blows by; those on the train hear the announcer go from Harvard to Davis, while those at the station never see the train at all. Does the train go through a fold in space and time? Is it briefly held in another reality? Or does the machinery simply shunt it through the maintenance line?<br /> -The streets of Boston are almost impossible to drive through, with winding one-way roads taking you far, far from your intended destination. It's not uncommon to see the building you want to go to, and end up circling it endlessly in your car, until and unless you find somewhere to park and go in by foot. What is it about cars that the city seems to hate? Has an old spell stuck around from the horse-and-buggy days? Has some Supernal interpretation of &quot;anti-magnetic&quot; been applied to certain buildings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T21:57:14-07:00","id":903271,"title":"","content":"I'm preparing to do full remake of NPC in Boston after reading new corebook. Problem is with <i>Thanatos</i> - new rules on Shadow Name make him staying with 'Necromancy-implying' one a character too much stretch. ( See 'A Rose is a Rose: Shadow Names' on page 292 of MtAw 2E ). <br /> <br /> <b>We need a more Alchemist sounding Name for character. So maybe Hades?</b> Or were there other figure connected to more Alchemy and little to Death in Greek myths?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T05:38:02-07:00","id":903415,"title":"","content":"You don't need to make him a one-mystery mage. You can be an alchemist and an obsessive necromancer as well, the latter provides the impetus for the former. I mean, his write-up is so heavily centred on the necromancer angle and the way it colours his whole personality, if you get rid of that you're basically making a new character.<br /> <br /> Although, if you look up Thanatos, there's an interesting description from the Theogony. &quot;the other [Thanatos] has a heart of iron, and his spirit within him is pitiless as bronze&quot;. Reminds me a little of the attainments that the Uncrowned Kings cultivate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T06:31:07-07:00","id":903437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=903415#post903415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to make him a one-mystery mage. You can be an alchemist and an obsessive necromancer as well, the latter provides the impetus for the former. I mean, his write-up is so heavily centred on the necromancer angle and the way it colours his whole personality, if you get rid of that you're basically making a new character.</div> </div> </div> </div>The soul of character is that he is victim of German Necromacers - that's why he started to study Uncrowned Kings. With 2E take on Shadow Name, calling one self Thanatos will lead you to become epitome of it's myth and role. Being personification of Death is rather bad idea, when you want to run from your Necromancers roots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=903415#post903415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, if you look up Thanatos, there's an interesting description from the Theogony. &quot;the other [Thanatos] has a heart of iron, and his spirit within him is pitiless as bronze&quot;. Reminds me a little of the attainments that the Uncrowned Kings cultivate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be used here - but still, most of Thanatos myths is all about death, so it's probably wrong idea, from Shadow Names rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T06:56:52-07:00","id":903447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=903437#post903437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The soul of character is that he is victim of German Necromacers - that's why he started to study Uncrowned Kings. With 2E take on Shadow Name, calling one self Thanatos will lead you to become epitome of it's myth and role. Being personification of Death is rather bad idea, when you want to run from your Necromancers roots.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it's not. It says they threw him out for something he did and they also probably taught him the legacy in the first place. Nothing in his description says he's running from his roots either, the reverse in fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T08:25:46-07:00","id":903556,"title":"","content":"&lt;Checking my copy of <b>Boston Unveiled</b>...&gt;<br /> <br /> You are right, huh.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BU, p. 86</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was reborn out of his own death, Awakened and, for the first time, truly alive. He learned his craft (and earned his shadow name) from a cabal of Necromancers in Germany, where his father was stationed, but was later cast out by them for some crime of which he does not speak. (He has occasionally intimidated that it was those same Necromancers who initiated him into his Legacy.) He returned to Boston, where he had been born and had spent summers with his mother, who had passed away two years before.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's still not working bit for me - even if we assume that he was trained by Necromancers, they why would he joined <i>Khumeia</i> and most Alchemical Legacy there is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T08:31:09-07:00","id":903564,"title":"","content":"Because Mages are more complex than a single magical issue and Necromancy and Alchemy are all mixed up in each other anyways since they share a Path.<br /> <br /> Actually, you can also look at it like this, he was trained by necromancers and took his shadow name while working with necromancers. It had already warped him in the way that shadow names do, working on his nimbus, having him become more like Thanatos, etc. Changing your shadow name is a big deal, maybe he's just acknowledging his past by keeping it, or maybe he feels trapped in it, or maybe he's come to identify with the name so much that despite moving away from necromancy he simply can't or won't separate himself from it.<br /> <br /> Rather than just saying it doesn't fit and changing it, how about figuring out the effects of it still being there, it can become a plot hook, maybe a Mystery even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-30-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T11:56:21-07:00","id":903691,"title":"","content":"There is also the fact that the term &quot;necromancers&quot; could have been used in the character description as a shorthand for Moros mages, since, you know, it's kind of their nickname back in 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:16:00-07:00","id":903732,"title":"","content":"The whole problem with 1E Thanatos character is that he is so &quot;bad necromancer&quot; archetype. For my chronicle I need him to be Alchemist, dedicated to Uncrowned Kings. But when I read his 1E description is just so... 'bad necromancer' - it's so bad taste plain, you know? Will need to think more on his idea to turn away from Death and embracing Matter and Mind then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:38:53-07:00","id":903751,"title":"","content":"Reading his description it looks like it was indeed just a group of Moros who weren't necessarily Death focused, he joined the Uncrowned Kings without giving it too much thought and then continued to delve into his dealings with ghosts and the Underworld. If he continues to develop his legacy then he'll probably use it to enhance his force of personality the better for controlling the restless dead of Boston.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:52:49-07:00","id":903996,"title":"","content":"<i>Illuminated Pentad</i>, as cabal, is written with Alchemy as main theme of their group and rituals. So it does have sense that their Moros that is Uncrowned King is Alchemist variant of the Path of Doom. Especially as 2E canonical change is that most Moros are Alchemist and Necromancers are a small minority - so highlighting proper Alchemist Moros in setting should be preferred.<br /> <br /> In the end - I will remake Thanatos in to Alchemist, rather than Necromancer. <b>Question is should he have changed Shadow Name to something more alchemy related with 2E rules on Names?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T03:27:26-07:00","id":904066,"title":"","content":"Just because the Moros Path now has two nicknames doesn't suddenly mean that Necromancers are in the minority.<br /> <br /> Obviously if you're remaking the character into something completely different he should have a different shadow name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T03:49:46-07:00","id":904072,"title":"","content":"Alchemist is the &quot;bigger&quot; name for Moros now, because both Death and Matter are forms of Alchemical Change; you can be a Death &quot;Alchemist&quot;, because Death is, in the essence, about changing from one state to another. Obviously, Necromancer wasn't that good of a nickname for Matter Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T05:05:04-07:00","id":904094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=903732#post903732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's so bad taste plain, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. But whatever.<br /> <br /> Pick an alchemist. Why not have him name himself after Flamel? I mean, your story is already about him, so why not make the link explicit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:29:42-07:00","id":904135,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who can't understand wrydhamster, but wants to respond seriously? @_@","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:21:12-07:00","id":904171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiwass</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=904135#post904135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who can't understand wrydhamster, but wants to respond seriously? @_@</div> </div> </div> </div>What is here to understand? I do remake of Boston setting in terms of 2E. I have chronicle centered on Supernal Alchemy, so I want too use extensively alchemy-based cabal from setting - <i>Illuminated Pentad</i>. Moros character in <b>Boston Unveiled</b> book - <i>Thanatos</i> - is written as 'bad Necromancer' stereotype, even if being member of Uncrowned Kings. I want to remake him into proper Alchemist then. <b>Question is should be still called <i>Thanatos</i> or should he be renamed - and if yes, then in to what?</b> It all comes from 2E rules on Shadow Names that they are meaningful for character and fulfill in stories.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:33:18-07:00","id":904178,"title":"","content":"Yes, you probably should rename him.<br /> <br /> There's nothing about being an Uncrowned King that prevents you from being a &quot;bad&quot; necromancer though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T03:52:23-07:00","id":904840,"title":"","content":"Ah. I'd keep him as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T06:17:59-07:00","id":923205,"title":"","content":"Run yesterday first game session in Boston proper setting - Had a slight problem as I needed some front for the work of <i>Illuminated Pentad</i> to recruit new mages. I thought that law firm would work with Silver Ladder profile of group and that Pentad is said to have two floors of scrapper, when one would be more than enough for cabals Lodge of Eight Chambers itself.<br /> <br /> So I made that PCs were invited by <i>Faustina</i> that 'happened' to cross paths with them ( ah, Fate magic! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and she get them business card of <i>'Saint Martin &amp; Partners'</i> law firm in downtown, where <i>Khumeia</i> and <i>Thanatos</i> ( that I will rename him to <i><a href=\"http://www.crystalinks.com/demosthenes2.html\" target=\"_blank\">Demosthenes</a></i> ) are running firm.<br /> <br /> <b>So what do you think about adding law firm as front to the Illuminated Pentad and the name of <i>'Saint Martin &amp; Partners'</i> sounds good?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-29-2016, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:15:12-07:00","id":923338,"title":"","content":"Doesn't Khumeia already own a private bank or financial firm? I kinda assumed that's the company's buidling. Changing it to a law firm isn't really a big stretch.<br /> <br /> Demosthenes isn't exactly the guy I think of for alchemy but whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:22:38-07:00","id":929806,"title":"","content":"I translate into Polish names of Boston cabals. But I have a problem with one name. <b>My dictionaries cannot found what does Putnams in '<i>White Putnams</i>'?</b> Can someone describe to me what is going in this name meaning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:12:03-07:00","id":929844,"title":"","content":"The Putnams were a family in the Salem area of New England during the witch trials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:46:11-07:00","id":929907,"title":"","content":"It will be something completely unclear to my Polish players. Would translation meaning 'Puritans' or 'Pilgrims'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:49:41-07:00","id":929910,"title":"","content":"Instead of translating, you could reinvent the name. Why are they called White Putnams? Find the question, find the answer in English, and then answer it in Polish. If it doesn't work, just create a new name that will resonate in Polish and will tell something about the Cabal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-11-2016, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:18:13-07:00","id":929929,"title":"","content":"I plan to end this way - 'White Pilgrims' or 'White Puritans' will be change of name, but adhere more to their identity than to surname players will not understand on first seeing.<br /> <br /> I have the same problem with <i>Sanguine Laurel </i> - 'Bloody Laurel' could work, but it adds a bit macabre tone to cabal name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:18:22-07:00","id":929930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=929907#post929907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will be something completely unclear to my Polish players. Would translation meaning 'Puritans' or 'Pilgrims'?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty unclear in English too. If you don't know much about the Salem Trials, you probably aren't going to get that it's a family name. As for the name itself it's modifed Old English. So, it has basically no meaning in even 17th century English.<br /> <br /> If you want to avoid mixing Polish and English in the same title, Pilgrims sounds like a good idea and kinda links with the motif of paths; whilst 'Puritan' isn't something you'd refer to yourself as. Mind you, I'm kinda curious what 'puritan' would be in Polish seeing as it's the name of an English religious movement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:25:37-07:00","id":929935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=929930#post929930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to avoid mixing Polish and English in the same title, Pilgrims sounds like a good idea and kinda links with the motif of paths; whilst 'Puritan' isn't something you'd refer to yourself as. Mind you, I'm kinda curious what 'puritan' would be in Polish seeing as it's the name of an English religious movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the same in English, But in Polish 'Puritan' is more precisely English settlers in America, as more general 'Protestant' is for any post-Luther Christian that is strictly non-Catholic. In feel that in our language 'Puritans=American settlers' than religion at large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T14:47:56-07:00","id":929979,"title":"","content":"I think you mean Democritus discoverer of the atom not Demosthenes the famous orator. Also in Dark Eras the Knights of St. George Hunters who specialize in hunting mages are the ones behind the witch trials. Is this realistic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T14:57:11-07:00","id":929984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=929979#post929979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you mean Democritus discoverer of the atom not Demosthenes the famous orator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you click the link? They appear to have borrowed the name from someones D&amp;D site, where Demosthenes is a God of Alchemy or something...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is this realistic? </div> </div> </div>In what sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T15:15:03-07:00","id":929993,"title":"","content":"In the sense that the supernaturals secretly behind the witch trials are a Conspiracy of Hunters who specialize in hunting mages. One of the earlier posters had the opinion that even in the CoD, the witch trials were strictly a mortal thing and had nothing to do with mages. I'm just pointing out that Dark Eras disagrees with his opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T15:43:54-07:00","id":930002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=929993#post929993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the sense that the supernaturals secretly behind the witch trials are a Conspiracy of Hunters who specialize in hunting mages. One of the earlier posters had the opinion that even in the CoD, the witch trials were strictly a mortal thing and had nothing to do with mages. I'm just pointing out that Dark Eras disagrees with his opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Knights ran a shadow court to prosecute hunters in parrallel to the witch trials.<br /> <br /> Also, Doubting Souls completely ignores Boston Unveiled. In BU, there are no Awakened in Salem at the time of the trials. The precursor to the Ebon Noose cabal summoned the Prince of 10,000 Leaves on the spot that would become Salem, and as a result the Awakened generally avoided the place because they can all tell that something really bad happened there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T00:44:28-07:00","id":930228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=930002#post930002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Doubting Souls completely ignores Boston Unveiled. In BU, there are no Awakened in Salem at the time of the trials. The precursor to the Ebon Noose cabal summoned the Prince of 10,000 Leaves on the spot that would become Salem, and as a result the Awakened generally avoided the place because they can all tell that something really bad happened there.</div> </div> </div> </div>As this is 2E patch of BU setting, maybe we should reconsider this subject.<i> Doubting Souls</i> is much more fresher setting, made for 2E <b>CoD</b> games. <b>Boston Unveiled</b> has over ten years now and this particular topic is made to clean it up. So maybe <i>Doubting Souls</i> should be taken in consideration of it,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T02:32:37-07:00","id":930252,"title":"","content":"I would dispute it being fresher but that's just personal preference. I could see melding them together. I mean, it is an interesting coincidence that the Knights decide to have their shadow court on the spot where an Annunaki was summoned into the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T02:48:23-07:00","id":930257,"title":"","content":"After looking over Doubting Souls and Boston Unveiled again, I realized Michael was right. Apparently the witch trials had little to do with mages after all. I will update my timeline accordingly. Thanks.<br /> S","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T02:51:06-07:00","id":930258,"title":"","content":"Actually, Doubting Souls outright says that during the Era, almost if not all of the Awakened left Salem during the trails. The book blames the chaos of the witch trails, but it is still allows a certain amount of coexistence between the two version, I think (need to check BU to be sure)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T22:44:10-07:00","id":930727,"title":"","content":"Have a need for NPC - One of my players wanted to play Seer. When asked why, she says that Sleepers are stupid. Mind I do not want to rebuild the game for this, but I thought that maybe little temptation of Other Side wanting to enroll character can be interesting. <b>So I need good Seer recruiter to eye for her - are those in <i>Boston Unveiled</i> or do I need to make one myself?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T01:13:35-07:00","id":930742,"title":"","content":"I think Kether would be a good choice. I mean, she's an alchemist, so she'll be interested in your plot; plus she's a more quiet Seer so she won't want your player to be murdering Pentacle magi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T01:46:18-07:00","id":930746,"title":"","content":"You might as well throw a Mysteium member at her too for comparison since that Order frequently harbors people who don't like Sleepers either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T02:55:46-07:00","id":930752,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a>, thanks for <i>Kether</i>, I will then get her updated to 2E from 1E corebook. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> , that was plan from the start - showing some lofty Mysterium mage that is biased against Sleepers - probably use <i>Potestat</i> for this. But I will get Seer also in her orbit - even just to tease player in going for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-13-2016, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T05:26:55-07:00","id":932473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=785575#post785575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that the subtext of The Unmurdered Man and The Human Heart was about the Nemean's Seeking, and that he is now an Archmaster proper, and an Aswad at that.<br /> Then again, I always looked upon the Nemean with some kind of horrified fascination and respect. I like the character, I really do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nemean is what made me think hey<br /> <br /> Hey maybe I won't always play an Obrimos","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:24:17-07:00","id":947114,"title":"","content":"I want to talk a bit about character of <i>Amanda Kether</i>. Mage 1E corebook shows she is Moros from Panopticon, yet she does not have any dot in Space. I also do not understand why she would be in Panopticon - she isn't very 'paranoia inducing'. I could say she used hallucinogens and her alchemy to created potions that will split humanity - and by this, she would work under Iron Seal of Unity. Maybe someone have good arguments why <i>Kether</i> should stay as Panopticon in 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T09:36:09-07:00","id":947822,"title":"","content":"There are three ideas that have occurred to me:<br /> <br /> 1) Make her a proper Watcher and change her traits accordingly. In this version of the character, Kether is a Panopticon Seer who works in hallucinogenic drugs that increase paranoia and makes people more susceptible to possession through an Profane Urim.<br /> <br /> 2) She only pays lip service to the Eye, she belongs in fact to the Oikoumene methodology, hoarding dangerous psyops drugs and leveraging them for influence and more research funds.<br /> <br /> 3) Change her allegiance to the Unity. Her research is clearly aimed at making people more docile and easier to manipulate. She could have the Asylum as a rival pylon, the latter devoted to the Eye and it's dream of control through surveillance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:42:28-07:00","id":947867,"title":"","content":"If Kether happens to have a Profane Urim in her possession (or can reasonably get access to one) she doesn't necessarily need any dots in Space herself. Just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T12:09:53-07:00","id":947936,"title":"","content":"I will probably change her to serve Unity - I like her as alchemist, so basic dots spread from corebook is okay.<br /> <br /> Also, my players are stuborn lot - they refuse to take Khumeia's 'offer' about giving them lessons and Awakened contacts for giving their Flamels books. Seeing how unreasonable they are, I think Khumeia will send friendly Guardian to watch over them and try to induct one of PCs most suitated to Veil. Question is simple - Who could it be from Boston setting? Best would be also one that can hide his aura with Prime 2 spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-10-2016, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:06:08-07:00","id":948156,"title":"","content":"Death 2 helps you hide your aura too. It's probably better than Prime 2, in fact, because it also hides all spells affecting you; that's a pretty nice benefit for one spell slot.<br /> Anyway, why do you consider them unreasonable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T23:08:49-07:00","id":948392,"title":"","content":"Looking over <i>Shadow Chorus</i> mages I see most Guardians in there already have Prime 1 - it's logical that they would want to rise it to Prime 2 in few years after the<b> Boston Unveiled</b> presentation that my setting is. I'm also baffled why <i>Disscordia</i> is from Mysterium - she is just as sneaky as rest of Guardians and she takes part in they dress ups. Mysterium mage would be <i>much</i> more straight forward, especially with their Order's Protocols.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=948156#post948156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death 2 helps you hide your aura too. It's probably better than Prime 2, in fact, because it also hides all spells affecting you; that's a pretty nice benefit for one spell slot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime 2 can change your Aura in to Sleeper - it's<i> best</i> solution, where you are looking as almost anybody in crowd, at least as magic goes. So I think there it also hide spells over you, as it would illogical otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=948156#post948156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, why do you consider them unreasonable?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Khumeia</i> asked them to get books - she planned to just studied them with PCs, she <i>does not</i> plan to steal them of them. She may seems very strong willed and a bit extortionist - but it's nothing than other Diamond mage would do about their Obsession. Players also have three of books, so it's bit weird they resist so much. Well, they need to see how Awakened world can be dangerous in first place, they will return to her then, begging for helping them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. I play <i>Khumeia </i>as strong willed and obsessed over Alchemy, but she is still leader of Silver Ladder - she just proposed job as intern in her law firm for Obrimos that previously worked as grocery store cashier. She also said that she can get her post somewhere else, if PC is more willing to that. Like she said: <i>'In Order we have proverb - Silver Ladder is road to victory.'</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T01:55:08-07:00","id":948450,"title":"","content":"If they don't like her because she keeps strong arming them then it's not unreasonable that they won't give her anything they don't have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T03:37:38-07:00","id":948480,"title":"","content":"Looking over how to disrupt my PCs life, I found out nice Banisher cabal called <i>St. Michael\u2019s Promise </i>that is from South End and Chinatown. And my most resisting PCs are staying with their Sleeper family on border between South End and Roxbury. I sense large subplot brewing here... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Is it only me or St. Micheal's Promise is working for Malleus Malleficafrum, even when they were created 3 years before Hunter Conspiracy?</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:33:32-07:00","id":948512,"title":"","content":"They're not. The priest who heads up that Banisher cabal is trying but has not succeeded (so far) in being validated by the Catholic Church as part of the Inquisition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T08:18:00-07:00","id":948619,"title":"","content":"Well, he is a mage. If I was in the MM I'd want to keep them at arms length and in one spot where I can see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T10:24:32-07:00","id":948668,"title":"","content":"<b>Boston Unveiled</b> seems to agree with me on Malleus Maleficarum...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BU, p. 98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The group has a mentor, Father David Pierce, who provides direct, personal pastoral counseling to the cabal and quietly informs the Vatican about what the Banishers are doing. Ideally, Father Pierce would like to get a special dispensation from the <b>Sacred Congregation for the Doctrine and the Faith</b> (the modern euphemistic name for the Office of the Inquisition) to allow St. Michael\u2019s Promise to travel as needed to perform exorcisms or otherwise fight the Devil, but no such dispensation has yet been received. Father Pierce is beginning to suspect that his agent within the Vatican is not reporting to the higher authorities but <b>to a secret society within its corridors instead</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>does</i> sound to imply workings of influenca from Shadow Congregation ( i.e. Malleus ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=948619#post948619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, he is a mage. If I was in the MM I'd want to keep them at arms length and in one spot where I can see them.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is also closeted homophobic gay, so I suspect hypocrisy he have enough in him to play with such.<br /> <br /> This leads to question about Father Pierce - <b>Should not he have Integrity instead of Wisdom as Banisher so centered on his worldview? Mage </b>2E let those on page 237. Maybe others memeber of St. Michael\u2019s Promise should also have Integrity instead of Wisdom?<br /> <br /> Also, I think that Father Pierce should have proper stats if he is Banisher - <b>What would you advice to give him, beside that he is Moros mage?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T11:04:50-07:00","id":948699,"title":"","content":"The Malleus Malificarum may be there, but as you can also see they're avoiding giving Father Pierce any special dispensation to go ahead with what he wants to do. You misunderstood Michael. He said the MM is avoiding giving Father Pierce too much access because -they- would be cautious about getting in too deep with a Mage. Father Pierce's hypocrisy is not a factor.<br /> <br /> You could make the Banishers with Integrity instead of Wisdom, and for them I probably would, but don't forget that some Mages with Wisdom choose to become Banishers. Those Mages don't replace their Wisdom with Integrity. The young Chinese American trio that have been getting pushed into being Banishers by St. Michael's Promise probably have Wisdom, they just don't know any better because the Banishers found them first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T13:06:35-07:00","id":948791,"title":"","content":"Rereading BU, Pierce is really the only one who has had anything like a twisted awakening. Hell, even Weapon seems to have a coherent idea what he's doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T13:39:13-07:00","id":948817,"title":"","content":"Coherent isn't really a good measure for whether they have Wisdom or Integrity though. I argue the kids have Wisdom because none of them are fully committed to the idea of eradicating Mages, which arguably means they don't feel revulsion to magic in general either in the way Banishers who retain Integrity do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T14:38:57-07:00","id":948860,"title":"","content":"I would have agreed but re-reading the Banishers section in 2e, it's actually pretty specific:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those whose Awakenings went wrong wield magic that they do not understand, lashing out with blind instinct at things that hurt them, rather than having a coherent reason to hate mages. </div> </div> </div>Weapon for example, does seem to have come to his own rather dubious conclusions based on his rather odd personal mythos/paradigm/whatever. He hates magic, but it doesn't seem to hurt him at all. (The reason I brought him up was that he's the one banisher in 2e). The five magi of St. Michael's Promise all seem pretty ok with themselves doing magic. Pierce is the one who has a real dread of magic.<br /> <br /> There is a bit of an issue with the group not being terribly well detailed. Only one of them has an explanation of why they're a Banisher and it's basically that being a Mastigos has made him both mysanthropic and increasingly paranoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T14:43:50-07:00","id":948867,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, it could just be one corrupting the rest and Father Pierce has gotten a lot further with Weapon and...can't remember the other guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T14:52:23-07:00","id":948873,"title":"","content":"I hadn't thought about that. There's the whole Banisher infection angle. Even if they started as only semi-banishers, I'm sure hanging out with him probably doesn't help.<br /> <br /> By the way I've confused things by bringing in Weapon, he's a lone Banisher unrelated to SMP. I just brought him up because he's kinda the archetypal Banisher and yet he doesn't really fit the twisted awakening model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:19:57-07:00","id":951527,"title":"","content":"I start to update other cabals from <b>Boston Unveiled</b> book. First goes <i>Shadow Chorus</i> and <i>Brotherhood </i><i>of the Ineffable Truth</i>, as they are needed for my now running plot. I have some thoughts on reworking <i>Chorus</i>:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>With all dress-up and \u2018you will not know our real identities\u2019, I think all members should be Guardians of Veil. Higher Wisdom is also not a problem as 2E point that High Wisdom are those of Awakened that are cautious with magic \u2013 that could be say all Guardians should be. Mysterium mages would also not being so secretive with their Order Protocols. Leaving <i>Culsu</i> and <i>Februs</i> as only Guardians in Boston would be too much hit to Eyes of Dragon also. So in my take <b>whole </b><i>Shadow Chorus</i> is from Guardians of Veil.</li> <li>Those members of Chorus that have Prime 1 or Life 1 will have those Arcana risen to 2nd dot in two years from <b>BU</b> presentation. They both help to conceal \u2018mundane\u2019 identities of Chorus, effectively making them Faceless faction from <b>Guardians</b> book.</li> </ol>Other things I should take in to consideration when making 2E update of NPCs from <i>Chorus</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T03:19:34-07:00","id":951580,"title":"","content":"On first NPC from <i>Shadow Chorus</i> I want to take Angerona as she is more helping from cabal. She is also Disciple of Life, so she can change her physical form with spells. In conversion she get a dot in Prime, to second one and one dot in Athletics as Defense is now higher in 2E and she seems to move a bit. I still need to hammer what of her 1E Rotes should be Praxis. Still not have idea on Legacy for her or Aspirations and Obsessions, as she is so enigmatic.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Angerona</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Quote: </b><i>What ails you? Speak truthfully, and perhaps I might recommend a balm for your pain.</i><br /> <b>Background: </b>Angerona\u2019s history is truly unknown. Even the ranking willworkers of the Consilium claim to have no knowledge whatsoever of her background. Her Shadow name is taken from a goddess of secrecy, a reliever of pain, a protector or any combination of the three. As to the name\u2019s<br /> significance, she will not say, only that it carries some clue as to her nature and her chosen task.<br /> <b>Description: </b>Angerona\u2019s mask is cut from what appears to be alabaster, and depicts the face of a serene, attractive woman with her mouth closed and bound. Her robes are midnight blue and billow out with the slightest movement.<br /> Her only exposed flesh is her hands, which are long-fingered and delicate. She speaks quietly, with a note of compassion, whether offering aid or promising terrible consequences for foolish actions.<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Of all of the members of the <i>Shadow Chorus</i>, Angerona is probably the most kind-hearted and benevolent. Like Culsu, she chooses her encounters carefully so as to give the impression of tremendous knowledge.<br /> Unlike Culsu, Angerona at least <i>appears </i>to offer her aid for unselfish ends. She is also the member of the Shadow Chorus likeliest to be seen alone, though always in some dark and out-of-the-way place.<br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools: </b>Alabaster mask<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Unknown<br /> <b>Path:</b> Acanthus<br /> <b>Order:</b> Guardians of Veil<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 4, Composure 4<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Computer 2, Investigation (Puzzles) 3, Medicine 4, Occult 4, Politics 2, Science 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Firearms 1, Larceny (Pickpocketing) 2, Stealth 4, Weaponry 1<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Empathy 3, Expression 2, Intimidation 2, Persuasion (Inspirational Speeches) 3, Socialize 2, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Hallow (Shared) 5, High Speech, Language (Latin), Advanced Library (Shared; The Abyss, Ghosts, Local Awakened History, Monsters and Thanatology), Occultation 2, Resources 4, Sanctum (Shared) 10, Status (Consilium 1, Order 2)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 7<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Balming (Charity)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Knowlagable (Pride)<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Help human in need, ???<br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> Identity?, ???<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 3<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Fate 4, Life 3, Prime 2, Time 2<br /> <b>Rotes:</b> Fate \u2014 Interconnections (\u2022), The Perfect Moment (\u2022\u2022), Lucky Coin (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Probable Cause (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022); Life \u2014 Sense Life (\u2022), Self-Purging (\u2022\u2022), Healing Heart (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Prime \u2014 Analyze Enchanted Artifact (\u2022); Time \u2014 Temporal Wrinkles (\u2022), Postcognition (\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Praxis:</b> ???<br /> <b>Mana/per Turn:</b> 12/3<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 4 ( Fate Armor )<br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> It appears as entangled threads, wrapped around her body and fading into invisibility perhaps two feet or so from her.<br /> <b>Tilt: </b> Everything is wrapped by threads - All characters get -2 to Perception rolls.<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> ??? \u2014???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T03:49:18-07:00","id":951584,"title":"","content":"To work out their aspirations you might want to work out who they actually are and what they're up to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T04:54:15-07:00","id":951606,"title":"","content":"Having some extra time, I done first draft of Culsu conversion. Reading her write-up I come to idea how to make her so driven to losing her own identity, secure her own, but also a bit tragic character. In my take Culsu is transsexual women locked into male body that needs to play all the time game of pretending \u2013 it become so much her second nature, that she became Guardian and now even is Epopt of Order. Still, her Awakened and \u2018Sleeper\u2019 responsibilities makes her impossible to study Life Arcanum enough to be what she want to be. From obvious reasons I think about her joining Dakasha Legacy, if she would find proper tutor. As always, Praxis are waiting for me to be in mood to look for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Culsu ( Epopt )</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Quote: </b><i>Most speak, a very few listen, and the barest fraction </i>understands <i>. . .</i><br /> <b>Background: </b>As is the case with all of the members of the Shadow Chorus, nothing is known of the true identity of Culsu, named for an Etruscan demoness, the guardian of the gates to the underworld. One rumor is that this shadowy figure is a wealthy and influential heiress, numbered among Boston\u2019s elite, but no one has been able to concretely track that rumor back to any person.<br /> <b>Description: </b>Culsu wears a grotesque theatrical mask in all Awakened dealings. She (for Culsu at least <i>seems</i>, by voice, mannerisms and build, to be female) has chosen for her image that of a hideous, snarling, fanged hag, the mask seemingly cut from gleaming black stone or metal. Her black robes are voluminous and billowing, her hood deep and shadowed and the black gloves on her hands are of formfitting leather. For those rare few who have caught a glimpse within the cowl, Culsu\u2019s eyes seem to be either green or blue \u2014 though one or two mages claim that they are red. Her voice is soft and quiet, and her words are usually both cryptic and carefully chosen.<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Culsu projects an image of omniscience. By choosing the times and circumstances of as many of her interactions as possible, she is able to seem virtually all knowing. Her advice and clues are obviously part of some larger scheme, but, thus far none \u2014 not even the wisest and most powerful mages of the Consilium \u2014 have been able to figure out what it is for certain. Whatever Culsu offers has a price, but never the obvious one. Often such a cost is paid not by the one who accepts her aid, but instead by his or her friends, allies and associates, whether they know it or not.<br /> <b><i>Secret:</i></b> Culsu <i>is</i>, in reality, male heir to one of powerful families of Boston elite that needs to sustain his family line. He still dreams to be female, but knows that without his male sex and good marriage his line will die out after his generation as he is single child. In last two years he started study of Life Arcanum from his cabal mates, but Culsu\u2019s responsibilities as Order\u2019s Epopt and Sleeper persona of power leaves very little time to went deep in it and achieving Disciple in Life needed for instant changes of her/his body.<br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools: </b>Mask<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Unknown<br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros<br /> <b>Order:</b> Guardians of the Veil<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 4, Composure 5<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Research) 3, Investigation (Puzzles) 5, Medicine 2, Occult 4, Politics 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Larceny 3, Stealth (Shadowing) 4, Weaponry (Knives) 2<br /> <b>Social Skills</b>: Empathy (Emotions) 3, Intimidation 3, Persuasion 2, Socialize (Awakened Gatherings) 3, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge (Lying) 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Dream 3, Eidetic Memory, Hallow (Shared) 5, High Speech, Language (Latin), Advanced Library (Shared; The Abyss, Ghosts, Local Awakened History, Monsters and Thanatology), Meditative Mind, Occultation 3, Quick Draw (Weaponry), Resources 4, Sanctum (Shared) 10, Status (Consilium 3, Order 4)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 6<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Idealistic (Hope)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Realistic (Envy)<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Perfect Awakened society of Boston, Sustain family line, Becoming woman<br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> Identity, Life Arcanum<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9<br /> <b>Health</b>: 7<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 4<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Death 4, Fate 3, Life 2, Matter 2, Mind 3<br /> <b>Rotes:</b> Death \u2014 Shadow Sculpting (\u2022), Suppress Aura (\u2022\u2022), Ghost Gate (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Revenant (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022); Fate \u2014 Interconnections (\u2022), The Evil Eye (\u2022\u2022), Superlative Luck (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Matter \u2014 Dark Matter (\u2022); Mind \u2014 Aura Perception (\u2022), Memory Hole (\u2022\u2022), Augment the Mind (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Praxis:</b> ???<br /> <b>Mana/per Turn:</b> 13/4<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 4 ( Death Armor )<br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> Crawling shadows that move against the light, creating ominous shapes on the walls, floor and ceiling..<br /> <b>Tilt: </b> Shadows are unnerving - All characters get -2 to resist Intimidation rolls.<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> None ( will become Dakasha if had a chance. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-28-2016, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T05:16:33-07:00","id":951611,"title":"","content":"Well, there are Daksha in the Guardians so it shouldn't be that difficult to find a mentor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T05:34:04-07:00","id":951622,"title":"","content":"Using extra time I making rest of Shadow Chorus. Februs is a bit straight forward in conversion - only needed to risen Mind and Life in his write-up. Gave him Athelics 2 as he is probably most 'physical' member of Chorus. He always try's to push people limits with his taunting. I added rumor on that Consilium is affraid of him as he sounds so much unstable individual. It could also interesting dynamic with Ruling Council itself - to giving sentences to that kind of men.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Februs ( Interfector )</b></span><br /> <b>Quote: </b><i>One way or the other, you will be cleansed. Tell me, are you afraid to die?</i><br /> <b>Background: </b>Februs is the most overtly sinister member of the Shadow Chorus. He seems to delight in making others uncomfortable \u2014 fitting for a man who has taken his name from a god of death and purification (later known as the patron deity of malaria). It is clear that most of the leaders of the Consilium do not much care for this man \u2013 but they also not restraining him. There are rumors that Ruling Council is a bit afraid of him.<br /> <b>Description: </b>Februs appears to be of average height and build. His mask is of a frowning old man, fashioned out of what seems to be cracked and pitted, mottled-gray stone. His elaborate, many-layered robes are of an extremely dark brown. His hands are covered with black leather gloves, and his feet with black leather boots of an antiquated style. His voice is a menacing rasp, sounding almost as though it is being whispered directly into the ear of the listener.<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>More so than any other member of his cabal, Februs goes out of his way to disturb people. His aid is always very obviously a double-edged sword, and he seems to take no end of joy in forcing others into situations in which they must choose between evils. While he rarely appears to others outside of the presence of the rest of the Shadow Chorus, Februs is known to send his words to others with magic, occasionally even into the hearts of their very sanctums.<br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools: </b>Mask<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Unknown<br /> <b>Path:</b> Mastigos<br /> <b>Order:</b> Guardians of the Veil<br /> <b>Mental </b>Attributes: Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 5, Composure 4<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Crafts 2, Investigation 4, Occult (Conspiracies) 4, Politics 3, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Larceny 3, Stealth (Shadows) 4, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy (Motivations) 3, Intimidation (Veiled Threats) 4, Persuasion 2, Socialize 1, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Dream 2, Eidetic Memory, Hallow (Shared) 5, High Speech, Language (Ancient Greek, Latin), Advanced Library (Shared; The Abyss, Ghosts, Local Awakened History, Monsters and Thanatology), Occultation 3, Resources 4, Sanctum (Shared) 10, Status (Consilium 1, Order 1), Toxin Resistance<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 5<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Restraining ( Temperance )<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Galling ( Wrath )<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Fulfill sentences of Consilium, Cleansing corruption, Irritate people<br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> People Limits, Mind Arcanum<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9<br /> <b>Health</b>: 7<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 4<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Death 4, Fate 3, Life 2, Matter 1, Mind 4<br /> <b>Rotes:</b> Death \u2014 Shadow Sculpting (\u2022), Suppress Aura (\u2022\u2022), Ghost Gate (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Revenant (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022); Fate \u2014 Interconnections (\u2022), The Evil Eye (\u2022\u2022), Superlative Luck (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Matter \u2014 Dark Matter (\u2022); Mind \u2014 Aura Perception (\u2022), Memory Hole (\u2022\u2022), Augment the Mind (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Praxis:</b> ???<br /> <b>Mana/per Turn:</b> 13/4<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 4 ( Death Armor )<br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> Cloud of large, reddish-black flies that issues from within his robes and clusters, soundlessly, in the air..<br /> <b>Tilt: </b> Flies covers everything - All characters get -2 to Perception rolls.<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> ???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-16-2016, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:02:56-07:00","id":951631,"title":"","content":"Last member of Chorus I made Cultor that takes few free Mystery Cults others cannot run. Discordia's nature seems to me work perfectly with this role in Guardians, especially as she loves to tempt people. Also, I changed her Magical Tool as with change of Order from 1E write-up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Discordia ( Cultor )</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Quote: </b><i>I know what you want, and it is within my power to offer it to you.</i><br /> <b>Background: </b>Discordia , named for the Roman incarnation of Eris, is almost never seen without another member of the Chorus. She plays the part of the devil on one\u2019s shoulder, offering gifts that must eventually culminate in strife. She is encouraged in this by Februs, while Culsu and Angerona work to curb her tendencies. Because Discordia exists in the shadow of other members of the Chorus, so to speak, she is a genuine cipher, virtually without an individual identity of her own, save as a purveyor of chaos-inducing temptations. Her duties in Order is to watch over few Mystery Cults from Labyrinth that other members do not on daily basis \u2013 and she loves to fool Sleepers in them.<br /> <b>Description: </b>Discordia\u2019s mask looks to be wrought of white gold, and depicts a beautiful woman, most often with eyes half-closed and full, lush lips curved upward into a mischievous smile. The mask is occasionally known to at least appear to change expression, sometimes within a single conversation. Her robes are of the darkest red, and she wears boots and gloves of the same shade. Her voice is deep and husky, with a note of malicious playfulness about it.<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Based upon her actions, it seems that Discordia wants to see the Consilium collapse into turmoil. She is kept in check by Culsu and Angerona, but sometimes manages to let some secret slip out that could potentially threaten the balance of power. Of course, just to keep people guessing, she is known to offer the rare bit of harmless information, no strings attached.<br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools: </b>Mask, ruby pendant (Prime magic)<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Unknown<br /> <b>Path:</b> Obrimos<br /> <b>Order:</b> Guardians of the Veil<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 2<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Computer 2, Crafts 1, Investigation 3, Occult 3, Politics (Scandals) 3, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 1, Larceny (Sleight of Hand) 2, Stealth 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy (Motives) 3, Expression 2, Persuasion 3, Socialize 2, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Hallow (Shared) 5, High Speech, Language (Latin) 1, Advanced Library (Shared; The Abyss, Ghosts, Local Awakened History, Monsters and Thanatology) 2, Occultation 2, Resources 4, Sanctum (Shared) 10, Status (Consilium 1, Order 1)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 6<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Patient ( Fortitude )<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Playful ( Gluttony )<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Tempting people, Watching over Labyrinth<br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> Life \u2018Roles\u2019, Matter Arcanum<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 2<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Forces 2, Matter 3, Prime 4<br /> <b>Rotes:</b> Forces \u2014 Read Matrices (\u2022), Control Sound (\u2022\u2022); Matter \u2014 Dark Matter (\u2022), Transmute Water (\u2022\u2022), Plasticity (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Prime \u2014 Discern Phantasm (\u2022), Activate Enchanted Item (\u2022\u2022), Controlled Dispellation (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Marionette (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Mana/per Turn: </b>11/2<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 3 ( Matter Armor)<br /> <b>Magic Shield:</b> 4 ( Prime Armor)<br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> Brilliant, silver-white flame that limns her form, curling lazily in the air, with leaping sparks that spin off into the air and dissipate.<br /> <b>Tilt: </b> Light and electricity is filling the air - All characters get 8 Again and +2 to Expression rolls.<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> ???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:17:58-07:00","id":951639,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if St. Michael\u2019s Promise members need update beside stating Father Pierce? They are very light in Mage mechanics from the start, rising their Arcana probably does not make sense and they do not need assertion of Order role and mechanics in them. What do you think? They are Nameless and Nameless are very sparse in crunch of write-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:28:40-07:00","id":951649,"title":"","content":"Maximum Sanctum value, shared of not, is 5+3, where 3 is specifically for making it a Demesne. I think Multilingual is better fit for Latin than Language, and for &quot;ancient languages&quot; in general, but it's a personal prerference. I like the words you picked for their Virtues and Vices. <br /> Some of their Rotes don't gain much from being Rotes. <br /> They all have lost some Wisdom - you could think about picking some Inured Spells for them. <br /> I'm suprised that no single one of them has even a dot of Shadow Name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:56:50-07:00","id":951673,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>, I will look over to fix Shadow Chorus in those ways you are pointing characters. But now we start Brotherhood...<br /> <br /> First write-up of Brotherhood from the oldest member of it. Potestas sounded to me like perfect material for the Hierophant of Mysterium, so he is one. I made him also most concerned with Khumeia rise to power, as he was planning to force next Mysterium member on Consilium. Still, he well can be a misogynist. Of course I added to him Egregore 5 Merit, but still have problem in mystical parts of character \u2013 his Obsessions or possible Legacy eludes me.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Potestas ( Consilium Councilor, Hierophant )</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Quote: </b><i>Do you think yourself wise, young one? Important? Powerful? You are </i>none <i>of these things. </i><i>You are a whelp with</i><i> delusions of grandeur. Allow me to illustrate to you your insufficiencies..</i><br /> <b>Background: </b>Potestas has been at the Academy for as long as anyone can remember. He is seen as akin to the sea, both tempestuous and eternal. Despite his obvious desires to the contrary, he has never and, at this point, will never hold the office of the Hierarch, though he has been a Councilor through the reign of the Nemean. It is a position Potestas has held since early in the ascension of the Nemean and from which the Nemean could not dislodge him, despite the other\u2019s efforts. Potestas is the loyal opposition, devoted to the Consilium, even as he stands against the power of the Ebon Noose and the White Putnams after Nemean \u2018disappearance\u2019. He was the one most strongly opposed to Khuemia rise on position of Councilor, saying even that it\u2019s \u2018grow men\u2019s club\u2019.<br /> As Mysterium\u2019s Hierophant, Potestas has a lot of ties among Boston\u2019s Awakened, more than anyone else cares to admit. Some believe that he has at least one spy in all but one or two of the other cabals of the area, though this is almost certainly an exaggeration. He is a master of misdirection, keeping enemies at one another\u2019s throats and leaving allies guessing as to his true capabilities and motivations.<br /> <b>Description: </b>Potestas is a tall, lean man with an intimidating presence. Now in his mid-80s, he looks as though he keeps standing solely on account of his unwillingness to yield to age or weakness. His beard and receding white hair are worn short, and his face is a network of wrinkles, deepening to shadowed grooves when he frowns in displeasure, which is often. He invariably wears fine suits, often in black, dark gray or dark blue, and uses a small, glittering black gemstone of unknown composition (he claims it is Atlantean) as a tie tack. His grammar is impeccable, though he always sounds a little hoarse. His instinct is to talk down to others, and he holds it in check with great difficulty (and then only when he truly wishes to).<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Potestas believes that wisdom conveys the right to power, not the other way around. He is tremendously disappointed with the fact that he was never able to successfully break with the Mysterium\u2019s unspoken policy of remaining a second-tier power in Boston, but pretends to be far more bothered by it than he actually is. In his eyes, only a fool laments that which has already come to pass, unless he somehow possesses the power to change it. Instead, Potestas works on establishing a firm position for the next generation of the Academy, from which they might chip away at the influence of the area\u2019s Silver Ladder in general and the Secret Concord in particular. He is connected to many willworkers in the city by the Egregore he is center, but has nowhere near the information network he has led others to believe. In truth, he finds great amusement in watching others scramble to figure out who his spies and informants are.<br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools: </b>Watch with mirrored case<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Carlo Fendi<br /> <b>Path:</b> Obrimos<br /> <b>Order:</b> Mysterium<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 6, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical</b> <b>Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 5<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 6, Investigation 4, Occult (Secret Societies, Egregore) 5, Politics 5, Science 4<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Brawl 2, Drive 1, Firearms 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 2, Survival 4, Weaponry (Swords) 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Expression 3, Intimidation 4, Persuasion 4, Socialize (Awakened Society) 2, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 5<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Advanced Library (Shared; Ancient Ruins, the Awakened in Politics, Cryptozoology, Goetia and Numerology), Contacts (Academia, Occult Community) 2, Eidetic Memory, Egregore 5, Hallow (Personal) 2, Hallow (Shared) 5, High Speech, Language (Ancient Greek, French, German,<br /> Hebrew, Latin, Mandarin, Russian, Spanish, Turkish), Resources 5, Sanctum (Personal) 5, Sanctum (Shared) 7, Sleepwalker Retainer 4, Status (Consilium 5, Order 5)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 6<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Dedicated (Fortitude)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Ego (Pride)<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Make Mysterium rulers of Boston, Prepare Academy for passing, Train new Hierophant<br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> ???<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 6<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Fate 2, Forces 4, Life 3, Matter 1, Mind 3, Prime 5, Space 2<br /> <b>Rotes:</b> Fate \u2014 Quantum Flux (\u2022), Shifting the Odds (\u2022\u2022); Forces \u2014 Control Sound (\u2022), Kinetic Blow (\u2022\u2022), Personal Invisibility (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Control Velocity (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022); Life \u2014 Sense Life (\u2022), Self-Healing (\u2022\u2022), Honing the Form (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Matter \u2014 Dark Matter (\u2022); Mind \u2014 One Mind, Two Thoughts (\u2022), Mental Shield (\u2022\u2022), Augment the Mind (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Prime \u2014 Dispel Magic (\u2022), Magic Shield (\u2022\u2022), Celestial Fire (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Supernal Dispellation (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), Siphon Mana (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022); Space \u2014 Correspondence (\u2022), Conceal Sympathy (\u2022\u2022), Scrying (\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Praxis: ???</b><br /> <b>Mana/per Turn:</b> 15/6<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 4 ( Forces Armor )<br /> <b>Magic Shield:</b> 5 (Prime Armor )<br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> Roiling tempest of seething energy, draped over his body like a kingly cloak and blazing brilliantly around his head like a crown.<br /> <b>Tilt: </b> Light is blinding - All characters get -2 to Perception rolls.<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> ???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-16-2016, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T07:25:12-07:00","id":951689,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't he want Khumeia on the consilium? If you want to destroy the Secret Concord, then offering the White Putnam ladder members a viable alternative to working with the Noose is a good way to do that. Plus, more broadly Khumeia's agenda is to bring the consilium back to Boston, which is really a necessary prelude to the Mysterium taking over.<br /> <br /> There's sexism and then there's actively undermining your own plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T09:10:22-07:00","id":951763,"title":"","content":"Yeah, thought about it on road to home - it does have sense that Potestas would be in favor of Khumeia. Question is who would be most against her in Ruling Council then? Chain Parris and Anacaona de Xaragua? But Chain would then risen on the same voting to his new position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:33:01-07:00","id":952350,"title":"","content":"When thinking about <i>Shadow Chorus </i>and reading Faceless section in <b>Guardians of Veil</b> book, I come to idea that maybe (Legion) sickness-heresy infestation in cabal could be interesting. Probably without taking proper Legacy, but some members could be much than interested in idea of losing self. Picking one, I probably think about <i>Discordia</i>, as she is most dedicated to 'play the role' and written with 'does not have character on herself'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T01:11:17-07:00","id":952382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=951763#post951763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, thought about it on road to home - it does have sense that Potestas would be in favor of Khumeia. Question is who would be most against her in Ruling Council then? Chain Parris and Anacaona de Xaragua? But Chain would then risen on the same voting to his new position.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Potestas doesn't need to be permanently on her side. There's advantage in getting her on the council, however once she's there, he's not exactly going to be happy with her jumping to Hierarch. The Mysterium hold the majority of seats on the consilium now. He probably expects to be made Hierarch in return for letting her get the councillors seat.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Khumeia has basically handed the consilium over to the Mysterium in return for her own advancement. She's not going to be a very popular deacon.<br /> <br /> One other thing occurred to me. In the intro fiction to Silver Ladder, the Nemean's younger self states that the Gryphon Knights were involved with the trial; that could indicate that Potestas was involved with Khumeia's plot. The Knights follow his orders afterall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:12:57-07:00","id":953264,"title":"","content":"Idea I got on yesterdays session - For Shadow Chorus to operate as true Faceless cabal, they need to assume other identikits. They need to <i>look</i> as other, normal people. So they Masks and Robes are some imbued items with Matter and Life spells to change shapes in to normal, Sleeper persons and their cloths on thought alone, probably made by Angerona with Culsu help. They just think ( or spend Mana ) and they change from latino sexy women, to stable businessman to old women, in almost blink of the eye. And when they are not changing it, they return to 'robes and masks' look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:15:32-07:00","id":953303,"title":"","content":"Or they could just invest heavily in Masques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:24:10-07:00","id":953312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=953303#post953303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they could just invest heavily in Masques.</div> </div> </div> </div>Masques do not change you <i>physically</i>, only your mental persona. It's 'I look as someone totally different' problem. Besides, <b>Guardians</b> Order book points heavy use of Life magic for shapechanging in Suspector section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:31:53-07:00","id":953319,"title":"","content":"Are you aware how much body language, posture, walking gait, vocal inflections and the like can change a person or can be used to identify someone? A Guardian who relies entirely on Life magic to make himself look different but doesn't take care to -act- different could still be spotted. Conversely, people who know how they normally behave and can change those behaviors and patterns up can fool people who know them into believing they don't at least at first glance. So, yeah, imbue a bunch of items with Life, or just use the Guardians' special merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:55:46-07:00","id":953334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=953319#post953319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, yeah, imbue a bunch of items with Life, or just use the Guardians' special merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or use <i>both</i> to get best results. That always was a plan.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:58:36-07:00","id":953642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=953319#post953319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you aware how much body language, posture, walking gait, vocal inflections and the like can change a person or can be used to identify someone?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Green Lantern:</b> Clark hides behind a pair of glasses and you're worrying about me?<br /> <b>Flash:</b> Clark slouches, wears clothes two sizes too big, and raises his voice an octave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T08:31:52-07:00","id":958244,"title":"","content":"Adding <i>Dead Wrens</i> cabal to game - but have problem translating them in to Polish. Wrens are very niche birds in Polish ( known as 'Strzy\u017cyki' ). They are part of Passerine family, that in Polish is also name for Sparrow ( i.e. 'Wr\u00f3bel' ). So more popular name of cabal could be <i>Dead Sparrows</i>. In first session with them I used translation for <i>Dead Crows</i>, as I did not know that Wrens aren't Crows. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To what translation I should stick now? Direct translation of Wren sound too weird for this cabal name in Polish.<br /> <br /> Other topic - <b>I see that <i>Dead Wrens</i> are multiOrder cabal on BU, but most characters are much better serving as Libertines.</b> Like <i>Rabid Anne</i> is literary practicing Techne on her Shadow Name persona, wanting to become embodiment of fantastical pirate. <i>Sunjata</i> write-up is never near sounding anything as true Silver Ladder. <i>Menelaus</i> looks like any character I could leave with his original Mysterium, but only on basis of his 'multiple adventures' before and old age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-27-2016, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T02:20:12-07:00","id":958653,"title":"","content":"Other problem - In coming plot I would use Consilium's Heralds extensively - But when reading <b>Boston Unveiled</b>, I see only one is <i>Arathnos</i> from <i>Ebony Noose</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay, I can run with PCs in rank of temporary 'heralds', but should not Consilium have stable ones? On the other hand, I wanted to play with Boston setting as understaffed, so only one Herald, and from Salem proper, could work with that theme. Still, this clash with number of Sentinels coming from <i>Ebony Noose</i> alone.<br /> <br /> if you got idea who from Pentacle NPC could work good as Herald, point me there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T08:52:01-07:00","id":958759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=958653#post958653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But when reading <b>Boston Unveiled</b>, I see only one is <i>Arathnos</i> from <i>Ebony Noose</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Okay, I can run with PCs in rank of temporary 'heralds', but should not Consilium have stable ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication of Arathnos' write-up is that the Nemean basically doesn't use the Heralds. He doesn't care about making friends with cabals or gauging their opinions or whatever, if he wants something he sends the Sentinels.<br /> <br /> If the Nemean has fallen then presumably the new administration would start appointing heralds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if you got idea who from Pentacle NPC could work good as Herald, point me there. </div> </div> </div>The non-sentinel members of the Gryphon knights seem a descent option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T02:28:17-07:00","id":969779,"title":"","content":"Where is official write-up of Khonsu Censor from Boston? I have player that want to become one so good would be to introduce setting one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:04:01-07:00","id":969912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=969779#post969779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is official write-up of Khonsu Censor from Boston? I have player that want to become one so good would be to introduce setting one.</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't one. Khonsu first appeared in the fiction of the Mysterium supplement, much later than the publication of Boston Unveiled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:24:21-07:00","id":969979,"title":"","content":"Yup unless it is on the 1st ed core there isnt stats for khonsu......thought khonsu-thout its one of the names of the blasphemous scribe just a coincidence i am sure...*wink* *wink*<br /> <br /> As for the stats for a censor i would use the stats for numa, for a bureocratic kind of censor or protestas for a hands on approach kind of censor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:02:56-07:00","id":970008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=969979#post969979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the stats for a censor i would use the stats for numa, for a bureocratic kind of censor or protestas for a hands on approach kind of censor.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Censor is a Status 1 job. Those two guys are both masters, sit on the consilium and are Hierophants of their Order in addition to having long careers as Awakened. I mean, it's possible, but using their stats seems kinda out of line with how he's presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:18:58-07:00","id":970014,"title":"","content":"In Censorious Khonsu says that he's a First Adept (I'd guess Forces, that seems to be his go-to arcana) and he's from Milwaukee Consilium not Boston.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:28:23-07:00","id":970066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=970008#post970008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Censor is a Status 1 job. Those two guys are both masters, sit on the consilium and are Hierophants of their Order in addition to having long careers as Awakened. I mean, it's possible, but using their stats seems kinda out of line with how he's presented.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> my bad, i was thinking of curator. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:06:20-07:00","id":970465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=970014#post970014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Censorious Khonsu says that he's a First Adept (I'd guess Forces, that seems to be his go-to arcana) and he's from Milwaukee Consilium not Boston.</div> </div> </div> </div>So he just by accident mixed with all Red Word problem in Chicago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:17:50-07:00","id":970471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=970066#post970066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> my bad, i was thinking of curator. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Local Curator is Aurem, Potestas once student. Numa is theoretically competing Mysterium member, but libraries of Laurel sounds a lot less like proper Atheneum, more as cabal private collection.<br /> <br /> From my gameplay solutions - I made Academy as private school - enough to make it elitist and locked in one tenement house, not too big to make it into Xaviers School in NY manor. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:19:44-07:00","id":970473,"title":"","content":"Someone had done a 1700s Boston consilium at one point. It may have been Chris, the Werewolf freelancer? Let me try and find it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T23:28:53-07:00","id":970526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=970465#post970465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So he just by accident mixed with all Red Word problem in Chicago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The author that his cabal are obsessed with accidently wrote a part of the Blasphemous Scribe. That caused the Red Word cult to come after him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:53:29-07:00","id":970558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=970465#post970465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So he just by accident mixed with all Red Word problem in Chicago?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're asking if the writers made a mistake, no, the Mysterium are the most travelled Order and so it's not really surprising he has adventures in Chicago and Boston.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T00:35:32-07:00","id":996484,"title":"","content":"So, reading more on Egregore ( called Atlantean Mystery in 1E <b>Mysterium</b> Order book ) I see that Potestats need at least some changes in Arcana department - as Hierophant should have Time ( and other high-ranking Mysterium do not have those ) to point others what their Mysteries could be to dwell in to, so I added Time 2. I\u2019m still not sure on this, as 2E \u2018Divination\u2019 spell has different wording, but from look on it, with Reach option in it those should work for Egregore in Order. I left him Fate 2 as Potestas sounds he may need Accelerated Advancements in Egregore on his students, even just hos to show them what they can achieve if they overcome obstacles. Then I added him Obsessions based on Mysterium book \u2013 in my eyes, Potestas is dedicated in finding partner for his last dot of Egregore. In meanwhile, he research magic and spells as general, because he is preparing for the last Egregore ritual. Also, I think more about tone of character and how it is played in my game. So here is rewrite of NPC - point me where it could be developed more.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Potestas ( Consilium Councilor, Hierophant )</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Quote: </b><i>Do you think yourself wise, young one? Important? Powerful? You are </i>none <i>of these things. You are a whelp with delusions of grandeur. Allow me to illustrate to you your insufficiencies..</i><br /> <b>Background: </b>Potestas has been at the Academy for as long as anyone can remember. He is seen as akin to the sea, both tempestuous and eternal. Despite his obvious desires to the contrary, he has never and, at this point, will never hold the office of the Hierarch, though he has been a Councilor through the reign of the Nemean. It is a position Potestas has held since early in the ascension of the Nemean and from which the Nemean could not dislodge him, despite the other\u2019s efforts. Potestas is the loyal opposition, devoted to the Consilium, even as he stands against the power of the Ebon Noose and the White Putnams after Nemean \u2018disappearance\u2019. He was the one most strongly in favor to Khuemia rise on position of Councilor, showing her as great opening for new Silver Ladder. In the end, on his private thoughts, he still thinks Consilium is \u2018grow men\u2019s club\u2019 and wanting to be proclaimed Hierarch.<br /> As Mysterium\u2019s Hierophant, Potestas has a lot of ties among Boston\u2019s Awakened, more than anyone else cares to admit. Some believe that he has at least one spy in all but one or two of the other cabals of the area, though this is almost certainly an exaggeration. He is a master of misdirection, keeping enemies at one another\u2019s throats and leaving allies guessing as to his true capabilities and motivations.<br /> <b>Description: </b>Potestas is a tall, lean man with an intimidating presence. Now in his mid-80s, he looks as though he keeps standing solely on account of his unwillingness to yield to age or weakness. His beard and receding white hair are worn short, and his face is a network of wrinkles, deepening to shadowed grooves when he frowns in displeasure, which is often. He invariably wears fine suits, often in black, dark gray or dark blue, and uses a small, glittering black gemstone of unknown composition (he claims it is Atlantean) as a tie tack. His grammar is impeccable, though he always sounds a little hoarse. His instinct is to talk down to others, and he holds it in check with great difficulty (and then only when he truly wishes to).<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Potestas believes that wisdom conveys the right to power, not the other way around. He is tremendously disappointed with the fact that he was never able to successfully break with the Mysterium\u2019s unspoken policy of remaining a second-tier power in Boston, but pretends to be far more bothered by it than he actually is. In his eyes, only a fool laments that which has already come to pass, unless he somehow possesses the power to change it. Instead, Potestas works on establishing a firm position for the next generation of the Academy, from which they might chip away at the influence of the area\u2019s Silver Ladder in general and the Secret Concord in particular. He is connected to many willworkers in the city by the Egregore he is center, but has nowhere near the information network he has led others to believe. In truth, he finds great amusement in watching others scramble to figure out who his spies and informants are.<br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools: </b>Watch with mirrored case<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Carlo Fendi<br /> <b>Path:</b> Obrimos<br /> <b>Order:</b> Mysterium<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 6, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical</b> <b>Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 5<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 6, Investigation 4, Occult (Secret Societies, Egregore) 5, Politics 5, Science 4<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Brawl 2, Drive 1, Firearms 1, Larceny 1, Stealth 2, Survival 4, Weaponry (Swords) 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Expression 3, Intimidation 4, Persuasion 4, Socialize (Awakened Society) 2, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 5<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Advanced Library (Shared; Ancient Ruins, the Awakened in Politics, Cryptozoology, Goetia and Numerology), Contacts (Academia, Occult Community) 2, Eidetic Memory, Egregore 4, Hallow (Personal) 2, Hallow (Shared) 5, High Speech, Language (Ancient Greek, French, German,<br /> Hebrew, Latin, Mandarin, Russian, Spanish, Turkish), Resources 5, Sanctum (Personal) 5, Sanctum (Shared) 7, Sleepwalker Retainer 4, Status (Consilium 5, Order 5)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 6<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Dedicated (Fortitude)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Ego (Pride)<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Become Hierarch, Prepare Academy for passing, Train new Hierophant<br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> Pass Mysteriorum Focus ( needs other Hierophant ), Thaumatology<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 6<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Fate 2, Forces 4, Life 3, Matter 1, Mind 3, Prime 5, Space 2, Time 2<br /> <b>Rotes:</b> Fate \u2014 Quantum Flux (\u2022), Shifting the Odds (\u2022\u2022); Forces \u2014 Control Sound (\u2022), Kinetic Blow (\u2022\u2022), Personal Invisibility (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Control Velocity (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022); Life \u2014 Sense Life (\u2022), Self-Healing (\u2022\u2022), Honing the Form (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Matter \u2014 Dark Matter (\u2022); Mind \u2014 One Mind, Two Thoughts (\u2022), Mental Shield (\u2022\u2022), Augment the Mind (\u2022\u2022\u2022); Prime \u2014 Dispel Magic (\u2022), Magic Shield (\u2022\u2022), Celestial Fire (\u2022\u2022\u2022), Supernal Dispellation (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), Siphon Mana (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022); Space \u2014 Correspondence (\u2022), Conceal Sympathy (\u2022\u2022), Scrying (\u2022\u2022); Time \u2013 Divination (\u2022)<br /> <b>Praxis: ???</b><br /> <b>Mana/per Turn:</b> 15/6<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 4 ( Forces Armor )<br /> <b>Magic Shield:</b> 5 (Prime Armor )<br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> Roiling tempest of seething energy, draped over his body like a kingly cloak and blazing<br /> brilliantly around his head like a crown.<br /> <b>Tilt: </b> Light is blinding - All characters get -2 to Perception rolls.<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> ???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:01:32-07:00","id":997214,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit late to the party - and worse, I haven\u2019t read the entire thread as in depth as I would. This abrogation of forum etiquette must arise of arrogance, for which I shall have to chastise myself at a later point (ie: when time permits). Further exacerbating my sin, circumstances afford me only enough time to present my initial whims as a sketch of an outline. <br /> <br /> <b>Consilium</b>: Not sure what the mystery of the Consilium would be. Maybe something about the concentration of places of worship, higher learning and Stephen King is a huge Red Sox fan? But, I agree with having cabals spread out across New England. Instead of a consilium, maybe make the post-Epona's Chariot Ebon Noose formation a tight-knit thearch+arrow caucus and/or experiment?<br /> <br /> Also, if I skimmed correctly, the chronicle's primary mystical motif and metaphor is alchemy. To me, this implies themes of change and the direction of enacting those changes; Tao vs. Western Alchemy; greed vs. inner growth; materialism vs. ephemeral/spiritual.<br /> <br /> Thus, for <b>Seers</b>, I imagine Mammon and/or Patrenoster would be fitting. (Maybe the decline of the Catholic church in the area plays into this. See: Pedo priests &amp; Cardinal Law.) (Also, Harvard has generated a <i>lot</i> of federal-level economic advisors.) (Also, this could tie into Khumeia\u2019s backstory somewhat.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>NPCs perhaps interested in the 'philosopher's stone'/directly reflecting alchemy:</b><ul><li>Have Potestas be undergoing the Final Key.<ul><li>Maybe this ties into your central chronicle. But awakened might consider this to be the ultimate inner-transformation.</li> <li>Either way, he\u2019s pulling away from \u201cEarthly concerns\u201d and Aurem is essentially Councilor, etc.</li> </ul></li> <li>Khumeia is \u201cstalling\u201d (stagnation) (Could also be applied to Apollonia, more readily, but I\u2019ll admit to not quite being sure what to do with her.)</li> <li>Tiamat &amp; the Alchemy of Life (and Shadowname)</li> <li>Vision could be an interesting \u2018pentacle-side\u2019 option for the materialism aspect of alchemy; but could also be interesting if he has some sort of \u2018mid-life crisis\u2019 and is trying to change himself and evolve into a mystagogue seriously.</li> </ul><b>Cabals</b><ul><li>The Shadow Chorus:<ul><li>Rumors that they are there because of the past and the Emerald Scroll. Personally, I think they are (primarily) Massachusetts natives who the nation-wide GoV (playing \u201cthe inter/national\u201d game) has assigned the task of re-taking Harvard from the Seers.<ul><li>Everything else is (probably) smokescreen.</li> <li>Being antagonistic to the FC will only make them more paranoid and wary of dangers?</li> </ul></li> <li>Theme-wise:<ul><li>Masks are transformative -&gt; They allow a person to assume (if only while donned) another guise/skin/etc.</li> <li>The Shadow Chorus as written (imo) are meant to be agents for <i>some</i> sort of change.</li> <li>Alternatively, if you go with the war vs. Seers option, maybe emphasize or contrast with the underlying themes of their nemeses.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Ebon Noose<ul><li>With the Hierarch gone, they\u2019ve lost a lot of knowledge and really are back to being the Fool. Will the cabal evolve and shed its Thearch past for something more Arrow-like?</li> <li>Has the Moros gone insane? What about Rubida/Tiamat\u2019s \u201cprotection\u201d from the Brotherhood?</li> </ul></li> <li>Putnams have change built right into their premise. A weak Noose likely means Simon &amp; Moriah go on \u201cthe offensive.\u201d (They want to change their cabal as a whole.)</li> <li>Numa/Sanguine Laurel could be used for \u201cchange\u201d plot points in terms of human growth. (Pregnancy/Birth, children, puberty/adolescence, divorce, empty nest syndrome.)</li> </ul>Anyway, maybe something here will tickle someone's fancy. But inevitably, choose to do what most inspires you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/793-phil","name":"phil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T23:28:22-07:00","id":997573,"title":"","content":"So here are answers on those ideas...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=997214#post997214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Consilium</b>: Not sure what the mystery of the Consilium would be. Maybe something about the concentration of places of worship, higher learning and Stephen King is a huge Red Sox fan? But, I agree with having cabals spread out across New England. Instead of a consilium, maybe make the post-Epona's Chariot Ebon Noose formation a tight-knit thearch+arrow caucus and/or experiment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, whole Caucuses are streteched on whole Massachusetes and neighbor counties. Exceptionally Silver Ladder has one mass Caucus in whole New England, where each Grand Magister is running his part of Super Caucus. Khumeia is simple Magister, for now, even when she should be Grand Magister by her running of local Order, what is putting stress on Boston Ladder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=997214#post997214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if I skimmed correctly, the chronicle's primary mystical motif and metaphor is alchemy. To me, this implies themes of change and the direction of enacting those changes; Tao vs. Western Alchemy; greed vs. inner growth; materialism vs. ephemeral/spiritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally. I seperate chronicles own falvor from official NPCs writings and updates - if I stir everything for the game, then my fan updates will be less useful for other players. They should be as much generalized as in <b>Boston Unveiled</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=997214#post997214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus, for <b>Seers</b>, I imagine Mammon and/or Patrenoster would be fitting. (Maybe the decline of the Catholic church in the area plays into this. See: Pedo priests &amp; Cardinal Law.) (Also, Harvard has generated a <i>lot</i> of federal-level economic advisors.) (Also, this could tie into Khumeia\u2019s backstory somewhat.)<br /> <br /> <b>NPCs perhaps interested in the 'philosopher's stone'/directly reflecting alchemy:</b><ul><li>Have Potestas be undergoing the Final Key.</li> <li>Maybe this ties into your central chronicle. But awakened might consider this to be the ultimate inner-transformation.</li> <li>Either way, he\u2019s pulling away from \u201cEarthly concerns\u201d and Aurem is essentially Councilor, etc.</li> <li>Khumeia is \u201cstalling\u201d (stagnation) (Could also be applied to Apollonia, more readily, but I\u2019ll admit to not quite being sure what to do with her.)</li> <li>Tiamat &amp; the Alchemy of Life (and Shadowname)</li> <li>Vision could be an interesting \u2018pentacle-side\u2019 option for the materialism aspect of alchemy; but could also be interesting if he has some sort of \u2018mid-life crisis\u2019 and is trying to change himself and evolve into a mystagogue seriously.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will think on those ideas for the chronicle itself. Thanks for pointing them out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=997214#post997214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Cabals</b><br /> <br /> The Shadow Chorus:<ul><li>Rumors that they are there because of the past and the Emerald Scroll. Personally, I think they are (primarily) Massachusetts natives who the nation-wide GoV (playing \u201cthe inter/national\u201d game) has assigned the task of re-taking Harvard from the Seers.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actual the backstory I use in game. It does have sense they were pointing to 'take back Boston'. Interesting is identity of Culsu, with whole Chorus affiliation with Faceless Guardians. And Culsu being hier to Boston Old Money Family. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-03-2016, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T08:21:19-08:00","id":1009339,"title":"","content":"I too am late to the party. I stopped running my Boston chronicle about 2 years ago, but I'm getting ready to run 2e and I just finished reading 22 months of forum posts. I still have about 25 days to go. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You might find my AP of a Consilium meeting at Cormant House amusing: <a href=\"http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log/session-thirty-five\" target=\"_blank\">http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal....on-thirty-five</a><br /> <br /> I also have a fully fleshed out &quot;dungeon crawl&quot; for Danvers Asylum: <a href=\"http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log/session-thirty-eight\" target=\"_blank\">http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal....n-thirty-eight</a><br /> <br /> I used material from Inferno, Asylum and Intruders. When the chronicle went dormant I didn't bother writing up the last few sessions, but if you're interested in the material, I will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:39:13-08:00","id":1023725,"title":"","content":"I'm about to start running my new Boston chronicle and could use some help.<br /> <br /> The introductory story involves a gang of drug addicts hopping onto the grounds of the cabal's sanctum just to party and make a bonfire. The cabal's sanctum is in Franklin Park in Roxbury and the fire could spread if the cabal doesn't do something about it.<br /> <br /> I'm just trying to teach the system mainly, but I'd like the gang to be addicted to the secret drug alluded to in the book. The one that might be from The Company Cabal, which I'm trying to set up as a rival cabal.<br /> <br /> I'd like the drug to be the first Mystery of the chronicle. I'd like the effects of the drug to make the gang members a little tougher to defeat than just regular Sleeper thugs. Also, the drug is supposed to effect peoples dreams and I'm thinking of The Company not being ultimately responsible, but rather the Seer Pylon - Psychometric Operations.<br /> <br /> Can anyone out there help me construct the Mystery Drug?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 12-29-2016, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:57:48-08:00","id":1023737,"title":"","content":"Dreams and making them harder to beat as Sleepers? Maybe when they dream they're able to pact with Acamoth for power ups, and when they're awake on the drug the Acamoth is fettered to them in Mind Twilight. Or scratch Acamoth, the drug is making the shard of the Abyss in the Oneiros of Sleepers gain sentience, continued use leads to Possession and eventually being Claimed by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T07:14:57-08:00","id":1023744,"title":"","content":"I like the Acamoth idea, because I want the story to lead to exploration of another realm. How do you think the drug is manufactured? Why would Psychometric Operations want to spread this, or is it an experiment gone wrong? How do you think Acamoth Possessed or Claimed would be stated out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T07:42:53-08:00","id":1023751,"title":"","content":"Why? I'm not sure what PO's motives are but if they can point the gangs at Mages in the Pentacle it's not a bad tactic. They might even just be experimenting to see if they can create a new kind of Servitor. The how? Not sure, maybe they have access to an Abyssal Verge that just leaves the stuff lying around like a shallow leaves Tass. Or maybe they've got their hands on a comatose Mad Scelesti so thoroughly tainted with the Abyss his bodily fluids can be synthesized into it. Etc.<br /> <br /> For Possessed or Claimed just stat out a spirit or goetia, slap the Abyssal Entity template on it and then follow the rules in the Manifestation section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T08:30:45-08:00","id":1023776,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it's the Asylum pushing it. PO seem to be their subordinates and Amanda seems pretty inwardly focused on her experiments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T08:55:07-08:00","id":1023787,"title":"","content":"What rank would you recommend for the Goetia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:04:52-08:00","id":1023797,"title":"","content":"Rank two or three probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T15:00:43-08:00","id":1023954,"title":"","content":"What do you think the twisted motivation of the Acamoth might be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T16:39:24-08:00","id":1023995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1023725#post1023725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm about to start running my new Boston chronicle and could use some help.<br /> <br /> The introductory story involves a gang of drug addicts hopping onto the grounds of the cabal's sanctum just to party and make a bonfire. The cabal's sanctum is in Franklin Park in Roxbury and the fire could spread if the cabal doesn't do something about it.<br /> <br /> I'm just trying to teach the system mainly, but I'd like the gang to be addicted to the secret drug alluded to in the book. The one that might be from The Company Cabal, which I'm trying to set up as a rival cabal.<br /> <br /> I'd like the drug to be the first Mystery of the chronicle. I'd like the effects of the drug to make the gang members a little tougher to defeat than just regular Sleeper thugs. Also, the drug is supposed to effect peoples dreams and I'm thinking of The Company not being ultimately responsible, but rather the Seer Pylon - Psychometric Operations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Psychometric Operations are Alchemist - maybe they made potion that changes subjects. As Mind Seers they probably work for Unity Exarch, and by this they are from Hegemony Ministry - and this faction makes Sleepers in to Hallowed, soules drones. Maybe Psychosometrics want to test how new transformation technique works on gangers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T16:40:40-08:00","id":1023996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1023954#post1023954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think the twisted motivation of the Acamoth might be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it really need a motivation beyond bringing more corruption into the Fallen? It might be better to ask what particular flavor of corruption it brings. This being Boston it wouldn't be terribly surprising if it was trying to create servants of the Prince of 10,000 Leaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T09:08:03-08:00","id":1025466,"title":"","content":"Would Psychometric Operations engage in Abyssal magic like these suggestions indicate? Don't Seers generally shun the Abyss as much as Pentacle mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T09:26:11-08:00","id":1025476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1025466#post1025466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Psychometric Operations engage in Abyssal magic like these suggestions indicate? Don't Seers generally shun the Abyss as much as Pentacle mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually, yeah, but they also believe in getting ahead by (almost) any means necessary. Seers are just as likely to go Scelesti as anyone in the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the real reason I see them trying it out is because it seems like it's under control. They're doing a bit of research to make sure that they understand this phenomena fully and then it will become a trump card if they ever need it, but they probably won't and there's no way they'd use it indiscriminately guys and of course they know everything about it they wouldn't be so hubristic as to not double check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T09:32:42-08:00","id":1025478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1025466#post1025466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Psychometric Operations engage in Abyssal magic like these suggestions indicate? Don't Seers generally shun the Abyss as much as Pentacle mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, even more. To Seers, Abyss is chaos uncontrolled. It is the thing that wants to destroy their Fallen kingdom. Still, Seers admits Gate as Eleventh Iron Seal and even it have it's secret Ministry in the Order - but most other Seers do not want to have anything with them and are <i>really</i> afraid of it's servants.<br /> <br /> So I do not see Psychometric Operations as going for Abyss. I <b>can</b> see them trying to make new Servitors for Unity they serving. Getting correct alchemical elixir for mass producing Hive-Souls would be truly terrifying!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-02-2017, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T13:20:33-08:00","id":1025541,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree with Wyrd. Amanda seems to be one of the sensible and conservative Seers. She already has a pylon, a government budget and a nice office at Harvard, why risk that by messing with the Abyss? Aside from the basic risks of the Abyss, when the effects come to the attention of the Pentacle, that's just the kind of thing that might actually provoke a reaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:09:17-08:00","id":1025803,"title":"","content":"Having some free time, I'm returning to Boston cabals updates to 2E. I want to make first Dead Wrens as they will be needed in my next sessions. As I mentioned earlier, I want them to be remade in to proper Free Council Column, seeing changes to Council in 2E. Wrens would have, on general, <i>Techne: Pirates</i> Merit and would still be most important figures in Assembly of Boston. Re-reading FC Order book, I think about giving those positions to members of Wrens:<ul><li><b>Davy Jones</b> - Syndic or Strategos. Theoretically, he would be Startegos as most old in the column. But I cannot see his proper 'area of expertise' for Strategos position on Assembly. On the other hand, as Syndic he would be \u2018political\u2019 inspiration for the rest, giving them \u2018guiding light\u2019 in Council affairs. He could become latter Strategos, if there would be official declared war with Guardians, for example.</li> <li><b>Ishmael </b>\u2013 Host or Voter only? He does not seems to go for any positions, just holding Dead Wrens together. I could see him as looking over club itself, and by this, being Host on the Assembly.</li> <li><b>Rabid Annie </b>\u2013 With her being Arrow in 1E, high combat Skills and general eagerness to fight, I can easily see her as Minute(wo)men in Assembly.</li> <li><b>Menelaus</b> \u2013 Here is where I\u2019m torn apart. He is written so enigmatic, that he can be both Mysterium member and Nameless most of his life. If the second, he would join Wrens on meeting Davy, becoming Free Council. But what would be his position in Assembly then? Maybe Startegos for Times Before things, as he is researcher and most of Voters very likes him?</li> <li><b>Sunjata</b> \u2013 Here is simple. I remade Sunjata in to Emissary of Assembly who is responsible with relations with Consilium. It let him still have his \u2018political aspirations\u2019, work to help with Wrens image, but not being in Silver Ladder just because \u2018they are political Order\u2019.</li> </ul>So what do you think about those changes, guys? Especially, I\u2019m interested in opinion of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:46:56-08:00","id":1025824,"title":"","content":"Don't forget you can give characters a dot of status in another order. Personally I'd leave Annie and Menelaus with 1 dot status in their original orders, though maybe not for Sunjata.<br /> <br /> About titles, personally I'd leave menelaus as a standard member (of whatever level you want). I mean, a strategos is a big deal and I don't really see why the Wrens would go to that level of formality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:58:07-08:00","id":1025829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1025824#post1025824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget you can give characters a dot of status in another order. Personally I'd leave Annie and Menelaus with 1 dot status in their original orders, though maybe not for Sunjata.</div> </div> </div> </div>So like 'those Libertines are friends to X' where X is Arrow and Mysterium, respectively?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1025824#post1025824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About titles, personally I'd leave menelaus as a standard member (of whatever level you want). I mean, a strategos is a big deal and I don't really see why the Wrens would go to that level of formality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will probably make Menelaus as standard Voter, but with high Status in Order - he is described as paternal figure for many Libertines in <b>Boston Unveiled</b>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:10:40-08:00","id":1025837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1025829#post1025829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So like 'those Libertines are friends to X' where X is Arrow and Mysterium, respectively?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends how you want to play it. I mean, there are members of the other Orders in Assemblies and I'm not all that clear how that's supposed to be played (I guess you could invent Assembly Status). It's possible that Menelaus is a Mysterium member who has simply let his contact with them slide.<br /> <br /> That said, the Knights of the Gryphon seem to operate an open door policy as long as you're into the duel arcane; I could see Rabid Annie being friends with them for that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:15:05-08:00","id":1025948,"title":"","content":"Rewritten opening on Dead Wrens, combined pices from <b>Mage</b> 1E and <b>Boston Unveiled</b>, with added my update ideas about group as whole.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Dead Wrens 2E</b></span><br /> Larcenous and daring, the Dead Wrens dominate occult activity in Boston Harbor. They preside over an unlikely alliance of longshoremen, fences, Port Authority officials and antiquarians. They are famous inside Free Council for their dedication to Techne: <i>Pirates</i>, something many people laugh, but many also respect in them.<br /> <br /> They are inheritors of Boston\u2019s Free Council freebooting legacy. Following a long conflict with Boston\u2019s ruling Guardians of the Veil in the early 20th Century, some Free Council mages adapted to the situation and decided to take up smuggling, sea trade and piracy. War struck Europe, and the new cabal found itself in great demand. With the danger of U-Boats and US patrols, the price of transatlantic contraband rose dramatically. The mages combined seamanship and magic to great effect, pulling off nearly impossible jobs under the noses of the world\u2019s militaries. In their success, they found a common identity. A series of Libertine columns followed. The Dead Wrens are the latest of the line, named after the wren feathers that sailors used as good-luck charms.<br /> The Dead Wrens\u2019 sanctum in Fenway is a Hallow that mockingly recreates the old Guardians of the Veil\u2019s Emerald Scroll sanctum. The Wrens run it as a \u201cfree house\u201d for Boston\u2019s mages \u2014 a place to haggle, eavesdrop and contact the Wrens or other New England Libertines by them. Theoretically, Emerald Scroll is also local Lorehouse, but it\u2019s very poorly equipped and Wrens are always looking for \u2018donations\u2019 from other Assembly members.<br /> <br /> The Wrens believe that mages should mind their own business, do as they please, and defend their liberty with necessary force, but minimal fuss. Even though the Dead Wrens are the product of Free Council maneuvers, they are largely apolitical. Pirates and vagabonds, the Dead Wrens do their collective best to remain out of the struggles of the Consilium. While the column agrees to generally abide Ruling Council\u2019s judgments when they are caught, the Wrens only reluctantly involve themselves in it\u2019s politics. After all, there\u2019s little profit to be made there if you\u2019re a little fish, and one never knows if and when the Guardians of the Veil may attempt to extract a pound of flesh from the easiest nearby target that presents itself. Instead, this cabal of miscreants eats, drinks and makes merry, driving back the shadows with laughter, and doing what they can to make peace with those shadows that fail to flee. Until they feel that Libertines in Boston and New England are suppressed \u2013 then they call the Assembly and give needed freedom for Libertine mages.<br /> <br /> The technically ringmaster of the Dead Wrens\u2019 column is the modern-day buccaneer, Davy Jones \u2013 he founded everyone and inspires rest of the group to their actions. In addition to the Emerald Scroll in Fenway, the Wrens maintain some dock space along Boston\u2019s waterfront, in order to have ready access to the sea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T13:15:45-08:00","id":1026133,"title":"","content":"My players are planning on attacking <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1016877-2e-bostonian-alchemist\">'Black' Alchemist from Golden Dawn era</a> living to this day and that kidnapped their Promethean 'friend'. As she is Pyros running relic from the past, involving Free Council in attack can spring wide range conflict between Shadow Chorus and Dead Wrens, or even Guardians and Libertines in general. My players are to decide if they tell everything Dead Wrens for support in strike. In three person cabal, two players are each for one vote to tell and not too ( Libertine and Guardian, respectively, of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). Undecided is Mysterium Novice that is under mentorship of Potestas - he will want to ask him for his opinion. On my first gut feeling Potestas would want to start conflict between Guardians and Libertines to make more place for Mysterium in Consilium power structures, but I'm not sure. What do you he would tell about this? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T15:23:57-08:00","id":1026185,"title":"","content":"First version of 2E Devy Johns, previous Minuteman and Citizen Agent. now Syndic of column. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Character use weapon rules from <b>Hurt Locker</b>. Hope you likes mine simple changes - added Athelics 2, 1 dot of Gnosis and 1 dot of Mind, compared to <b>Boston Unveiled</b>. I have taken 1 dot of his Wisdom, as I cannot see mage with those stats not loosing any dot on the road. As always, any comment is looked for, especially from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a>.<br /> <br /> <b>Davy Jones ( Syndic, possible Strategos )</b><br /> <br /> <b>Quote</b>: <i>Dead men tell no tales and necromancers are bad luck. Meet me at the Scroll with cash in hand, and I\u2019ll pass off a trinket that solves the former problem without causing the latter.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Like his Finnish father, Jones loves the sea. Like his Spanish mother, he\u2019s a profligate spender. This combination inspired him to sign aboard a merchant vessel at the age of 16. Already versed in a morass of nautical and gambling superstitions, Jones Awakened when his ship encountered a savage storm. Though half the crew died, the vessel managed to limp to Boston Harbor. Shaken by the experience, Jones stayed in his cabin while the survivors rested on dry land. Where the rest of the crew saw only great waves and heard only the creaking of the ship, Jones experienced the ship sailing to the mythic edge of the world to be devoured by nameless, horrifically formed creatures beyond. It had taken every bit of his will to climb a spar and learn the secret tides and vortices that would bring the ship to safety. Nowadays, he knows that he experienced a Waking World Awakening \u2014 with the spar as the Acanthus Watchtower \u2014 but he doesn\u2019t always believe it.<br /> <br /> He encountered the second surprise of his life when two cabals snuck aboard ship and fought a magical battle for possession of an obscure piece of cargo. In an instant, he somehow felt that one of the groups was responsible for the storm, so he helped the other. His new allies were the Dead Wrens forefathers. They drove the other cabal away and offered Jones training and adventure in return for the disputed cargo. He accepted, and initiated himself into the Free Council. Soon, he collected his won merry company of \u2018pirates\u2019, starting Dead Wrens. Their forefathers granted them items and need titles to operate \u2013 and went to their own adventures around the world.<br /> Nowadays, Davy Jones patrols the waterfront in a patched black motorboat. On most days, he deals with sailors, long-shoremen and petty smugglers for the Dead Wrens. Jones spends his money freely, cheerfully deals with visitors to the city, and dreams of sailing a modest ship around the world for a bit of anti-authoritarian piracy. Will he disrupt the flow of oil or precious metals? He hasn\u2019t decided yet.<br /> Davy is Dead Wrens Syndic \u2013 philosopher and lobbyist in Assembly, pushing others to do what\u2019s need to be done. Or to the next great adventure. He has history as previous Minuteman, then Citizen Agent but risen from the position in surprisingly quick time. He could be Strategos if Boston Assembly would need one. Or if he just fight he\u2019s natural care free nature. But until Libertines freedom is not endanger, he likes just to makes wheels turning in his own column. And have as much fun as he can.<br /> <b>Description: </b>Jones has long, black dreadlocks, ice-blue eyes and a lithe body given to flamboyant gestures. He usually brings a bit of good rope, a large knife and a smoking pipe (for idle moments) with him to any job. His outfits consist of a mix of sandals, steel-toed boots, coveralls, army-surplus wear and an open bowling shirt. He\u2019s in his mid-twenties.<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Most people will never meet anyone else who says \u201cAvast!\u201d without the slightest hint of self-consciousness. To Jones, pirate talk is just another part of his convoluted Techne \u2014 a modern freebooter\u2019s koans. Other mages treat his habits and shadow name with anything from amusement to contempt, believing Jones to be something of a comedian. The mage takes it all quite seriously, however, and is willing to talk at length about the progressive social revolutions that occurred in historical pirate communities or how Pirate Republic of Nassau was first true precursor for Free Council that Silver Ladder with Seers of Throne crashed before it\u2019s true potential could start mass Awakened revolution. He peppers his self-indulgent talk with all kinds of rumors, offerings and warnings, since he often takes a liking to visitors and underdogs. Still, he is partially political animal \u2013 he knows when he needs to agree with Consilium or to better not start war with them. For now, at least.<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools: Compass</b><br /> <br /> <b>Real Name: </b>Joachim Mhekka<br /> <br /> <b>Path: </b>Acanthus<br /> <br /> <b>Order: </b>Free Council<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b><b> I</b>ntelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Attributes: </b>Strength 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <br /> <b>Social Attributes: </b>Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills: </b>Computers 2, Crafts (Knot Tying) 3, Investigation 2, Medicine 2, Occult 3, Science 2<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills: </b>Athletics 2, Brawl 3, Drive 4, Firearms (Pistols) 4, Larceny 4, Stealth 3, Weaponry 2<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills: </b>Empathy 3, Persuasion 3, Socialize 3, Streetwise (The Docks) 4, Subterfuge 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Contacts (The Street) 1, Hallow (Shared; The Emerald Scroll) 3, High Speech, Library (Occult, Shared ) 3, Library, Advanced ( Local Legends, Witchcraft, Haunted Ships), Resources 3, Sanctum (Shared; The Emerald Scroll) 5, Status (Order 3), Techne: Pirates<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 6<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Driven (Fortitude)<br /> <b>Vice: </b> Overconfident (Pride)<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Get next \u2018Booty\u2019, Smuggle Artifacts under nose of Consilium, Fight \u2018Hierarchy\u2019 \u2013 Seers of Throne or Guardians of Veil<br /> <br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> New England\u2019s Magic, Techne: Pirates<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed: </b>11<br /> <b>Health: </b>8<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 4<br /> <br /> <b>Arcana: </b>Fate 3, Life 2, Mind 2, Space 3, Time 1<br /> <b>Praxis: ???</b><br /> <b>Rotes: ???</b> <b>Nimbus: It appears as a momentary visual sharpening or accentuation of his physical presence, as if he carried a great weight of importance.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tilt: </b>Things looks more real, people also - All characters get +2 to Presence rolls.<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons:</b><br /> <b>Desert Eagle (Heavy Pistol):</b> Damage +2L, Range: Long, Capacity: Medium, Initiative: \u20132, Strength: 3, Size: 1 \u2013 Dicepool: 9<br /> <b>HK MP-5 (9mm) (SMG, heavy):</b> Damage +2L, Range: Medium, Capacity: High, Initiative: \u20133, Strength: 3, Size: 2 \u2013 Dicepool: 8<br /> <b>Brass Knuckles:</b> Damage +0L, Initiative: \u2013 0, Strength: 1, Size: 1 \u2013 Dicepool: 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2017, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T01:55:55-08:00","id":1026406,"title":"","content":"Prepered 2E version of Aurem from Brotherhood as I will need his relations with players on next sessions. Beside adding official title of Atheneum's Curator, I changed all Atlantis mentioning to Time Before, added him 1 dot of Gnosis and 2 dots of Mind. I done this, as his new Obsessions are about Goetia - something he does have lore in Atheneum about, but did not character have large experiance with - and Time Before as his previous Atlantis beng. Beside preparing for taking over Academy and expending Atheneum collection, he is looking over future cabal mates, after he plans to disband Bortherhood. Eager PCs can be those future colleagues of him...<br /> <br /> <b>Aurem (Potestas\u2019 Provost, Atheneum\u2019s Curator)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>As far as we can tell, the protocol in Time Before for such a situation would \u2014 what? Because that is what is written. Well, naturally, such accounts are shrouded in symbolism and deliberate occlusion. Now, where was I?</i><br /> <b>Background:</b> Aurem is Potestas\u2019 oldest surviving student, and he has inherited much of the elder willworker\u2019s contentious nature. Aurem is arrogant like his teacher but perhaps not quite as abrasive and blatant in his elitism. Potestas took the newly Awakened man under his wing while on a trip to Cambridge, England, while there to visit with an old associate he had met during the Second World War. Over time, Potestas and Aurem, so similar in personality, have come to clash over a number of issues and Aurem, long in his mentor\u2019s shadow, began to push for increased control over the Brotherhood. His appointment to the position of Potestas\u2019 Provost in 1990 has furthered his ambitions in some respects, and stymied them in others. All the same time Aurem was hoarding new collections for Boston Atheneum, beings it\u2019s Curator, since his predecessor left the post.<br /> <br /> Now, the two divide control of the Brotherhood between them, as well as control over the Exalted Knights of the Gryphon. Still, Aurem is keenly aware that his day will only truly come when Potestas is out of the picture. Such knowledge pains Aurem on one level, but he comforts himself with the understanding that Potestas\u2019 vision of the rise of the Academy is bigger than any one person and the old man would want his onetime student to prosper by his demise.<br /> <br /> Until that day, however, Aurem bides his time, ever expanding collections of Atheneum and hones his skills in the constant duel with Potestas for mastery of the Academy.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Aurem is a stately older man, now in his mid-60s. His features are severe, and his dark brown skin is creased from long years spent squinting over old tomes. His gray hair is neatly trimmed at all times, as is his goatee. He tends toward suits in browns, beiges and grays, and walks with an unadorned cane of brass and ash. Increasingly, he is forced to resort to glasses with small, rectangular lenses and gold frames when reading. His British accent is undiminished by time and, depending upon his exact tone, makes all he says sound haughty, sophisticated or both.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Well aware that Potestas\u2019 days in this world are few now, Aurem is getting all of his affairs in order, so as to best capitalize upon what he knows will be left to him when the older mage passes. Like Potestas, Aurem wants to see the Mysterium rise to become the dominant order of the region, and he knows that he\u2019s got at least another good decade, maybe two, left in him, barring ill fortune. Further, he\u2019s willing to set up another, a generation or two down the line, if need be, to assume leadership of the Consilium. His patience and calculation are reflected in his speech and his mannerisms, as is his great intellect. As he intends to disband the Brotherhood upon Potestas\u2019 death, Aurem is ever mindful of the doings of talented willworkers who might be persuaded to join him.<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools: </b>British coin marked with a pentagram, sapphire ring (Prime magic)<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Zachary Harcourt<br /> <b>Path:</b> Obrimos<br /> <b>Order:</b> Mysterium<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 5, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes: </b>Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills: </b>Academics 5, Computer 2, Crafts 2, Investigation (Research) 4, Medicine 2, Occult 5, Politics 4, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Drive 1, Stealth 1, Weaponry (Swords) 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 2, Expression 2, Intimidation 3, Persuasion 3, Socialize 3, Subterfuge (Lies) 4<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Dream 3, Hallow (Shared) 5, High Speech, Language (Ancient Greek, French, Hebrew, Latin, Spanish), Library (Occult, Shared) 3, Library, Advanced ( Time Before, the Awakened in Politics, Cryptozoology, Goetia and Numerology), Resources 4, Sanctum (Personal) 2, Sanctum (Shared)<br /> 7, Status (Consilium 4, Order 4)<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Cautious (Prudence)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Arrogant (Pride)<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Expand Atheneum collections, Prepare for taking Academy, Find future cabal members<br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> Goetia, Time Before ( Atlantis )<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 5<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Fate 2, Forces 4, Life 2, Matter 2, Mind 2, Prime 4, Spirit 3<br /> <b>Rotes: </b>???<br /> <br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> Bolts of golden lightning, radiating outward from him and licking at every surface within 10 feet of his body.<br /> <b>Tilt: </b> Light is blinding - All characters get -2 to Perception rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T14:25:32-08:00","id":1026691,"title":"","content":"Get Ishmael from Dead Wrens now. Changes, beside adding his role as Host of Assemblies, are simply Gnosis dot, rising Defense and Aspirations and Obsessions. Obsessions are just copy of Davy as Ishmael is all about 'doing what rest do/want me to do', I only do not have idea for his 3rd Aspiration. Maybe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1470_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1470\" data-vbnamecard=\"1470\">Johnny Awesome</a> will look on latest characters and write what he thinks of them? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Ishmael ( Voter and Host )</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>If it\u2019s \u2018Avast!\u2019 and \u2018Yo-ho!\u2019 you\u2019re looking for, then it\u2019s Davy you\u2019re after. If you\u2019re in the mood for strong spirits, then you want Annie. If you need \u2014 what? Oh, me? I just kinda sit around and soak up the local character . . .</i><br /> <b>Background:</b> Antonio Aceveda was never comfortable with the spotlight. Given the choice, he always preferred to be the sidekick to a more capable and charismatic person. In elementary school, Antonio ran with the good-natured troublemakers and took more than his fair share of the blame for their mischief when things went wrong and none of the credit when they went right. In high school, he was the long-suffering but high-spirited fall guy for the popular kids. Right around graduation, he did some soul-searching and came to terms with the notion. Without the inclination or the grades to enter college, Antonio took up working on the docks in Boston, and was content, if not really happy, for a time.<br /> <br /> Like Davy\u2019s, Antonio\u2019s Awakening came at sea, but his involved a near-death experience by way of drowning. It was Davy who fished him out of the ocean. As Antonio was regaining consciousness, Davy, decked out in pirate finery that somehow made Antonio think of Moby Dick, asked him his name. Antonio could only think to quip, \u201cCall me Ishmael.\u201d The name stuck, becoming Antonio\u2019s Shadow Name. Since then, he has been Davy\u2019s devoted sidekick and the glue that holds the Dead Wrens together \u2013 also by making sure about Emerald Scroll as the Host of Assembly meetings in there. He run most of day to day issues with Sanctum.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>Ishmael is a trifle scrawny and a bit shorter than average, but with a scruffy and somewhat roguish look that some find appealing. His badly bleached hair is tangled from long hours at sea, and he rarely finds the time to properly maintain his thin mustache and the narrow strip of beard just under his lower lip. His dress is flamboyant, but not as much as Davy\u2019s, and Ishmael instinctively and comfortably falls in behind the other mage\u2019s lead.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Ishmael is a perpetual henchman, and he\u2019s quite good at the role. Furthermore, he\u2019s only truly comfortable when in the shadow of a more dynamic figure. Being in the spotlight as the butt of a friendly joke or when explaining his role in someone else\u2019s brilliant plan works fine for him; being the life of the party or the one coming up with the brilliant plan, on the other hand, just isn\u2019t his style. He\u2019s also got the best handle on all of the Dead Wrens\u2019 disparate interests, though he would never knowingly betray that confidence.<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools:</b> Cell phone<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Antonio Aceveda<br /> <b>Path:</b> Acanthus<br /> <b>Order:</b> Free Council<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 2<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 1, Computer 1, Crafts 2, Investigation 1, Medicine (First Aid) 1, Occult 2, Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Swimming) 2, Brawl 1, Drive 2, Firearms 1, Larceny 2, Stealth (Crowds) 3, Survival 1<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Empathy (Motives) 3, Persuasion 3, Socialize (Bar Hopping) 2, Streetwise 4, Subterfuge (Spotting Lies) 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Barfly, Contacts (Coast Guard, Dock Workers, Port Authority), Hallow (Shared) 3, High Speech, Language (Spanish), Library ( Occult, Shared) 3, Library, Advanced ( Local Legends, Witchcraft, Haunted Ships), Resources 2, Sanctum (Shared) 5, Status (Order 2), Techne: Pirates<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower: </b>5<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Helpful ( Charity )<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Clingy ( Lust )<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Help Dead Wrens, Take care of Sanctum, ???<br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> New England\u2019s Magic, Techne: Pirates<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative: </b>6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 2<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Fate 2, Mind 1, Prime 1, Space 1, Time 2<br /> <b>Rotes:</b> ???<br /> <br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> Dappling of light all over and around him, as though from tropical sunlight reflected from gentle waves.<br /> <b>Tilt: </b>Light is blinding - All characters get -1 to Perception rolls.<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons:</b><br /> <b>Glock 17 (9mm) (Light Pistol):</b> Damage +1L, Range: Long, Capacity: Medium, Initiative: \u20130, Strength: 2, Size: 1 \u2013 Dicepool: 4<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-05-2017, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:15:46-08:00","id":1026914,"title":"","content":"Time for Rabid Annie! Beside making her Minutewoman, adding one Status in Free Council and Adamantine Arrow for her, adding dot in Gnosis and Life ( to let her cast <i>Knit </i>herself ), I made her Familiar a little bit more powerful, as by 2E he would be on the edge of Rank 1 spirit - so I gave him Rank 2 by adding one Attribute dot more. I also changed her Irrationality to Dehumanization Condition, as it is much better working with her profile of 'constant fighting' Libertine. Her cutlass stats are based on Machete from <b>Hurt Locker</b>. I also have problem with Bane for her Familiar, as I do not know what concept of spirit he was based of - any ideas would be great on this one. So here it is she and her bird. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Rabid Annie ( Minutewoman )</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>Storm\u2019s comin\u2019. Bad one, too.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Laura Passius loved to listen to her mother\u2019s stories of her ancestor, \u2018Rabid Annie\u2019 Shaw, whom she was told was a pirate who sailed the Spanish Main. Of course, as she got older, Laura learned that \u201cRabid Annie\u201d was likely nothing more than a bedtime fable made up to put a hyper-active tomboy to sleep with tales of high-seas adventure.<br /> <br /> Somehow, that struck the young girl as terribly unfair and, at the age of nine, she resolved to become Rabid Annie when she grew up. Laura had no one particularly qualified to teach her about sailing ships, so she taught herself through a combination of books, television and raw intuition. Her peers laughed at her in middle school and high school, but she didn\u2019t particularly care for their opinions on much of anything, anyway. When she finally dropped out during junior year and ran away from home, she booked passage on a ship bound for Europe and spent some time in a sleepy fishing village in Greece, learning the unglamorous basics of her self-appointed vocation: knot work, predicting the weather and the like.<br /> <br /> She doesn\u2019t speak of her Awakening, but returned to America a willworker, going by the name of her imaginary ancestor. She drifted for a few years, only settling down in Boston after meeting Davy Jones at sea. (Both were in stolen boats at the time). Her brewer\u2019s skills, picked up here and there, made her an instant hit with the newly formed Dead Wrens, and she was quickly voted in as a member. Since then, she has been with the Wrens, and has been Davy\u2019s on-again, off-again lover.<br /> <br /> Her combat determination and connections to Adamantine Arrows \u2013 as she was rumored to be inducted to Dragons Talons first, in Europe \u2013 make her great material for Minutewoman in Assembly, ready to strike as her Shadow Name giver in her stories is. Annie still sustain positive Arrow contacts by participating in duels with Knights of Gryphon.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>Had her life taken a different course, Rabid Annie might have been a very pretty woman. Though weathered by sun and sea, she\u2019s still handsome, despite looking well older than her 30 or so years. No one is quite certain of her ethnic background judging by her appearance alone, but it is obvious that at least some of her ancestry is Mediterranean. She habitually wears a heavy, leather long coat (once black and now a dark and battered brown), and is often clad in leather pants, engineer\u2019s boots and tight-fitting shirts. When at sea, far from the eyes of the authorities, she\u2019s known to keep an ornate cutlass belted at her left hip.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Rabid Annie fancies herself a modern-day pirate, rather than one in the traditional mold, like Davy Jones. She prefers her two speedboats and small modern yacht to any old-fashioned schooner or sloop. She isn\u2019t terribly practical, but is far more so than Davy, and can make him see reason when others fail to \u2014 a role she has comfortably adopted within the Dead Wrens. Annie is also a veteran carouser and can drink any of the Wrens (and most people besides) under the table.<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools:</b> Silver hipflask<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Laura Passius<br /> <b>Path:</b> Mastigos<br /> <b>Order:</b> Free Council ( probably ex - Adamantine Arrow )<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 2, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Crafts (Brewery) 2, Medicine 1, Occult (Nautical Phenomena) 1, Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Swimming) 3, Brawl (Dirty Tricks) 2, Drive (Speed Boats) 2, Firearms 1, Larceny 3, Stealth 1, Survival 1, Weaponry 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken (Birds) 1, Empathy 1, Intimidation (Bluster) 2, Persuasion (Fast-Talking) 2, Socialize (Carousing) 2, Streetwise 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Allies (Smugglers) 1, Direction Sense, Familiar 4 (embodied macaw; see below), Hallow (Shared) 3, High Speech, Imbued Item 4, Language (Greek), Library (Occult, Shared) 3, Library, Advanced ( Local Legends, Witchcraft, Haunted Ships), Resources 2, Sanctum (Shared) 5, Status (Free Council 2, Adamantine Arrow 1 ), Techne: Pirates, Toxin Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 5 (Dehumanization)<br /> <b>Dehumanization </b>- Res+Comp roll when inconvenienced or frustrated by other people's perceived weakness or stupidity. On failure, -2 to all Social rolls except Intimidation.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Hopeful (Hope)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Rivalry (Envy)<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Win conflicts, Sparing with people, Fight for Assembly<br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> New England\u2019s Magic, Techne: Pirates<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 3<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Life 3, Mind 2, Space 3<br /> <b>Praxis: </b>Co-Location<br /> <b>Rotes: ???</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> Shows as a flickering of afterimages, like stutters of her movement, lagging behind her in space.<br /> <b>Tilt: </b>Images are confusing - All characters get -2 to Perception rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons:</b><br /> <b>Imbued Cutlass*</b> - Damage +2L, Initiative: \u20132, Strength: 2 Size: 2 - Dicepool: 6<br /> * Rabid Annie\u2019s imbued cutlass can be used to cast the Prime 3 \u201cCelestial Fire\u201d spell as a contingent power (in addition to serving as a normal cutlass).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b><i>Mister Higgins, Annie\u2019s Macaw Familiar</i></b></span><br /> <br /> The familiar spirit known as Mister Higgins is locked in a form of a particularly large and colorful macaw. For the most part, he keeps his silence and acts the part of an ordinary animal when around those outside Annie\u2019s cabal. Occasionally, however, especially around Sleepers (particularly if he\u2019s mad at Annie for something or just feeling perverse), he likes to say things that have no business coming out of a parrot\u2019s mouth. While he knows that his mischief will earn him something foul for dinner, the comedic value is (usually) worth the price.<br /> <br /> Beyond his questionable sense of humor, Mister Higgins is rather wise and well versed in many paranormal secrets, as well as a keen student of human nature. His insights into potential business partners (often whispered into Annie\u2019s ear while she steps away to grab a few drinks for people) have proven quite valuable to the cabal in more than one instance.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 3, Finesse 4, Resistance 2<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 15<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed: </b>17 (flight only; species factor 10)<br /> <b>Size:</b> 2<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 4<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Cunning \u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Drain, Innocuous, Seek<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Familiar, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Mister Higgins may not refuse any food offered to him, no matter how unpleasant or dangerous it may be.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Axe used to cut down a palm tree","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-05-2017, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:24:51-08:00","id":1026918,"title":"","content":"How about an axe used to cut down a palm tree? That's a callback to the origin of macaw parrots and their current endangerment via deforestation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T03:28:30-08:00","id":1026954,"title":"","content":"And here is Menelaus in 2E. Beside making him possible Strategos on Time Before, he is the one responsible on Lorehouse in Emerald Scroll. As to stats changes I given him 1 dot in Occult to show his dedication to supernatural and Time Before, one dot in Status of Free Council and Mysterium, but I taken away Encyclopedic Knowlegde, as it in 2E Merit needs to be pointed to what Skill he would have this - and any Skill I can think of, he already has 4 dots in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I also add him one dot to Gnosis, because of his age and many adventures.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Menelaus ( Voter. possible Strategos on Time Before )</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>Where\u2019s your taste for adventure, boy? Better to die young, in the jaws of something unspeakable, than at home, in bed, surrounded by weeping faces!</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>Damien Charles III lived a reasonably humdrum life up until graduate school in archaeology. He was cataloguing a dig site in the Cambodian jungle when the visions came to him. His team thought he had fallen ill, and he ranted about a \u201cbook of stone, covered in vines\u201d and \u201can ancient evil.\u201d They confined him, but his strength seemed almost unnatural. He broke the ropes that had been used to bind him, and disappeared into the wilds. Two years after all efforts to find him had ceased, he emerged, having at long last bested the dark spirit he sensed.<br /> <br /> Charles wandered the world aimlessly, stumbling upon adventure after adventure, and began to fancy himself a modern-day Menelaus, who learned the secrets of safe passage across the seas from the god Proteus, adopting the name as his own. He met up with Davy Jones in Iceland; both men were searching for the same piece of Viking treasure, only to find that it had been looted perhaps a century before. Despite the difference in their respective ages, the two men hit it off grandly, and Menelaus returned to Boston with the younger willworker, eager to offer his knowledge and experience to the Wrens, a task he performs with the same gusto he devotes to all the pursuits of his colorful life.<br /> <br /> Menelaus were in Mysterium at time of his recruitment by Davy. He technically <i>still is</i>, but by the years he understood that Mystygouges are too boring to him and he much more like merry company of Boston Assembly. He impress rest of the group on his knowledge of Time Before and is treated as parental figure for most of them. If anytime there would be needed official Strategos on grounds of Artifacts or secrets of (many) Atlantis(is), Menelaus would surely be the guy to get job done. For now, he is mostly responsible for Lorehouse in Emerald Scroll.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Menelaus looks like an old salt now, with a weatherworn face, a thick beard, gray-streaked hair and a nose swollen from one too many old breaks. He dresses simply, favoring heavy, dark wool coats (to ward off the ocean\u2019s chill) and sturdy boots. In warmer weather, he sheds the coat, revealing worn jeans and light, comfortable shirts. Somewhere along the line, he started smoking a pipe, and now boasts an impressive collection of them, often cycling a new one into use every two weeks or so. Smiles come easily to him, and his peals of laughter can be hard booming over all but the stormiest seas.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Menelaus wants to sail the seas, find treasure, fight monsters and otherwise do all the things heroes in ancient tales do. He\u2019s a seasoned traveler and knows a little something about most any port of call. His academic background makes him knowledgeable, and his experiences make him wiser than he often lets on. He sees Davy as a younger brother \u2014 or perhaps even a son (even he\u2019s not sure which) \u2014 and as a comrade-in-arms, a fellow seeker of the world\u2019s mysteries. The rest of the Dead Wrens are all seen in an unambiguously paternal light.<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools:</b> Personal journal<br /> <b>Real Name:</b> Damien Charles III<br /> <b>Path:</b> Thyrsus<br /> <b>Order:</b> Free Council (ex \u2013 Mysterium )<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Archaeology) 4, Crafts (Shipwright) 2, Investigation (Artifacts) 4, Medicine 2, Occult (Superstitions) 4<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Firearms 1, Larceny 2, Stealth 1, Survival 2, Weaponry 1<br /> <b>Social Skills: </b>Empathy 1, Intimidation 1, Persuasion 1, Socialize 2, Streetwise (Ports) 3, Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Contacts (Black Market, International Shipping), Direction Sense, Hallow (Shared) 3, High Speech, Language (Ancient Greek, Arabic, Cambodian, Cantonese, Filipino, Italian, Latin, Portuguese, Spanish), Library (Occult, Shared) 3, Library, Advanced ( Local Legends, Witchcraft, Haunted Ships), Resources 3, Sanctum (Shared) 5, Status (Consilium 1, Free Council 3, Mysterium 1)<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Idealist (Hope)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Thrill-Seeker (Gluttony)<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Find adventures, See the world, Build Lorehouse collection<br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> New England\u2019s Magic, Time Before<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 4<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Fate 2, Life 3, Spirit 4, Time 2<br /> <b>Praxis: </b>Gossamer Touch, Honing the Form<br /> <b>Rotes: ???</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> Manifests as phantom scenes of ancient battles, perceived just around him, seen as though through a swirling fog.<br /> <b>Tilt: </b>Images are confusing - All characters get -2 to Perception rolls.<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons:</b><br /> <b>Imbued Brass Knuckles*</b> - Damage +0L, Initiative: 0, Strength: 1 Size: 1 - Dicepool: 5 (8)<br /> * Menelaus imbued brass knuckles can be used to cast the Life 3 \u2018Honing the Form\u2019 and Spirit 2 \u2018Gossamer Touch\u2019 spells as a contingent power (in addition to serving as a normal brass knuckles). In bracelets Dicepool after activating \u2018Honing the Form\u2019 power, with used Reach to go beyond human limits in to Strenght, for 1 Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-05-2017, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T05:36:16-08:00","id":1026978,"title":"","content":"And last but not least - Sunjata, the Emissary to Consilium. Beside highlighting his role in Assembly, I removed him being Silver Ladder in 1E, as it was weird looking. I also added him one dot of Gnosis and Death and changed his Boxing Fighiting Style for Kino Mutai that will give him extra damage on Grapple actions he likes so much. He use Tiger Claws as weapon both more effective and exotic than brass knuckles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Left him with Artifact Merit rating, but as it was a bit lower on costs, I also give him Mental Shield from it. Any comments welcome.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Sunjata ( Emissary )</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>I shall have it for you at the appointed hour, but in exchange, you must do for me those favors we agreed upon. Do we have a bargain? Good. Then let our pact be sealed in blood.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Sunjata doesn\u2019t remember where he comes from, anymore. He has vague recollections of a great battle at sea, with cannons roaring and men with swords, but knows that such memories cannot be. And, yet, so many things are alien to him. Cars and computers baffle him, but the sea is comforting: it is eternal, and, when the winds blow just right, from east to west, there is a hint of memory, just on the edge of his consciousness, that he cannot quite get hold of. It is enough for him, though; it has to be.<br /> <br /> Sunjata found the Wrens when the cabal was vacationing in Jamaica. He knew where to look for them, and that he needed to find them (but not why) \u2014 and could not recall what he was doing on the island or how he had gotten there. After a few bottles of spirits, Sunjata and the Dead Wrens came to the agreement that he should join the cabal. Davy called it \u201cgood fortune,\u201d and everyone left it at that. Since coming on board, Sunjata has tried to encourage the rest of the cabal to take a more active hand in the Consilium\u2019s politics but has thus far met with little success, despite his own inroads into the local power structure. As Emissary, it\u2019s his obligation to lower tensions between Consilium and Assembly \u2013 but more than most he must save Libertines from next hasty judgment of Ruling Council for they next breaking of local laws. None the less, if you want to resolve problem with Diamond mages, Sunjata is your guy in Boston.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>Sunjata is a towering, muscular man. His hair is worn in long, thick dreadlocks, and his complexion is a deep, rich brown, contrasting sharply with the white gleam of his perfect teeth when he flashes one of his dashing, dangerous smiles. Gold hoops dangle from his earlobes.<br /> <br /> When on land, he wears one of his many tasteful suits. (He claims that the garb, combined with his wild mane of hair and looming height, serves to put others off balance). At sea, he dresses far more simply: jeans and little else, save in the most frigid weather. His voice is a low, dignified rumble, and his pronunciation of all of the languages he knows is flawless and eerily unaccented.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> At his core, Sunjata is a lost man, without a past and disconcerted at the prospect of what the future holds. He is aware that his name (which he somehow knows was adopted, not his real name) means \u201cHungry Lion\u201d and, beyond that, has only a few flashes of images and some inexplicable memories. Two are scents (jasmine and pine), and the other is a short sentence (a sibilant voice hissing the words, \u201cI know where she is,\u201d in German). He wants to see the Dead Wrens take on a position of prominence and influence, in the hopes that doing so will enable him to discover more about who he really is, but he is coming to believe that such is not truly why he is here, now, with Davy and the rest.<br /> <br /> <b>Dedicated Magical Tools:</b> Antique gold Indian Madras Presidency Star Pagoda coin (with five-pointed star)<br /> <b>Real Name: </b>Unknown<br /> <b>Path: </b>Acanthus<br /> <b>Order:</b> Free Council<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 2, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes: </b>Strength 4, Dexterity 2, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills: </b>Academics 1, Crafts 2, Investigation 1, Occult (Witchcraft) 3, Politics 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Distance Running) 3, Brawl (Grappling) 4, Survival 2, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Empathy 2, Intimidation 3, Persuasion 2, Socialize 1, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge (Misdirection) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Artifact 4 (The Seal of Nar-Khedai), Kino Mutai 2, Giant, High Speech, Language (English, French, German, Portuguese), Sanctum (Shared) 5, Status (Consilium 2, Order 2), Striking Looks 2<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> 5<br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Honorable (Justice)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Ambitious (Greed)<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> Get back his memories, Help Assembly members in political problems, Rise in power in Consilium<br /> <b>Obsessions:</b><br /> Lost memories, Understand his Destiny with Dead Wrens<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed: </b>11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 3<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Death 2, Fate 4, Time 3<br /> <b>Praxis: </b>?<br /> <b>Rotes: ???</b><br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> Image of a ghostly lion from behind him to curl its lips back in an unheard roar.<br /> <b>Tilt: </b>Lion after Sunjata is frightening \u2013 He get\u2019s +2 to all Presence rolls. But people are also afraid of him \u2013 he get\u2019s -2 penalty to any Manipulation rolls for the Tilt being.<br /> <b>Legacy Attainments:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons:</b><br /> <b>Imbued Tiger Claws</b> - Damage +1L, Initiative: -1, Strength: 2, Size: 2 - Dicepool: 8 ( 9 je\u015bli Grappling )<br /> * Sunjata imbued Tiger Claws can be used to cast the Death 2 \u2018Touch of the Grave\u2019 spellas a contingent power (in addition to serving as a normal Tiger Claws).<br /> <br /> <b>The Seal of Nar-Khedai (Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Durability 5, Size 1, Structure 5<br /> Mana Capacity: Maximum 8<br /> This ivory pendant is elegantly carved into the stylized image of a grinning hyena\u2019s head, and is considered by some scholars to have once been the personal seal of the Atlantean exile Nar-Khedai, a powerful Mastigos. A small loop at the back of the Artifact allows it to be threaded on a thin cord of some sort. (Currently, it is worn on a slim leather thong). The seal is believed to have originated in Pandemonium, and allows its bearer to manipulate others\u2019 initial impressions of him \u2014 a contingent Mind 2 \u2018First Impressions\u2019 and \u2018Mental Shield\u2019 effects (see both in <b>Mage: The Awakening 2E</b>, p. 160) that is activated by touching the pendant lightly, whether directly or through clothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T21:25:03-08:00","id":1031972,"title":"","content":"As my players starting to work as proper mages, I start to look for constant Caucuses schedule. For now I have those from <b>Boston Unveiled</b>:<ul><li>Adamantine Arrow - Bi-monthly, third weekend of month, Windham Manor.</li> <li>Free Council - 'Infrequent', at sea.</li> <li>Guardians of Veil - Monthly, ??? , Oubliette. / Here is change from BU as I marked that I want to make GotV proper Caucuse, so regular meetings are nessecery /</li> <li>Mysterium - Monthly, every 15th at 8 P.M, Atheneum in Academy.</li> <li>Silver Ladder - ??? as we rewritten Order Caucus and Nemean running the show is long missing.</li> </ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1470_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1470\" data-vbnamecard=\"1470\">Johnny Awesome</a>, what do you have on this time table?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:31:48-08:00","id":1034741,"title":"","content":"Preparing Mysterium Caucus for running meeting scene of all members. And I found some problems with members adherents to Mysterium dogma and tradition from Order book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I written in format Shadow Name - Cabal from where NPC is - Possible Legacy for him - Ranks in Mysterium - Sophiad ( greater Obsession ) of character. Any help would be appreciated. Maybe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> or <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1470_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1470\" data-vbnamecard=\"1470\">Johnny Awesome</a> have some comments on those?<br /> <br /> <b>Seraphim</b> \u2013 Gravediggers \u2013 Scions of God \u2013 Daduchos, Acquisitor - Teratology ( Angels and Spirits )<br /> <b>Potestas</b> \u2013 Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth - ??? \u2013 Hierophant of Mysterium \u2013 Taumatology<br /> <b>Aurem</b> - Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth - ??? \u2013 Daduchos Superior, Curator of Ateneum \u2013 Supernology and Sidereology ( Goetia )<br /> <b>Agdos</b> - Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth - ??? - Alchemists, Neokoros Superior, Acquisitor \u2013 Exoterics ( Metallurgy and Chemistry )<br /> <b>Numa</b> - Sanguine Laurel - ??? - Daduchos Superior, Savant \u2013 Supernology ( Time Before and Blood of Dragon ) and Exoterics ( History )<br /> <b>Blanchefleur</b> - Sanguine Laurel - ??? - Neokoros Superior \u2013 Supernology ( Time Before )?<br /> <b>Ranae </b>\u2013 Sanguine Laurel - ??? \u2013 Daduchos, Savant \u2013 Supernology ( Time Before ) and Exoterics ( History )<br /> <b>Hrothwulf - </b>Sanguine Laurel - ??? - Neokoros Superior, Acquisitor \u2013 Supernology ( Time Before )<br /> <b>Ahriman</b> \u2013 Ebon Noose - ??? - Daduchos Superior, Savant \u2013 Abyss and Occultism ( Death rituals )<br /> <b>Chain Parris</b> \u2013 White Putnams - ??? \u2013 Daduchos, Acquisitor \u2013 ( I really do not have idea on him, he\u2019s write-up screams to me about more spiritual Silver Ladder than Mysterium member\u2026 :/ )<br /> <b>Magdalena </b>- White Putnams - ??? \u2013 ??? - ( Another I really do not have idea on her\u2026 :/ )<br /> <b>Sophia</b> - White Putnams - ??? \u2013 ??? - ( Another better in Silver Ladder from her write up\u2026 :/ )<br /> <b>Silentium \u2013 </b>White Putnams - ??? \u2013 Censor? \u2013 ( Another one I do not think works with Mysterium, or only bearly. )<br /> <b>Tisiphone </b>- Hecate\u2019s Labrys - ??? - Neokoros Superior, Acquisitor? \u2013 Occultism ( Wicca? )<br /> <b>Stryx</b> - Hecate\u2019s Labrys - ??? - Neokoros Superior, Censor? \u2013 Thaumatology?<br /> <b>Obsidi Anne</b> - Hecate\u2019s Labrys - ??? - Neokoros, ??? \u2013 Exoterics (Architecture)<br /> <br /> Still needs some ideas for experts on Magosophy and Sidreology in Caucus. White Putnams do not work with Mysterium focus on uncovering lore, at least I cannot see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-19-2017, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T18:43:44-08:00","id":1034989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1034741#post1034741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Putnams do not work with Mysterium focus on uncovering lore, at least I cannot see it.</div> </div> </div> </div> You are right, they do seem like a poor fit for the Mysterium. Me, I prefer to acknowledge this dissonance as a heritage from their all-thearch days. However, in between soirees and power-brokering, the Putnams move their Guanxi like no other cabal does: they have access to private collections, research fund donations, prime real estate and old-boys clubs. After all, knowledge really IS power, and money and connections are just another tool for the acquisition of more knowledge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T19:45:50-08:00","id":1035010,"title":"","content":"It's subtle, but basically the Mysterium members of the White Putnams focus on studying the intersection of faith and magic. They aren't an entirely Mysterium cabal though so their focus is muddied by also needing to acquire and utilize political power. Plus they're a legacy cabal, mission drift is practically unavoidable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T21:19:19-08:00","id":1035051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1034989#post1034989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, in between soirees and power-brokering, the Putnams move their Guanxi like no other cabal does: they have access to private collections, research fund donations, prime real estate and old-boys clubs. After all, knowledge really IS power, and money and connections are just another tool for the acquisition of more knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>But how to acknowledge White Putnams and their Guanxi 'power house'? That they are all Acquisitors, collecting books for Atheneum by using their high spheres connections? And what about Sophiad of members - Supernology ( Angels ) and Teratology ( Angels )? Because I have problem pointing them all as Sophiad = Magical Jesus... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I try to pin point them to what could they talk about on Symposium part of Mysterium meeting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-20-2017, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T01:36:03-08:00","id":1035128,"title":"","content":"Khonsu gave you at least one hint, Chain at one pint was interested in the mystic relevance of Orthodox paraphernalia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T02:02:39-08:00","id":1035132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1035128#post1035128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Khonsu gave you at least one hint, Chain at one pint was interested in the mystic relevance of Orthodox paraphernalia.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Occultism ( Christanity myths )?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T02:07:25-08:00","id":1035135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1035132#post1035132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Occultism ( Christanity myths )?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, obviously, like I said before the Mysterium members of the White Putnam are interested in investigating the intersection between faith and magic. Their main Mystery they focus on is defining a form of Christianity that they can still follow while having their worldview altered so heavily by the knowledge they gain from the Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T03:59:04-08:00","id":1035154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1035135#post1035135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, obviously, like I said before the Mysterium members of the White Putnam are interested in investigating the intersection between faith and magic. Their main Mystery they focus on is defining a form of Christianity that they can still follow while having their worldview altered so heavily by the knowledge they gain from the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess the Thearch half of the cabal is interested in a new Awakened Christian doctrine compatible with the Elemental Precepts, while their mystagogue companions probably focus more on the power of faith, miracles, angels and Christian relics.<br /> This thread, BTW, is really helping me to flesh out the Boston setting. Thank you to all involved!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:19:20-08:00","id":1035403,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So, here is my first stab at the Mystery Drug mentioned in the book:</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Deep Purple</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">In an effort to create soul-less hive mind drone servitors for Unity, Dr. Amanda Keller of Psychometric Operations has synthesized an intravenous drug that slowly subverts the Oneiros and destroys the Daimon of the user. The Oneiros of the users slowly mutate into identical forms with no individual identity with a connection to one another in the Temenos.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Side effects</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- The drug causes strange dreams where the user feels their identity and desire for self-improvement fade away over several weeks of habitual use. It\u2019s also a heroin hybrid with heightened effects.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- The Astral effect attracts the attention of Acamoth dedicated to corrupting the users into cannibals in the service of the Prince of 100,000 Leaves. The Acamoth initially Fetters itself to the user, then Possesses and eventual Claims him. This was undiscovered in initial testing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Acamoth</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Rank 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Influence: Hunger 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Power: 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Finesse: 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Resistance: 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Size: 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Speed: 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Corpus: 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Willpower: 9</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Essence: 15</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Manifestations: Twilight Form</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Numina: Fetter, Urge, Possess, Claim, Bolster*</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">* Increase physical traits of Fettered host with Essence on a 1-1 basis for a scene<br /> <br /> I'd still like constructive criticism, some help in naming and defining the appearance of the Acamoth, and in building this as a Mystery (rules wise with Opacity etc...)<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T16:43:43-08:00","id":1035515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1035403#post1035403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- The drug causes strange dreams where the user feels their identity and desire for self-improvement fade away over several weeks of habitual use. It\u2019s also a heroin hybrid with heightened effects.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This works with Amanda's focus as Unity Seer...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1035403#post1035403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">- The Astral effect attracts the attention of Acamoth dedicated to corrupting the users into cannibals in the service of the Prince of 100,000 Leaves. The Acamoth initially Fetters itself to the user, then Possesses and eventual Claims him. This was undiscovered in initial testing.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>... but this not very much. Prince of 100,000 Leaves is not very much prawling the Astral, he is Annanuki, Abysal alternate world, outside of normal time and space. Prince is Time phenomena, as he <i>is</i> alternate timeline where sacrifice someone is greatest feat of love. If you look for Acamoth in Boston, I can point you to mine proposed New England Mystery ( loosly based on Stephen Kings books ) to that Secret Concord is connected - <i>Spirit of the Land</i>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=827351#post827351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Great Mystery of New England \u2013 Spirit of Land</b></span><br /> There are forces in New England lands. Secret whispers between the sights of wind. The sounds of running river are the same as rhythms of Supernal incantations. Lines of power are crossing land, pointing to forgotten symbols. Immaterial beings are hunting those places for centuries \u2013 and yet they work in to something greater, like common mind. Natives American say this land has its own <i>soul</i>. They may not be wrong\u2026<br /> <br /> From the time first European witches and sorcerers come to the New World, they tried to communicate with this intelligence. It is commonly called \u201eSpirit of Land\u201d \u2013 but Awakened are not sure is it spirit, goetia, powerful ghosts \u2013 or even just some presence they feel when they are alone in the woods. All they want to be study it. And to get the power from it.<br /> <br /> Many attempts on this gone badly \u2013 Spirit, if it\u2019s even exists, is fighting with mages to not get locked up by them. Salem Witch trials are said to be result of first famous attempt. Hubristic Awakened tried to play with forces they could not understood \u2013 and innocent people paid the price. Or at least it\u2019s what Guardians of Veil from New England say.<br /> <br /> Secret Concord from Boston is to be the latest successive attempt on that. Whoever \u2013 no, <i>what</i>ever - is third signer of the document is probably the \u201eThe Spirit of Land\u201d. This is why Ebon Noose and White Putnams so much fortune favors them - the land itself helps them to maintain power. Or so rumors in Awakened circles say.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Possible solutions to Mystery:</b></span><ul><li><b><i>Spirit of the Land</i></b> \u2013 Mysterious being most Awakened sought to know in New England <i>is</i> a powerful Shadows spirit of this Lands. It\u2019s Rank 7 being, on par of Wolf gods the werewolf worship or just a bit below ephemeral beings like Sun or Moon. Many wonder how spirit of surrounding can be this powerful and wonder if Atlantean civilizations that left ruins in New England woods have something to do with it. ( See <b>Boston Unveiled</b>, Chapter Four \u201eOff the Map\u201d )</li> </ul><ul><li><b><i>Bound</i></b> <b><i>unbound </i></b>\u2013 Other theory states that this being is Supernal god, thrown into our world when Exarchs took their Thrones. Instead of being bound in some ancient prison, this being freed itself and roam freely the land. It would explained local Seers interest in to phenomena, as one of their most important dogmas it to lock and sentry this kind of beings. It would also clear why some Awakened disappear in the middle of the night when left alone in the woods \u2013 Bound are always hungry for Mana, pouncing on anything that has a greater amount of it in his Pattern. Awakened are then ideal meal.</li> </ul><ul><li><b><i>Prisoner from Abyss </i></b>\u2013 Most disturbing theory is that \u201eSpirit\u201d is powerful Acamoth, abyssal being living in Astral Space. Most seek mages to use their Astral link with Abyss to go over their home they were separated eons ago. But the New England being had somehow evolved and can travel between strata of Astral on its own \u2013 it lies in Anima Mundi most often, leaving imprint on the land and beings in region. Still, it likes to play with Awakened, offering lore and power. For the price.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I would only point that if first variant is true to particular chronicle, then Woods of Empty Houses ( see Boston Unveiled, Chapter Four \u201eOff the Map\u201d ) is his direct subordinate and Wood is part of Spirits Court. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T17:04:22-08:00","id":1035525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1035515#post1035515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... but this not very much. Prince of 100,000 Leaves is not very much prawling the Astral, he is Annanuki, Abysal alternate world, outside of normal time and space. Prince is Time phenomena, as he <i>is</i> alternate timeline where sacrifice someone is greatest feat of love.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no reason that Acamoth wouldn't be in service to a Time Annanuki. Nothing in the write-up suggests that the Prince himself is prowling the Astral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T07:07:32-08:00","id":1035702,"title":"","content":"I agree. Do you have any suggestions for naming and describing the Acamoth? All I have is a stat block right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:30:57-08:00","id":1035812,"title":"","content":"You can have the Acamoth represent a belief held within the Prince of 100,000 Leaves. Treating an atrocity as a holy act is the most obvious example. For instance, Boston's Abyssal counterpart has cannibalism as a religious sacrament. This Acamoth would encourage those with authority to eat the weak, and the weak to accept it as a way of things. Notice that it's not about hunger - Boston's cannibal spirits have it covered, and they resent the Abyssal Intruders. It's about holy duty. As a result, the name is likely to sound like an euphemism - Bringer of Blessings, The Great Kindness, Sanctifier of the Meek. A benefit of such approach is that players will dread what the euphemism means, instead of learning from an obvious name.<br /> <br /> Any target of Acamoth's Influence would suffer cognitive dissonance between what they always believed to be right and what they're led to believe. Imagine a social worker getting intrusive thoughts that maybe the best charity they could give to a struggling family is to eat one of them, and that very family starting to yearn for that blessing - to their own distress. That assumes they're decent people. People in more pathological circumstances would slide down that slope much faster - likely using the same excuses they used for their ordinary misdeeds (sense of privilege and shifting the blame).<br /> <br /> If you want to expand your options, you can search existing religions for unique beliefs and then corrupt them. For instance, a twisted belief in reincarnation can give raise to a caste of torturers. If causing pain nets you negative karma, but suffering nets you positive karma, it's reasonable to create Hell on Earth to have humanity reach Nirvana faster. It demands some to accept the stains on their Souls to bring anguish to others, for the good of all. Of course, for their sacrifice they deserve special privileges in life. On the other hand, a twisted belief in an afterlife can lead to creation to human farms, where children are conceived and promptly aborted to fill the Heavens with innocent Souls, for the glory of God.<br /> <br /> Acamoth would promote such beliefs in the Fallen World. Worryingly, the can be savvy enough to be subtle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T10:53:42-08:00","id":1036711,"title":"","content":"I like everything you wrote for a certain kind of game, but I think I'm looking for something less subtle. The people being possessed and influenced by the Acamoth are habitual drug users. Do you have any ideas given that? Any thing to describe the Acamoth better in appearance and name. I'm having a really hard time being creative here for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:45:14-08:00","id":1037165,"title":"","content":"If you're going for something more visceral, you could focus on the new behavior of the addicts. I don't know if you decided what it's going to be. If not, you could consider using the Hunger affliction. It was first described in the Antagonists supplement, and mentioned in Boston Unveiled. It's a condition that causes human cannibals to degenerate into monsters. I think some Red Word cultists keep their afflicted grandfather as a pet. It has the benefit of transforming multiple subjects, as opposed to just the Claimed one.<br /> <br /> As for the Acamoth, you can keep the motif of corrupt sanctity. Start as if you're making a Spirit of Faith: a priest in rich robes, a beam of holy light and music, an Angel, a praying supplicant. Then, add a splash of something horrible: the priest has multiple hungry holes in place of a face, the light is accompanied by screams of agony, the Angel is designed by H. R. Giger, the ecstatic supplicant has their skin chewed off. An Actual Play called &quot;Skyscaper Graveyard&quot; used lyrics from Pink Floyd's Sheep as an Abyssal prayer, so you can borrow that. Choose an innocuous name and make sure to describe it all as sacred, because it is. Within the Prince, at least.<br /> <br /> Do you only need a description of the Acamoth, or do you want ideas on its behavior as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:45:24-08:00","id":1037555,"title":"","content":"I love what you've given me so far, so by all means continue ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:10:18-08:00","id":1037965,"title":"","content":"The Acamoth's plans depend heavily on two external factors, namely the Red Word Cult and Dr. Amanda Keller.<br /> <br /> If you want to keep things simple, the Cult doesn't factor into the story at all. It doesn't exist, or the Acamoth works alone, either through ignorance or on purpose. Alternatively, you can allow for minor interaction between the two sides. Leave phone records, bus tickets or addressed packages for your players to find - just enough to point towards Howard's Rock. A step further is to create a close cooperation, but at this point things are getting intricate. The last option is to, if the PCs fail at their mission, have remnants of the addict group be creators of the Red Word Cult.<br /> <br /> Dr. Amanda Keller, ruthless as she is, is as likely to abhor the Abyss as any other sane Mage. If you want to keep things simple make her ignorant of Deep Purple's effects. The Acamoth is subtle, or the affected addicts were dropped from the project, and she didn't care to check. Alternately, she knows and is doing damage control. Her reputation is at stake, so the test subjects are being killed off, whether they're compromised or not. A final option is that not only doesn't she know - she is being manipulated. See below.<br /> <br /> The Acamoth might come up with one or more of the following plans:<br /> 1. It tries to redeem its wards by replacing drug addiction with hunger for flesh. By its reckoning, being transformed by the Hunger is an obvious improvement of their lot. That makes it a pretty straightforward antagonist. It doesn't need to be subtle - it uses their desperation, persuasion and coercion to get them to eat human flesh, until someone becomes afflicted.<br /> 2. It sees potential in at least some of its prot\u00e9g\u00e9s, and attempts to turn them into proper worshipers. Methods vary, but include: cult tactics, editing the Oneiros, punishment and reward, being a confidante, Investments (fittingly, &quot;Break an Addiction&quot; is one of them) and strategically used Numina (like Rapture).<br /> 3. It knows about Deep Purple and wants it to find wider use. The first tactic is to recreate the recipe for its own use. The other is to give Dr. Keller the most successful drug trial she has ever seen. If it's particularly ambitious, it might gradually push her research onto a darker path. If other Seers accuse her of Scelesti practices (deservedly or not), it will offer a helping hand, and the Cult will find it's first Awakened member.<br /> <br /> Involving the Abyss in the game is a balancing act. You want to make it alien and horrifying, but at the same time to give your players some point of reference. Normally these points are contradictory, but the Prince of 100,000 Leaves is unusually hospitable for an Abyssal Realm. You could even live there (not that you'd want to). That makes its Acamoth relatively understandable, which means you can imbue them with personality. <br /> 1. A judgmental Acamoth will raise righteous fury against those who oppose it. It speaks like a hell-fire preacher, accompanied by holy light and sound of horns. Angry and not interested in negotiation, it will accept only other worshipers and sacrifices.<br /> 2. A compassionate Acamoth is a genuinely kind person... thing. It will empathize with you and try to solve your problems. Some of its advice is actually very good. Other will involve cannibalism, and it will call invoke happiness, dignity and living for a purpose as arguments for it. If one of its Cultists is killed, it will plead for your players to eat their body - for dignity's sake. When refused it will break down crying, unable to understand.<br /> 3. An intellectual Acamoth is aching to understand the real world. Somewhat distracted, it has strange speech patterns, such as repetition, meandering sentences, not using statements or referring to concepts as if to people. It actually admires Jesus Christ, as the Holy Lamb for the Slaughter, but asks for clarification on multiple points. For instance, why do people use bread as substitute?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T02:20:09-08:00","id":1038811,"title":"","content":"If you have a moment, I was hoping for some final feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:35:45-08:00","id":1040785,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I've been behind on my forum reading and only got to this thread again right now.<br /> <br /> This stuff is brilliant. I'll likely use all of it. I used the Red Word quite a bit in my last Chronicle and was planning to weave Reign of the Exarchs into this one instead with the Acamoth/Deep Purple thing just being more of an introductory story.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all of your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:40:16-08:00","id":1040863,"title":"","content":"Happy to help. Do you still write an Actual Play as you did years ago?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:33:31-08:00","id":1041562,"title":"","content":"I'd love to, but have decided to simply spend more time playing games instead of talking and writing about them. I might change my mind and write something up, but for now I'm sticking to just running games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:27:59-08:00","id":1041581,"title":"","content":"Oh, what about a ban and a bane for the Acamoth? I went with the empathetic Sanctifier of the Meek motif.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T18:31:09-08:00","id":1041616,"title":"","content":"By the way, while you're thinking about that, I'd like you (or anyone else here) to critique the Mystery:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Mystery of Deep Purple</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Opacity</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 3</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Surface Information</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> [through Revelation w/o Scrutiny]:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Death - Soul of user has been altered in some way by the drug</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life - User exhibits extreme steroid use symptoms and suffers from an unnatural hunger</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter - Altered chemical substance similar to heroin, mixed with blood through Patterning</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind - User\u2019s Oneiros has been altered, Acamoth Tethered to user in Mind Twilight</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime - Drug carries traces of Awakened magic, undecipherable Signature Nimbus</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time - Drug vial is 3 months old, user has been under the effects for 3 weeks</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Deep Information</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[through lowering Opacity w/Scrutiny]:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fate - Users share their fates with one another (converging lines)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Matter - The blood part of the substance carries an Abyssal taint, the magic drug is Lasting</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind - User\u2019s Daimon is extremely weak or non-existent, Acamoth is causing the hunger</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime - Resonance of Compliance can be found as well as a trace Abyssal taint, </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Signature Nimbus causes drug to appear more translucent as if being X-rayed</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Space - Users share a strong sympathetic connection, even if unrelat</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ed</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Final Solution</b> [at Opacity 0]<br /> <br /> Users share a realm in the Temenos: Purging the drug from the user\u2019s system, severing their link to the hive in the Temenos with Space, and repairing their Oneiros with Mind can save a victim and begin the recovery process.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 01-31-2017, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T11:15:06-08:00","id":1041933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1041581#post1041581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, what about a ban and a bane for the Acamoth? I went with the empathetic Sanctifier of the Meek motif.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the moment you know more about the Acamoth than I do. Still, I'll make a shot in the dark and try anyway. Since the Acamoth represents a belief, its weakness can lie either in needing to uphold that belief, or in subversion of that belief. If you give the Acamoth additional symbolism, you can design its weaknesses after that, but I'm working off what I know.<br /> <br /> Let's start with the obvious:<br /> Ban: It can only affect users of Deep Purple. It might discover other means of access in the future.<br /> Ban: It can only affect perpetrators and victims of cannibalism. A shared Temenos realm circumvents this Ban.<br /> <br /> Dogma:<br /> Ban: Whenever a killer refuses to consume their victim the Sanctifier will intervene. It's always aware when this happens around its cultists. If the killer successfully pleads their case (succeeds at an appropriate Social or Mental roll), the Sanctifier may become traumatized.<br /> Ban: Both disrespecting and easing the suffering of the sacrifices are unacceptable. Sanctifier will intervene to correct that misconduct. If the perpetrator successfully pleads their case (succeeds at an appropriate Social or Mental roll), the Sanctifier may become traumatized.<br /> Ban: When approached respectfully, Sanctifier will happily share advice on any topic. After all, fulfilling lives make for both better sacrifices and priests. However, it won't knowingly go against its prot\u00e9g\u00e9s interests by doing so. <br /> <br /> Blasphemy:<br /> Bane: Force-feeding one's flesh to an unwilling human being reverses the Ruler - Sacrifice relation. The Acamoth suffers from witnessing that act.<br /> Bane: Funerals as we know them are alien to the Sanctifier. Cremated or embalmed remains, or bodies allowed to decay act as its Bane.<br /> Bane: Whenever a cultist earnestly accepts mercy and help after being defeated, they become Sanctifier's Bane. There needs to be notable effort or sacrifice on part of the mercy-giver.<br /> Bane: People in an unequal relationship praying together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T02:02:46-08:00","id":1054685,"title":"","content":"Two things coming from my latest games session:<br /> 1. Guardian player is interested in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1053120#post1053120\">(Legion) </a>heresy Legacy. Shadow Chorus members are looking as good material for heretics - still, I don't think all members of cabal would be. For example Culsu seems to be fixed on her one Shadow Name persona only. Who's from Chorus would be from (Legion)?<br /> 2. Promethean player want to equal non-mages in the eyes of local Lex Magica. So I need to know about local non-mages supernaturals societies. Are there described in books? If not, have you got fan idea on Boston societies of vampires, werewolves or changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-25-2017, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T04:05:33-08:00","id":1054704,"title":"","content":"1) The whole point of (Legion) is that you wouldn't know who's in it. I think you'd get more bang for your buck if they were a mystery mentor whose identity you can't pin down. Heck, (Legion) is thought of as a disease, it's entirely possible they meet only one time and the student accepts it and becomes infected. From there all meaningful interaction might happen Sympathetically and/or anonymously to decrease the likelihood of discovery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T05:25:51-08:00","id":1054722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1054685#post1054685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guardian player is interested in (Legion) heresy Legacy. Shadow Chorus members are looking as good material for heretics - still, I don't think all members of cabal would be. For example Culsu seems to be fixed on her one Shadow Name persona only. Who's from Chorus would be from (Legion)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have the book on me, but &quot;Left-Hand Path&quot; starts with a story of a Shadow Chorus member being (Legion). Also Mrmdubois is in the right. (Legion) is a condition where your identity is slowly obliterated. Only self-destructive characters would want that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T05:58:11-08:00","id":1054725,"title":"","content":"For the record you'd also want to put some serious work into (Legion) when retooling it for 2e, in 1e its attainments were basically unworkable giving up way too much (Essentially all your magic when using the attainments) while giving not enough (A disguise ability done better by Prince of Masks) for too high a price (Soul stealing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:12:53-08:00","id":1054824,"title":"","content":"There is very nice <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1053120#post1053120\">(Legion) Legacy 2E update</a> made by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a>. And maybe Legacy is sub-optimal from OOC view, but characters in the game join most Left-Hand Legacies because, well... they were being tricked in to them. And my player is interested in exploring (Legion), as her Guardian PC is <i>already</i> over dogmatic for most Guardians.<br /> <br /> Read <b>Left-Hand Path</b> books intro and there is mentioned <i>Kenosia</i> as (Legion) member. She is not described in <b>Boston Unveiled</b>. Is there some source where she is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:31:25-08:00","id":1054839,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> Did a good job overcoming the original problems the legacy had in 1e. The rest of what I said about how I'd make the mentor as anonymous as possible still applies. (Legion) is about subsuming the self so I can't really imagine members actually wanting to know each other more than absolutely necessary. Basically, I figure a member of (Legion) would show up and say, &quot;I'm here to offer you an opportunity, do you want in?&quot; and they wouldn't say, &quot;Hey, my name is Kenosia and I'm a member of (Legion), do you want in?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T11:34:41-07:00","id":1094898,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to convert Beast of Burden to 2e.<br /> <br /> Do you think the Shinje should still be Rank 4 in 2e?<br /> <br /> Any tips for converting this mystery into a &quot;Mystery&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T13:44:51-07:00","id":1100948,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I pretty much decided to keep The Shinje as written.<br /> <br /> Here is the mystery breakdown I came up with if anyone is interested or wants to critique it:</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mystery - Beast of Burden</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Shinje - Threefold Resurrection Spirit</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Opacity</b>: 3</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Surface Information</b> [through Revelation w/o Scrutiny]:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Death - Phurba has Death resonance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Life - Wu is weak</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Matter - Cage has been strengthened with a Matter spell</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mind - Wu is distraught</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prime - Traces of Awakened magic on the shattered cage</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Spirit - Gauntlet has been strengthened inside the zone of the cage, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Phurba has a Spirit resonance </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Time - The cage was shattered two hours ago</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Deep Information</b> [through lowering Opacity w/Scrutiny or other investigation]:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Death - Wu lacks a soul (must contend with Transform Aura first), </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Shinje possesses two souls</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fate - Phurba has a strong connection to Khatvanga/Shinje</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Life - The Shinje is capable of shifting forms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mind - Breach the Vault of Memory spell exists on Wu (Clash vs. 12 dice)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prime - Transform Aura spell on Wu so he appears Awakened with a soul (Clash vs. 11 dice), </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Otherwise he registers as Awakened </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Space - Phurba has an Intimate connection to Khatvanga/Shinje</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Time - Whatever is supposed to happen will happen within the next 7 days </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Final Solution</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> [at Opacity 0] - Full extent of Khatvanga\u2019s intentions and how the Shinje works becomes known. Likely only possible with Athaneum research.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 06-06-2017, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T09:30:12-07:00","id":1105423,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1470_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1470\" data-vbnamecard=\"1470\">Johnny Awesome</a> I've been wondering how the Acamoth and its plot thread went over with your players. Did you get any interesting reactions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T12:35:05-07:00","id":1105487,"title":"","content":"That group doesn't play that often but it's been going well. I'll post a plot summary at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T19:12:52-07:00","id":1154933,"title":"","content":"Teatime,<br /> <br /> This group is finally playing again after a 4-month hiatus.<br /> <br /> They've tracked the source of Deep Purple to Harvard and confronted Clint Zellner, Dr. Kether's assistant. He co-located to her lab and one of the PCs managed to jump through the portal before it closed and fought Clint for a brief time before realizing he was in trouble and managed to use Velocity to quickly exit the building and rendezvous with the other PCs.<br /> <br /> My players are 10, 12 and 40 years old, btw, but the kids are super smart. Given their age they definitely have a tendency to prefer action. They told me that they were going to go back into Kether's lab to confront her. She has informed campus security and the Boston PD as well about the assault on her lab, so the PCs will have to hurry.<br /> <br /> In keeping with the flavor of the chronicle, I'm expecting them to fight Clint and Dr. Kether which might lead them to Dr. Imes's lab through another discovered portal. It's protected by super zombies and it's where the Deep Purple is being manufactured using the blood of a comatose mad scelesti.<br /> <br /> My question is: If the comatose Scelesti wakes up (Adept of Space, I've decided) do you have any cool ideas for Abyssal Investments he could have and an idea for his appearance given the &quot;Boss battle&quot; nature of the encounter? I supposed I'm looking for someone/thing monstrous that they need to put down.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:30:51-07:00","id":1155144,"title":"","content":"I think it's best to build upon facts you've already established. Ask yourself why the Seers came to use blood of a Scelestus and if they knew about their captive's nature. Who is the Scelestus? Is he related to the Prince of 100.000 Leaves? Is it Blood of the Lamb? Perhaps Deep Purple's properties are an indirect result of an Investment, and the corruption begun with blood.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hqVbOSEsJNo\" target=\"_blank\">A source of inspiration</a><br /> <br /> Unprocessed blood might have dangerous properties of its own, perhaps even intended by the Investment:<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 Puddles of blood are deeper than possible, so objects and people might fall in.<br /> \u2022 Contact can cause hallucinations that deal psychosomatic damage.<br /> \u2022 A degree of body control. Not too much, though - players hate losing agency.</span></span><br /> If the Scelestus keeps on bleeding beyond what he should be able to, it would be a good reason to outright disintegrate him.<br /> <br /> Beyond the blood moving by its own volition, the Scelestus' Space Arcanum may cause it to:<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>Spill towards walls, forcing your players to dodge.<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>Pool on the floor, walls or the ceiling.<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 Float as if in absence of gravity.<br /> \u2022 Slowly flow towards the characters, forcing them to play &quot;The Floor is Lava&quot;, while everything goes haywire.<br /> All of which makes it </span></span>difficult to navigate the room.<br /> <br /> As for making the Scelestus look like a Boss Battle, transforming the enemy into a monster is a classic:<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xRoWFw8JAwE&amp;t=2m26s\" target=\"_blank\">Another source of inspiration</a>. Horrendous noise optional. I'd lean away from making him look a more functional monster, but towards showing that he's suffering as well.<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 Have the Scelestus peel his skin open to reveal a different place. A rotting forest, a field of furnaces, a mound of frozen corpses. You can literally connect him to an Annunaki of your choice. Bonus points if that vista is the source of the blood.<br /> \u2022 Something I learned from Earthbound (the Nintendo game). An opponent wasting their turn to do something unnerving shows how little contact with reality they have. Make sure to make up for it somehow, so the players don't win too fast.</span></span><br /> <br /> You can also transform the environment. The Space Arcanum is enough to do that.<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=94goG-pLtaQ\" target=\"_blank\">Yet another source of inspiration.</a></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>You can reverse gravity to make equipment fall on players. Bonus points if the Scelestus gets hurt too - hanging from his catheters. That would underscore that nobody has control over the situation.<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2022 </span></span>Portal players to a storage box sunken in the ocean and filled with bones of other victims. Boston is a port city, after all. Only do this to players you know will survive it. Note that players might want to investigate the remains.<br /> <br /> On top of that, a barely lucid Scelestus will probably cause and release Paradox like nobody's business. This fact makes the battlefield your playground. You have every excuse to throw in creepy effects, dangerous phenomena or go all-out and summon Gulmoth...s. Gulmoi? Summon Abyssal Intruders. The longer the fight goes, the bigger the Paradox pool, so this gives your players a sort of countdown.<br /> <br /> As you players approach the opponent you have a chance to build atmosphere. I'm thinking of blinking panels on the wall, stating &quot;Silent alarm activated. The asset is awake. Initiate Indigo evacuation procedure&quot; - or something in that vein. When things get tough, you can activate the emergency speaker system, and when they escalate further, you can make it give twisted messages, explode, bleed or melt.<br /> <br /> A final thought: If the Seers knew what they were dealing with, the players may decide to tattle to their superiors or competitors. Which seems pretty reasonable, all things considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 11-02-2017, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T12:56:25-07:00","id":1155170,"title":"","content":"This stuff is gold. I'll let you know which way I go with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T13:50:04-07:00","id":1155181,"title":"","content":"Happy to help!<br /> <br /> One more idea: The Seers probably left Spells in place to keep their prisoner contained. You could do the ironic thing and make the same Spells work against your players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T09:35:38-08:00","id":1158194,"title":"","content":"So things went a little differently than I had planned, but not necessarily in a bad way.<br /> <br /> The group immediately decided on defensive measures(all group spells): Honing the Form (+3 Stamina), Ward (+3 on the Clash for 6 dice), Wards &amp; Signs (Potency 4)<br /> <br /> Clint (the Mastigos Seer) attempted 4 times to open a Scrying window on them and failed due to Clashing with the Ward and/or not having enough Potency to overcome Wards &amp; Signs. After spending 4 Mana he gave up, much to Dr. Kether's dismay.<br /> <br /> In the mean time, the group managed to get to her lab and use Telekinesis to open the locked door, only to find the two Seers arguing.<br /> <br /> Dr. Kether was sizing them up and cast Mental Scan, but did not overcome the Wards &amp; Signs again.<br /> <br /> So both groups were in a situation where they were worried about the power level of their potential opponent. A true stand off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The PCs informed her about the Sanctifier of the Meek (Acamoth) to her surprise and she acquiesced that &quot;the Abyss concerns us all&quot;, but that she needed to know who they were &quot;What Ministry do you serve?&quot; to establish some trust.<br /> <br /> The Mastigos leader of the group rolled no successes on a roll to know anything about Seer hierarchy so instead of trying to fake it he told her that the group were Apostates, but he rolled so poorly she just laughed and accused them of being Pentacle mages.<br /> <br /> The Thyrsus Silver Ladder decided that if the jig was up he would just throw the Guardians under the bus, since they aren't very well represented in Boston and worrying about the Abyss was in their wheelhouse. He rolled ok, but she rolled an exceptional success to detect his ruse. She played along just to diffuse the situation.<br /> <br /> She agreed that they would temporarily halt the distribution of Deep Purple at least long enough for the Acamoth to be dealt with.<br /> <br /> Campus security came knocking and the group headed back to their Sanctum after being escorted off campus.<br /> <br /> After a good night sleep they got up, harvested Mana from their Hallow and decided that they would leave the Seers alone for now and deal with the cannibal splinter group, under the control of the Acamoth, that has taken control of the gang distributing Deep Purple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-13-2017, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T10:49:56-08:00","id":1158217,"title":"","content":"Sounds like it was fun! Incidentally did you change or update Dr Kether at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T11:33:59-08:00","id":1158232,"title":"","content":"Not much. I don't remember what she was, but she's Gnosis 4, Matter 4, Life 4, Death 3, Mind 3 now.<br /> <br /> I made her light on Mind Rotes, assuming she would be more into the pharmaceuticals given the direction of the story we're telling.<br /> <br /> If a fight broke out she was going rely on Degrade the Form and Lethal Life spells if needed, but she still had Emotional Urging (Dice Pool 10) as a Rote to calm tensions if needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T14:50:23-08:00","id":1158277,"title":"","content":"Universe, why do you tease me so... But seriously, being able to go off script is a mark of a great GM, and a strong reason why role-playing games are so fun. Speaking of which, did your players meet the Acamoth face-to-face, or is it still coming?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T06:39:02-08:00","id":1158444,"title":"","content":"They did and were suitably freaked out by his obsession with cannibalism and calm demeanor.<br /> <br /> Here's a recap:<br /> <br /> The way the chronicle started was that the gang members (The Postmen) were having a bonfire in the vicinity of the PCs sanctum, which they did not approve of. So the Thyrsus (Thirio) in the group decided to scare them away with a couple nearby deer. The Deep Purple user in the gang, named Jimmy decided to run after the deer instead of scatter like the rest of his friends. The Acamoth that was tethered to him in Twilight boosted Jimmy's attributes who fought and was subdued by the cabal and the Thyrsus' spirit bear familiar (Moksgm 'ol - Mok for short) that were coming to the rescue of the deer.<br /> <br /> The Mastigos (Utelius) in the group noticed the Acamoth and Jimmy was carrying a vial of Deep Purple (DP) on him. That's when their Obsession with Deep Purple began. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They found the mail symbol tatoo on Jimmy's arm and the Obrimos (Nakkuru) called his retainer (Pete Adams), a pizza delivery guy Sleepwalker and fellow Arrow to find out what gang Jimmy was in and to find out where their HQ was. Pete Adams has high Streetwise and managed to get this information within a few hours.<br /> <br /> They incarcerated Jimmy and the Acamoth and had some interesting conversations with this Sanctifier of the Meek.<br /> <br /> The next morning when they went to investigate The Postmen they stumbled upon an interrogation on an unrelated matter. That's when an escaped boosted Jimmy broke through the door and insisted that the interrogated man be sacrificed and consumed. Half the Postmen present agreed and the rest did not. This caused a fight to break out between the cannibals and the non-cannibals in the Postmen and the cabal decided to free the man and get out of there. Pete had found out through his contacts that the ultimate source of DP was at Harvard, so the cabal decided to go there to pick up the trail.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, Jimmy has taken over The Postmen and introduced cannibalism to many of the gang. The Company (see Boston Unveiled) has lost control of The Postmen at this point and won't be happy about it.<br /> <br /> I've decided to have Clint with the help of Life &amp; Mind magic infiltrate The Postmen to find out what's going on and get the distribution of DP back on track.<br /> <br /> The cabal is intending to shut down The Postmen completely, which will put them into conflict with The Company, which will set up events in Reign of the Exarchs nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-14-2017, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T08:10:23-08:00","id":1158476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1158444#post1158444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did and were suitably freaked out by his obsession with cannibalism and calm demeanor.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Leans back, satisfied*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1158444#post1158444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They incarcerated Jimmy and the Acamoth and had some interesting conversations with this Sanctifier of the Meek.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Leans forward* Actually, I'd love to hear more on how that went, if you have time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T11:08:49-08:00","id":1158563,"title":"","content":"After they defeated Jimmy, The Sanctifier of the Meek tried to convince them that they needed to consume him according to the proper rites. He offered to &quot;help&quot; them since they were new to the rites.<br /> <br /> Nakkuru (Obrimos) became a little curious about the vial of DP so the Sanctifier used his Influence to increase Nakkuru's hunger for DP, but Thirio (Thyrus) used Life magic to satiate Nakkuru's desire. He wouldn't give up the vial though and still carries it on his person, something which became important later when they confronted Clint in his office and he co-located to Dr. Kether's lab to escape them and the portal was Keyed to carrying DP. Nakkuru was the only one who could follow him through the portal.<br /> <br /> The Sanctifier decided to abandon the cabal and concentrate on converting The Postmen for now, but he may end up trying to get Nakkuru to shoot up the DP, if given the opportunity.<br /> <br /> So there are a lot of balls in the air right now. The Acamoth is trying to promote cannibalism and DP use. The Seers are trying to promote DP use. The Company are trying to regain control of The Postmen and the cabal are trying to sort it all out. The Consilium doesn't really know what's going on yet, but I might have the Adamantine Arrow figure it out given how much Pete Adams is sniffing around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-14-2017, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T19:36:08-08:00","id":1168463,"title":"","content":"For the Boston lovers out there in Mage-land:<br /> <br /> I might recap more of the above Chronicle when I get a chance, but we only played one more session before breaking for Christmas.<br /> <br /> I really like the Boston setting and I'm quite familiar with it, so my 3rd Boston Chronicle has begun picking up steam as well.<br /> <br /> We're four Chapters into Beast of Burden.<br /> <br /> The cabal is composed of a Moros (FC) and an Obrimos (Arrow) and an Acanthus joined for two sessions as well, but left due to personal conflict with the Moros (and pretty much everyone, he was a problem player). In Chapter 5 they'll be joined by a Mastigos (Guardian).<br /> <br /> They managed to track The Shinje to Copp's Hill Burial Ground with the help of Rabid Annie of the Dead Wrens, who just did not get along with the Moros. He DF'ed a seduction and an intimidation roll against her, but she was under orders from Davy Jones to help them anyway.<br /> <br /> The fight was probably the most deadly I've ever run in Mage (after about 70 sessions over 3 Chronicles), but could have been much worse as The Shinje failed 2 our of 4 Withering spells.<br /> <br /> It's Zombie allies kept Annie and the Moros occupied while the Obrimos closed to melee range and began pummeling it with Telekinetic Blows with some help from a Necroamalgam under the Moros' command. The Obrimos was at 5 Aggravated out of 8 Health when the Shinje finally went down to a hail of gunfire from the Moros who then promptly cast Soul Jar to trap the two souls that were released with the Shinje's destruction.<br /> <br /> I've never had a player come that close to death as my Mage games tend to mostly revolve around investigation and politics. Everyone had a blast.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T13:33:13-07:00","id":1507510,"title":"","content":"I've run 7 sessions of my Boston Chronicle in the last 2 months and the players are liking it quite a bit. I have some questions for those knowledgeable enough to help.<br /> <br /> What Legacies do you think the following Mages might have:<br /> <br /> Rabid Annie (Dead Wrens)<br /> Archer (Exalted Knights)<br /> Cathubodva (Exalted Knights)<br /> Agdos (Brotherhood)<br /> Renard (Special Media Group)<br /> <br /> Do you think anyone in the Boston book might be a Crytologos? I have a player that wants to join that one.<br /> <br /> Lastly, are their any Acanthus Legacies with Spirit as a Ruling Arcana? If not, any idea on what a concept might be?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T03:05:18-07:00","id":1507570,"title":"","content":"All listed Mages are only Gnosis 2. They're at the beginning of their journeys and it's reasonable for them to not have joined a Legacy yet. Also, I'm not sure but I don't think they could induct new members either way, at least until they gain higher Attainments.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'm assuming that these Mages would join Legacies that match their approach to Magic and their Arcana spreads. That does not have to be the case. They can join unfitting Legacies through political pressure, social benefits, or carelessness.<br /> <br /> Looking at Rabid Annie's and Archer's Arcana spread, there are no official Legacies that would fit their inclinations. You would need to either assign them new Arcana dots, or let them go through formative experiences that send them on a new trajectory through life. Preferably in-character.<br /> <br /> Cathubodva is easy, because her Arcana fit two official Legacies. Her friendship with Spirits would make her into a great <i>Keeper of the Covenant</i>, and her affinity for Celts would guide her towards <i>Sodality of Tor</i>.<br /> <br /> Agdos doesn't have the necessary Arcana ratings yet, but she seems to be bound towards an alchemical Legacy like <i>Uncrowned Kings</i>, or towards other material-based direction like <i>Forge Masters</i>.<br /> <br /> Renard seems to take the Awakened condition lightly enough that I would make it a point that she didn't join a Legacy at all. <i>Sisterhood of the Blessed </i>might have something she'd like, but they would require her to show some effort, and that's a tough call.<br /> <br /> I don't know who to choose as the <i>Cryptologos</i>, because I can't check all the writeups at the moment. This matter is a bit complicated, because this Legacy was based on Mind in 1st edition, but on Prime in 2nd edition, and only the former has had its Attainments published. If I had to make a pick I'd choose Ahriman, because he's said to know languages unsuited for humanity, he knows a lot of Prime and a little bit of Mind. It would also be a surprise for the players, because his career was mostly focused on Death and forbidden lore. Him having such a respectable Legacy would be a curveball.<br /> <br /> There are no Acanthus-specific Spirit Legacies, but you are aware that Mages of any Path can join any Legacy? <i>Keepers of the Covenant</i>\u200b are based on Fate and Spirit already, and you can just grant that player Spirit as an extra Ruling Arcanum. Outside of that, <i>Scions of God</i> and <i>Gaolers of Ialdabaoth</i> are not aligned with any Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 04-06-2023, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T10:53:26-07:00","id":1507947,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the well thought out response.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering about Ahriman, because my original plan was for him to try to become a Tremere. Can a Cryptologos do that or do I need to either make someone else the Tremere candidate or pick someone else to be a Crytologos tutor for one of my PCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T11:43:52-07:00","id":1507949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=1507947#post1507947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the well thought out response.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering about Ahriman, because my original plan was for him to try to become a Tremere. Can a Cryptologos do that or do I need to either make someone else the Tremere candidate or pick someone else to be a Crytologos tutor for one of my PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends if you mean Tremere as Legacy - or Tremere as Order? In 2E Tremere are changed from stricte Legacy to Nameless Order that is based on original Legacy - with 'Houses' interpreting and integrating their members previous Legacies as alternative attainments for Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T03:00:28-07:00","id":1508012,"title":"","content":"Mages with a Legacy may become Tremere. If their Legacy is not soul-related (like Cryptologos), it becomes erased as if they never joined it. That includes removing the sympathetic links to other Legacy members, which may tip PCs off that something is amiss. If their Legacy is soul-related it may be transformed into a Tremere House, but that doesn't apply in this case.<br /> <br /> With mechanics out of the way, all that's left to determine is which approach your players would like most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}